window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD && window.__LIZZWORD_DEEP_SHARD("0020", [{"word":"intense","ipa_uk":"/ɪnˈtens/","ipa_us":"/ɪnˈtens/","definition_zh":"强烈的；剧烈的；紧张的；热切的；高强度的","definition_en":"existing in a very high degree; very strong in feeling, force or concentration","core_image":"一根橡皮筋被拉到接近极限，纤维绷得发亮，随时会弹回","scene":"夏夜的操场上，一名短跑运动员蹲在起跑器上，全身肌肉绷紧，只等发令枪。教练在他耳边低声说：The pressure is intense.","sceneCN":"这里 intense 是「（压力、紧张感）极强、绷得很紧」（第 1、3、7 个义项：程度极高、注意力高度集中、压力紧绷）；句意：压力非常大。图中可辨识物件：起跑器、发令枪、跑道、运动员。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"强烈的；剧烈的；紧张的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"热切的；专注的；感情强烈的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"intense heat","zh":"酷热；强烈的热"},{"phrase":"intense pressure","zh":"巨大的压力"},{"phrase":"intense competition","zh":"激烈的竞争"},{"phrase":"intense emotion","zh":"强烈的情绪"},{"phrase":"intense concentration","zh":"高度专注"},{"phrase":"under intense scrutiny","zh":"受到严密审视"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级（更多用 more 构成）","form":"more intense"},{"label":"最高级（更多用 most 构成）","form":"most intense"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"intensity","pos":"n.","zh":"强度；强烈；烈度"},{"word":"intensely","pos":"adv.","zh":"强烈地；极度地"},{"word":"intensify","pos":"v.","zh":"加强；加剧；增强"},{"word":"intensive","pos":"adj.","zh":"密集的；加强的；深入细致的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Stretched to a high degree","titleCN":"被拉到很高的程度：强烈的、剧烈的","definition":"of a quality, feeling or condition, present in a very high degree","definitionCN":"（性质、感受或状况）以非常高的程度存在","example":"The desert sun was intense at noon.","exampleCN":"正午时沙漠的太阳极为猛烈。","why":"Latin intensus is the past participle of intendere 'to stretch out'. Anything stretched tight has its qualities raised to a high pitch, so 'stretched' became 'very great in degree'.","whyCN":"拉丁语 intensus 是 intendere“拉长、绷紧”的过去分词。任何被拉紧的东西，其性质都被提到很高的程度，于是“被拉紧的”就变成了“程度极高的”。"},{"no":"02","title":"Feeling at full volume","titleCN":"满音量的情感：感情强烈的","definition":"of emotion, felt with great force and with little room for anything else","definitionCN":"（情感）以极大的力量被感受到，几乎容不下别的东西","example":"She felt an intense love for her newborn son.","exampleCN":"她对刚出生的儿子怀有强烈的爱。","why":"Emotion is pictured as a string that can be tight or slack. When it is stretched to its limit, joy or grief fills the whole field of attention.","whyCN":"情感被想象成一根可紧可松的弦。当它被拉到极限时，喜悦或悲伤就占满了整个注意力场。"},{"no":"03","title":"Eyes locked on one point","titleCN":"目光锁在一点：专注的、热切的","definition":"of a person or their attention, very concentrated and earnest, often to the exclusion of other things","definitionCN":"（人或其注意力）高度集中而认真，常常排除其他事物","example":"He was so intense about his work that he forgot to eat.","exampleCN":"他工作专注到忘了吃饭。","why":"The same Latin verb intendere also meant 'to turn one's attention toward'. Attention is a beam stretched toward an object; an intense person keeps that beam taut.","whyCN":"同一个拉丁动词 intendere 还表示“把注意力转向”。注意力是一束射向对象的光；一个 intense 的人会把这束光一直绷紧。"},{"no":"04","title":"Heat and light that press on you","titleCN":"逼人的热与光：酷烈的","definition":"of physical forces such as heat, light or radiation, very strong and concentrated","definitionCN":"（热、光、辐射等物理力量）非常强而集中","example":"The intense light made everyone cover their eyes.","exampleCN":"强光让所有人都遮住了眼睛。","why":"Physical intensity is energy packed into a small area. The image of stretching becomes packing: the same force over less space presses harder.","whyCN":"物理上的强度，是能量被压进很小的面积。拉紧的意象转成挤压：同样的力量分布在更小的空间里，压迫感就更强。"},{"no":"05","title":"Colour at full saturation","titleCN":"饱和度拉满的颜色：浓烈的","definition":"of colour, flavour or smell, vivid and concentrated rather than pale or mild","definitionCN":"（颜色、味道或气味）鲜明浓烈，而非淡薄温和","example":"The painting uses intense blues and reds.","exampleCN":"这幅画使用了浓烈的蓝色和红色。","why":"A saturated colour has more pigment per drop of medium. Like a taut string, it has no slack: nothing dilutes it.","whyCN":"饱和的颜色在每一滴介质里有更多颜料。像一根绷紧的弦，它没有松弛的余量：没有任何东西稀释它。"},{"no":"06","title":"Competition with no slack","titleCN":"没有余量的竞争：激烈的","definition":"of competition, pressure or activity, carried on with great force and little margin","definitionCN":"（竞争、压力或活动）以极大的力量进行，几乎没有余量","example":"Competition for the scholarship is intense.","exampleCN":"奖学金的竞争非常激烈。","why":"When many people pull on the same rope, every pull is felt. Intense competition is a field where no participant can relax without losing ground.","whyCN":"很多人拉同一根绳时，每一次用力都会被感觉到。激烈的竞争就是一个谁都不能松劲、否则立刻落后的场。"},{"no":"07","title":"Pain or pressure at its peak","titleCN":"痛与压的峰值：剧烈的","definition":"of pain, pressure or a sensation, sharp and severe","definitionCN":"（疼痛、压力或感觉）尖锐而严重","example":"He felt an intense pain in his chest.","exampleCN":"他感到胸口一阵剧痛。","why":"Sensation is described by its degree, not its kind. A sensation stretched past the ordinary range is reported as intense rather than as a new quality.","whyCN":"感觉是按程度而不是按种类描述的。当一种感觉被拉过平常的范围，人们就说它 intense，而不是给它一个新的性质名。"},{"no":"08","title":"The person who feels everything strongly","titleCN":"什么都感受得很强的人：情绪浓烈的","definition":"of a person's character, serious, passionate and inclined to deep engagement, sometimes hard for others to match","definitionCN":"（人的性格）认真、热烈、倾向于深度投入，有时让旁人难以跟上","example":"He is an intense young man with very strong opinions.","exampleCN":"他是个情绪浓烈、观点极强的年轻人。","why":"From the 1630s intense was applied to persons as 'high-strung'. A tightly strung instrument sounds louder, so a tightly strung person feels and expresses more.","whyCN":"从 17 世纪 30 年代起，intense 被用于人，表示“神经绷得很紧”。绷得紧的乐器声音更响，所以绷得紧的人感受和表达都更多。"},{"no":"09","title":"Intensity as a measurable quantity","titleCN":"intensity：可测量的强度","definition":"the noun intensity names the amount of energy, force or feeling carried per unit","definitionCN":"名词 intensity 指单位面积或单位时间内承载的能量、力量或感受的量","example":"The intensity of the earthquake was measured at 6.2.","exampleCN":"这次地震的强度测得为 6.2 级。","why":"Physics turned the metaphor into a number: intensity is how much of a stretched quantity passes through a given area. The taut string became a scale.","whyCN":"物理学把这个比喻变成了数字：强度就是某种被“拉紧”的量有多少穿过给定面积。绷紧的弦变成了刻度。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Intense comes from Latin intensus 'stretched, strained, high-strung', the past participle of intendere 'to stretch out, direct'. The modern sense of 'very great in degree' grew out of the physical image of a string pulled tight.","cn":"intense 来自拉丁语 intensus“被拉紧的、紧绷的、神经紧张的”，是 intendere“拉长、指向”的过去分词。现代义“程度极高”正是从“绳子被拉紧”这一具体意象发展出来的。"},"items":[{"era":"PIE *ten-","en":"The root *ten- 'to stretch' underlies Latin tendere and English tense, tension and tend. A thread, a tendon and attention are all things drawn out in a line.","cn":"原始印欧语词根 *ten-“拉伸”是拉丁语 tendere 以及英语 tense、tension、tend 的共同来源。线、腱、注意力，都是被拉成一条的东西。"},{"era":"LATIN intendere","en":"Intendere meant literally 'to stretch out, extend' and figuratively 'to turn one's attention, strain toward a goal'. The literal and mental senses existed side by side in Latin.","cn":"intendere 字面义是“拉长、伸展”，引申义是“把注意力转向、朝目标使劲”。字面义与心理义在拉丁语中同时存在。"},{"era":"LATIN intensus","en":"Its past participle intensus described anything drawn tight: a stretched bowstring, a strained voice, a high-strung mind. The adjective was formed directly from this participle.","cn":"它的过去分词 intensus 描述任何被拉紧的东西：绷紧的弓弦、紧张的声音、高度紧绷的神经。形容词直接由这个分词形成。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH → ENGLISH, early 15c.","en":"Old French intense (13c.) carried the word into English by the early 15th century, first of situations and qualities meaning 'great, extreme'.","cn":"古法语 intense（13 世纪）把这个词带入英语，15 世纪初最早用于情境和性质，意为“巨大的、极端的”。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, 1630s","en":"The sense 'high-strung, feeling things strongly' is recorded from the 1630s, applied to persons. This is a metaphor from a tightly tuned instrument.","cn":"“神经紧绷、感受强烈”这一用于人的义项记录于 17 世纪 30 年代，这是从“调得很紧的乐器”借来的比喻。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, 17c.–19c.","en":"Intensity (17c.) and intensify turned the adjective into measurable quantity and process, and physics later gave the word a precise technical sense.","cn":"intensity（17 世纪）和 intensify 把形容词变成了可测量的量与过程，物理学后来又赋予它精确的技术含义。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group shares the Latin tend-/tens- 'stretch' family; the near-meaning group contains words that also name a high degree, each from a different angle.","cn":"形近组共享拉丁词干 tend-/tens-“拉伸”；近义组里的词也都表示“程度高”，但角度各不相同。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"intensify","ipa":"/ɪnˈtensɪfaɪ/","tag":"same root, verb","definition":"to make or become stronger or more extreme. It is the verb built on intense plus -ify 'to make'.","definitionCN":"使变强、使加剧。它是 intense 加 -ify“使……”构成的动词。"},{"word":"intensive","ipa":"/ɪnˈtensɪv/","tag":"same root, different suffix","definition":"concentrated on a small area or a short period, as in intensive care or intensive training. It stresses concentration rather than raw degree.","definitionCN":"集中在很小范围或很短时间内的，如重症监护（intensive care）或强化训练。它强调集中，而不是单纯的强度。"},{"word":"intend","ipa":"/ɪnˈtend/","tag":"same root, base verb","definition":"to have in mind as a purpose. It is the Latin verb from which intense was formed, keeping the 'turn attention toward' sense.","definitionCN":"打算、意欲。它是构成 intense 的拉丁动词，保留了“把注意力转向”的意思。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"strong","ipa":"/strɒŋ/","tag":"power","definition":"having great physical power or effect. It is the broad everyday word and can describe both people and tastes.","definitionCN":"有强大体力或效果的。它是最宽泛的日常词，既能形容人也能形容味道。"},{"word":"extreme","ipa":"/ɪkˈstriːm/","tag":"far end","definition":"at the furthest point of a scale, often beyond what is usual or acceptable. It focuses on position at the end, not on felt force.","definitionCN":"处于尺度的最远端，常超出通常或可接受的范围。它强调处在末端的位置，而不是被感受到的力量。"},{"word":"fierce","ipa":"/fɪəs/","tag":"violent energy","definition":"violent, aggressive or very strong, especially of animals, weather or competition. It adds danger and aggression.","definitionCN":"猛烈、凶狠或极强的，尤用于动物、天气或竞争。它带有危险与攻击性。"},{"word":"vivid","ipa":"/ˈvɪvɪd/","tag":"clear and bright","definition":"producing strong, clear images in the mind; of colour, very bright. It stresses clarity of impression rather than force.","definitionCN":"在脑中产生强烈清晰图像的；（颜色）非常鲜艳的。它强调印象的鲜明，而非力量。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: Latin tendere 'stretch', the participle intensus, and the ordinary English family intensity, intensify, intensive.","cn":"只用真实构件：拉丁语 tendere“拉伸”、分词 intensus，以及英语常用词族 intensity、intensify、intensive。"},"normal":[{"en":"In- means 'toward' and tendere means 'stretch'. Intense is the state of being stretched toward something until there is no slack left.","cn":"in- 意为“朝向”，tendere 意为“拉伸”。intense 就是被朝某个方向拉到没有余量的状态。"},{"en":"A tense muscle and an intense feeling are the same picture: fibres pulled tight. Tense is the straight Latin participle; intense is the same idea applied to degree.","cn":"绷紧的肌肉和强烈的情绪是同一幅图：纤维被拉紧。tense 是直接的拉丁分词；intense 是同一观念用在程度上。"},{"en":"Intensity is the noun of amount, intensify is the verb of increase, and intensive is the adjective of concentration. Three suffixes, one taut string.","cn":"intensity 是表示“量”的名词，intensify 是表示“增强”的动词，intensive 是表示“集中”的形容词。三个后缀，同一根绷紧的弦。"},{"en":"Do not confuse intense with intensive: intense heat is very great heat; intensive farming is farming concentrated on a small area.","cn":"不要混淆 intense 与 intensive：intense heat 是极强的热；intensive farming 是集中在小面积上的密集耕作。"},{"en":"The everyday patterns are intense + noun (heat, pressure, competition) and under intense + noun (scrutiny, pressure).","cn":"常见搭配是 intense + 名词（heat、pressure、competition），以及 under intense + 名词（scrutiny、pressure）。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Think of a volume knob at maximum. Nothing is different in kind; everything is simply turned up until the same signal fills the room.","cn":"想象一个音量旋钮拧到最大。种类没有变，只是同一个信号被调到填满整个房间。"},{"en":"Intensity is always relational: a colour, a pain or a competition is intense compared with an ordinary level of the same thing.","cn":"强度总是相对的：一种颜色、一种痛或一场竞争，是相对于同类事物的平常水平而言才显得强烈。"},{"en":"The taut string explains both the compliment and the warning: an intense person can be deeply alive and also unable to relax.","cn":"绷紧的弦同时解释了赞美与警告：一个 intense 的人可以活得非常饱满，也可能无法放松。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The heat in the closed room was intense.","cn":"封闭房间里的热气非常强烈。"},{"en":"She has an intense interest in ancient history.","cn":"她对古代史有极浓厚的兴趣。"},{"en":"The two teams are engaged in intense competition for the contract.","cn":"两支队伍正为这份合同展开激烈竞争。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“因·腾斯”——因（为）腾（空）斯（文），气氛被拉到极限 → intense 强烈的、紧张的","word":"intense"},"root":"源自拉丁语 intensus“被拉紧的”，是 intendere（in-“向” + tendere“拉伸”）的过去分词，核心是“绷紧到极限、没有余量”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of intense, all built on one physical state: a string pulled tight. Heat, emotion, attention, colour, competition, pain and personality are each described by how far they are stretched beyond the ordinary.","cn":"intense 的九个义项都建立在一个物理状态上：一根被拉紧的弦。热、情感、注意力、颜色、竞争、疼痛和性格，都用“被拉到超出平常多远”来描述。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a taut string stretched to its limit, with no slack left.","cn":"核心意象：一根被拉到极限、再没有余量的紧绷之弦。"},"chain":["STRETCH","DRAW TIGHT","HIGH DEGREE","STRONG FEELING","FOCUSED ATTENTION","EXTREME STATE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S4 · S7","en":"FORCE IN DEGREE: heat, light, pain and other physical quantities are raised far above the ordinary level.","cn":"程度上的力量：热、光、疼痛等物理量被提高到远超平常的水平。"},{"senses":"S2 · S8","en":"FORCE IN FEELING: emotion and personality are described as tightly strung, so that everything is felt and expressed at full volume.","cn":"感受上的力量：情感与性格被形容为“弦绷得紧”，因此一切都以满音量被感受和表达。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"FORCE IN ATTENTION: the mind turns toward one object and holds the beam taut, excluding other things.","cn":"注意力上的力量：心智转向一个对象并把光束绷紧，排除其他事物。"},{"senses":"S5 · S6","en":"FORCE IN QUALITY OR CONTEST: colour at full saturation and competition with no margin both leave no room for dilution or relaxation.","cn":"性质或竞争上的力量：饱和度拉满的颜色与没有余量的竞争，都不给稀释或松劲留空间。"},{"senses":"S9","en":"FORCE MADE MEASURABLE: intensity turns the metaphor into a number, the amount of a quantity per unit area or time.","cn":"被量化的力量：intensity 把这个比喻变成数字，即单位面积或单位时间内某量的多少。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Intense is a Latin participle used as an adjective: in- + tens- + -e. English then adds -ity, -ly, -ify and -ive, each with its ordinary force.","cn":"intense 是拉丁分词用作形容词：in- + tens- + -e。英语随后加上 -ity、-ly、-ify、-ive，各自保持通常的构词作用。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin family is the tend-/tens- 'stretch' set: tendere, intendere, intensus, intensio. English tense and tension belong here too.","cn":"拉丁词族是 tend-/tens-“拉伸”这一组：tendere、intendere、intensus、intensio。英语的 tense 和 tension 也属于这里。"},"items":[{"word":"intense","structure":"in- (toward) + tens- (stretched) + -e (adjective)","meaning":"stretched tight; very great in degree","meaningCN":"强烈的；剧烈的（字面“被拉紧的”）","example":"The intense heat dried the lake bed.","exampleCN":"酷热把湖床晒干了。"},{"word":"intensely","structure":"intense + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in a very strong or concentrated way","meaningCN":"强烈地；极度地（-ly 构成副词）","example":"She disliked him intensely.","exampleCN":"她非常讨厌他。"},{"word":"intensity","structure":"intense + -ity (noun of state)","meaning":"the degree of strength of something","meaningCN":"强度；烈度（-ity 构成状态名词）","example":"The intensity of the light hurt my eyes.","exampleCN":"光的强度刺痛了我的眼睛。"},{"word":"intensify","structure":"intense + -ify (to make)","meaning":"to make stronger or more extreme","meaningCN":"加强；加剧（-ify 表“使……”）","example":"The storm intensified overnight.","exampleCN":"暴风雨一夜之间加剧了。"},{"word":"intensive","structure":"intense + -ive (tending to)","meaning":"concentrated, using much effort in a small area or time","meaningCN":"密集的；加强的（-ive 表倾向）","example":"She took an intensive course in English.","exampleCN":"她上了一门英语强化课程。"},{"word":"intensively","structure":"intensive + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"with concentrated effort","meaningCN":"密集地；集中地","example":"The land is farmed intensively.","exampleCN":"这片土地被密集耕作。"},{"word":"intensification","structure":"intensify + -cation (noun of process)","meaning":"the act of making something stronger","meaningCN":"强化；加剧（-cation 构成过程名词）","example":"The intensification of the conflict worried observers.","exampleCN":"冲突的加剧让观察者担忧。"},{"word":"intensifier","structure":"intensify + -er (agent)","meaning":"a word or device that strengthens something","meaningCN":"强调词；增强装置（-er 表施动者）","example":"In grammar, 'very' is an intensifier.","exampleCN":"在语法中，very 是强调词。"},{"word":"tense","structure":"Latin tensus, past participle of tendere","meaning":"tightly stretched; nervous","meaningCN":"紧绷的；紧张的（同根形容词）","example":"His shoulders were tense before the exam.","exampleCN":"考试前他的肩膀紧绷着。"},{"word":"tension","structure":"Latin tensio, from tendere","meaning":"the state of being stretched; nervous strain","meaningCN":"张力；紧张（同根名词）","example":"The rope snapped under the tension.","exampleCN":"绳子在张力下断了。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"tendere","structure":"PIE *ten- 'to stretch'","meaning":"to stretch, extend, direct","meaningCN":"拉伸；伸展；指向"},{"word":"intendere","structure":"in- 'toward' + tendere","meaning":"to stretch out; to turn the mind toward","meaningCN":"拉长；把心思转向"},{"word":"intensus","structure":"past participle of intendere","meaning":"stretched, strained, high-strung","meaningCN":"被拉紧的；紧张的"},{"word":"intensio","structure":"intendere + -tio (noun of action)","meaning":"a stretching, intensity","meaningCN":"拉紧；强度"}]}},{"word":"interact","ipa_uk":"/ˌɪntərˈækt/","ipa_us":"/ˌɪntərˈækt/","definition_zh":"相互作用；互动；交流；发生反应","definition_en":"to act on each other, so that each side affects the other; to communicate or work together; of substances, to react","core_image":"两个咬合的齿轮，一个转起来，另一个被带着朝相反方向转","scene":"科学博物馆里，两个孩子同时转动两个相连的把手，屏幕上两个光点开始互相追逐。讲解员说：The two parts interact.","sceneCN":"这里 interact 是「两个东西互相作用、彼此影响」（第 1、6 个义项：相互影响、物理系统内的相互作用）；句意：这两个部件互相作用。图中可辨识物件：把手、连线、屏幕光点、两个孩子。","pos":[{"tag":"vi.","zh":"相互作用；互相影响；互动交流"},{"tag":"vi.","zh":"（药物、化学物质等）发生相互作用"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"interact with","zh":"与……互动；与……发生作用"},{"phrase":"interact socially","zh":"进行社交互动"},{"phrase":"interact directly","zh":"直接相互作用"},{"phrase":"interact closely","zh":"密切互动"},{"phrase":"interact online","zh":"在线互动"},{"phrase":"interact badly with","zh":"与……产生不良相互作用"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"interacts"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"interacted"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"interacted"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"interacting"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"interaction","pos":"n.","zh":"相互作用；互动；交流"},{"word":"interactive","pos":"adj.","zh":"互动的；交互式的"},{"word":"interactively","pos":"adv.","zh":"互动地；交互地"},{"word":"interactivity","pos":"n.","zh":"互动性；交互性"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Two things acting on each other","titleCN":"两个东西作用于对方：相互作用","definition":"of two or more things, to act on each other so that each produces a change in the other","definitionCN":"（两个或更多事物）互相起作用，使各自都让对方发生变化","example":"Gravity and the Moon's motion interact to produce the tides.","exampleCN":"引力与月球的运动相互作用，产生了潮汐。","why":"Inter- means 'between' and act means 'to do'. Interact is simply 'do between': an action that passes from one side to the other and comes back changed.","whyCN":"inter- 意为“在……之间”，act 意为“做”。interact 就是“在之间做”：一个动作从一边传到另一边，再带着变化回来。"},{"no":"02","title":"Talking and answering","titleCN":"说与答：交流互动","definition":"of people, to communicate with one another by speaking, listening and responding","definitionCN":"（人）通过说、听和回应彼此交流","example":"Children learn language by interacting with adults.","exampleCN":"儿童通过与成人交流学习语言。","why":"Conversation is the clearest case of action passing between two sides: one speaks, the other answers, and each turn changes the next.","whyCN":"对话是“动作在两边之间传递”最清楚的例子：一方说，另一方答，每一轮都改变下一轮。"},{"no":"03","title":"Mixing with other people","titleCN":"与人相处：社交互动","definition":"to mix with and respond to other people in a social setting","definitionCN":"在社交场合与他人相处并作出回应","example":"He interacts well with his classmates.","exampleCN":"他和同学相处得很好。","why":"Social interaction is reciprocal action spread over a group: each person's behaviour adjusts to the behaviour of the others.","whyCN":"社交互动是扩散到群体中的互惠行动：每个人的行为都在根据他人的行为作出调整。"},{"no":"04","title":"Working with a machine","titleCN":"人与机器：交互操作","definition":"of a user, to use and respond to a computer system through commands, a screen or a device","definitionCN":"（用户）通过命令、屏幕或设备使用计算机系统并对它作出回应","example":"Users interact with the app through simple gestures.","exampleCN":"用户通过简单的手势与这个应用交互。","why":"In computing the two sides are a person and a system. The person acts, the system answers, and the answer shapes the next action, so the loop is genuinely two-way.","whyCN":"在计算机领域，两边是人与系统。人做出动作，系统给出回应，而回应又塑造下一个动作，所以这个循环是真正的双向。"},{"no":"05","title":"Substances that change each other","titleCN":"物质彼此改变：发生化学反应","definition":"of chemicals or drugs, to react with each other, often producing a new effect or substance","definitionCN":"（化学品或药物）互相反应，常产生新的效果或物质","example":"This drug can interact with alcohol.","exampleCN":"这种药会与酒精发生相互作用。","why":"When two substances meet, their molecules act on one another and neither leaves unchanged. The word keeps its literal sense of mutual action.","whyCN":"两种物质相遇时，它们的分子互相作用，谁都不会原样离开。这个词保留了“互相作用”的字面义。"},{"no":"06","title":"Particles and forces in a system","titleCN":"系统内的粒子与力：物理相互作用","definition":"of particles, fields or bodies, to affect one another through physical forces","definitionCN":"（粒子、场或物体）通过物理力彼此影响","example":"Charged particles interact through electromagnetic forces.","exampleCN":"带电粒子通过电磁力相互作用。","why":"Physics uses interact for the basic way bodies influence one another at a distance or on contact. The gear image is at its purest here.","whyCN":"物理学用 interact 指物体通过接触或隔空互相影响的基本方式。齿轮的意象在这里最纯粹。"},{"no":"07","title":"Factors that reshape each other's effect","titleCN":"因素彼此改变效果：变量交互","definition":"of factors or variables, to influence one another so that their combined effect is not simply the sum of their separate effects","definitionCN":"（因素或变量）互相影响，使其组合效果不只是各自效果之和","example":"Diet and exercise interact to shape long-term health.","exampleCN":"饮食与运动相互作用，共同塑造长期健康。","why":"Statistics borrowed the word for variables whose effects overlap. When two causes act between each other, the result belongs to the pair rather than to either alone.","whyCN":"统计学借用这个词，指效果相互重叠的变量。当两个原因彼此作用时，结果属于这一对，而不属于其中任何一个。"},{"no":"08","title":"Good or bad compatibility","titleCN":"相容还是相冲：搭配得好或坏","definition":"to combine with something in a helpful or harmful way","definitionCN":"与某物以有益或有害的方式结合","example":"The new coating interacts badly with salt water.","exampleCN":"这种新涂层与盐水发生不良相互作用。","why":"Once two things act on each other, the outcome can be judged. 'Interacts badly' is a verdict on how the mutual action turned out.","whyCN":"两样东西一旦互相作用，结果就可以被评价。“interacts badly”就是对这种互相作用结果下的判断。"},{"no":"09","title":"Interaction as a thing","titleCN":"interaction：互动本身","definition":"the noun interaction names the mutual action or exchange itself, seen as a single event","definitionCN":"名词 interaction 指互相作用或交流本身，把它看作一个整体事件","example":"The interaction between the two chemicals produced heat.","exampleCN":"两种化学物质的相互作用产生了热。","why":"English commonly turns a verb of action into an -ion noun. Interaction freezes the moving exchange into a countable object that can be studied.","whyCN":"英语常把动作动词变成 -ion 名词。interaction 把流动的交流冻结成一个可研究、可计数的对象。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Interact is an English compound of Latin pieces: inter- 'between, among' plus act, from Latin actus/agere 'to do, drive'. It is not an inherited Latin verb; English built it, and its first recorded date is given differently by different dictionaries.","cn":"interact 是英语用拉丁构件拼成的复合词：inter-“在……之间、在……之中”加 act，后者来自拉丁语 actus/agere“做、驱动”。它不是拉丁语直接传下来的动词，而是英语自己造的；不同词典标注的首次记录年代并不一致。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN inter","en":"Inter meant 'between, among, during'. It is the same preposition that appears in interval, intervene, internal and interpret, though each of those took a different second element.","cn":"inter 意为“在……之间、在……之中、在……期间”。interval、intervene、internal、interpret 里都是这个介词，只是各自的第二成分不同。"},{"era":"LATIN agere / actus","en":"Agere meant 'to drive, do, perform'; its past participle actus gave the noun 'a doing, an act'. English act comes from this family.","cn":"agere 意为“驱动、做、执行”；其过去分词 actus 给出名词“行为、行动”。英语 act 就来自这个词族。"},{"era":"ENGLISH COMPOUND, 18c.","en":"English joined inter- and act to make a verb meaning 'act reciprocally'. Dictionaries differ on the first date (often given as the 1730s, sometimes 1805), but the construction is transparent and undisputed.","cn":"英语把 inter- 与 act 组合成动词，意为“互惠地行动”。各词典对首见年代的说法不一（常见作 1730 年代，也有作 1805 年），但构词方式透明且没有争议。"},{"era":"19c. EXPANSION","en":"Through the 19th century the word spread from general reciprocal action to people, social life and chemical substances, wherever two sides change each other.","cn":"在整个 19 世纪，这个词从一般性的互惠作用扩展到人、社交生活和化学物质，凡是两边彼此改变的地方都能用它。"},{"era":"20c. COMPUTING","en":"Computing gave interact its modern high-frequency use: a user and a machine exchanging actions. Human-computer interaction became a named field in the 1970s–80s.","cn":"计算机领域赋予 interact 现代高频用法：用户与机器交换动作。人机交互（human-computer interaction）在 20 世纪 70–80 年代成为一个正式命名的领域。"},{"era":"NOUN interaction","en":"Interaction is the -ion noun of the verb, recorded in English by the 19th century and now used across physics, chemistry, sociology and design.","cn":"interaction 是该动词的 -ion 名词，19 世纪已见于英语，如今通用于物理、化学、社会学和设计领域。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group shares the inter- prefix or the act family; the near-meaning group contains verbs of contact and exchange, each stressing a different part of the loop.","cn":"形近组共享 inter- 前缀或 act 词族；近义组是表示接触与交流的动词，各自强调循环中的不同环节。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"interaction","ipa":"/ˌɪntərˈækʃn/","tag":"same verb, noun","definition":"the mutual action or exchange itself. It is interact plus -ion, naming the event rather than performing it.","definitionCN":"相互作用或交流本身。它是 interact 加 -ion，指事件而不是执行动作。"},{"word":"interactive","ipa":"/ˌɪntərˈæktɪv/","tag":"same verb, adjective","definition":"describing something that allows or requires two-way action, such as software or a display. The suffix -ive marks a tendency or capacity.","definitionCN":"描述允许或要求双向作用的事物，如软件或显示屏。-ive 后缀表示倾向或能力。"},{"word":"interrelate","ipa":"/ˌɪntərɪˈleɪt/","tag":"same prefix, different verb","definition":"to have a mutual relationship or connection. It uses inter- with relate and stresses links rather than actions.","definitionCN":"具有相互的关系或联系。它是 inter- 加 relate，强调联系而不是动作。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"communicate","ipa":"/kəˈmjuːnɪkeɪt/","tag":"exchange messages","definition":"to share or exchange information, ideas or feelings. It focuses on the content carried, not on mutual modification.","definitionCN":"分享或交换信息、想法或感受。它关注被传递的内容，而不是相互改变。"},{"word":"engage","ipa":"/ɪnˈɡeɪdʒ/","tag":"draw in","definition":"to attract and hold someone's attention or participation. It stresses one side drawing the other in, not a symmetrical loop.","definitionCN":"吸引并保持某人的注意或参与。它强调一方把另一方拉进来，而不是对称的循环。"},{"word":"cooperate","ipa":"/kəʊˈɒpəreɪt/","tag":"work together","definition":"to work with someone toward a shared aim. It adds a purpose and a willingness that interact does not require.","definitionCN":"为共同目标与他人合作。它附加了目标和意愿，而 interact 并不要求这些。"},{"word":"mingle","ipa":"/ˈmɪŋɡl/","tag":"mix socially","definition":"to move among and talk with people at a social event. It describes social mixing rather than the mechanics of mutual action.","definitionCN":"在社交活动中穿梭于人群并交谈。它描述社交混合，而不是相互作用的具体机制。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: inter- 'between' and act 'do', plus the ordinary nouns and adjectives interaction, interactive, interactivity.","cn":"只用真实构件：inter-“在……之间”与 act“做”，以及常用名词、形容词 interaction、interactive、interactivity。"},"normal":[{"en":"Inter- = between, act = do. To interact is literally to 'do between': my action goes out, yours comes back, and both are changed.","cn":"inter- = 在……之间，act = 做。interact 字面上就是“在之间做”：我的动作出去，你的动作回来，两边都被改变。"},{"en":"The word is a two-way street. If only one side acts and the other merely receives, it is not interaction but instruction.","cn":"这个词是一条双向街。如果只有一方行动、另一方只是接受，那就不是互动，而是指令。"},{"en":"Interaction is the event, interactive is the ability, interactivity is the degree of that ability. One loop, three noun and adjective shapes.","cn":"interaction 是事件，interactive 是能力，interactivity 是这种能力的程度。一个循环，三种名词和形容词形态。"},{"en":"In chemistry and medicine, interact usually carries a warning: two substances act on each other and the result may be unwanted.","cn":"在化学和医学里，interact 通常带有警告意味：两种物质互相作用，结果可能不受欢迎。"},{"en":"The fixed patterns are interact with someone/something and interact well or badly with something.","cn":"固定搭配是 interact with someone/something（与某人/某物互动）和 interact well/badly with something（与某物相容/相冲）。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Picture two people pushing the same swinging door from opposite sides. Neither move alone explains the door's motion; only the between-action does.","cn":"想象两个人在相反方向推同一扇弹簧门。单看任何一方的动作都解释不了门的运动，只有“之间”的作用能解释。"},{"en":"Interaction is not addition. Two things that interact produce a third state that belongs to the pair, which is why the word is so useful in science.","cn":"互动不是加法。两个互相作用的东西会产生属于这一对的第三种状态，这正是这个词在科学中如此有用的原因。"},{"en":"Every interaction has a boundary condition: too much interference destroys the loop, too little contact leaves two separate things.","cn":"每一次互动都有边界条件：干预太多会破坏循环，接触太少则仍是两个分离的东西。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The two chemicals interact to form a harmless gas.","cn":"这两种化学物质相互作用，生成一种无害气体。"},{"en":"Good teachers interact with every student, not just the loud ones.","cn":"好老师会和每个学生互动，而不只是活跃的那些。"},{"en":"In this game, players interact with the world by moving their hands.","cn":"在这个游戏里，玩家通过手部动作与世界交互。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“因特·阿克特”——因特（网）上阿克（克）特（特）别会聊，一来一往 → interact 互动、相互作用","word":"interact"},"root":"由拉丁语介词 inter“在……之间”加 act（拉丁 agere/actus“做、行动”）构成，核心是“动作在两边之间来回传递”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of interact, all one loop: an action leaves one side, reaches the other, and returns changed. People, users, particles, drugs and variables are all pairs in that same between-action.","cn":"interact 的九个义项都是同一个循环：动作从一边出发，到达另一边，再带着变化回来。人、用户、粒子、药物和变量，都是这个“之间作用”里的成对角色。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: two meshed gears, each turning because the other turns.","cn":"核心意象：两个咬合的齿轮，一个转是因为另一个在转。"},"chain":["SIDE A ACTS","ACTION CROSSES","SIDE B RESPONDS","BOTH CHANGE","NEW COMBINED STATE","ONGOING LOOP"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S6","en":"PHYSICAL MUTUAL ACTION: bodies, particles and forces affect one another directly or through a field.","cn":"物理上的互相作用：物体、粒子与力直接或通过场彼此影响。"},{"senses":"S2 · S3","en":"HUMAN EXCHANGE: speech, listening and social response form a loop between people.","cn":"人的交流：说、听与社交回应在人与人之间形成循环。"},{"senses":"S4","en":"HUMAN–MACHINE LOOP: a user acts, a system answers, and the answer shapes the next action.","cn":"人机循环：用户行动，系统回应，回应又塑造下一个动作。"},{"senses":"S5 · S8","en":"SUBSTANCES IN CONTACT: chemicals and drugs change each other, and the outcome may be good or bad.","cn":"物质接触：化学品与药物彼此改变，结果可能有益也可能有害。"},{"senses":"S7 · S9","en":"INTERACTION AS A UNIT: variables whose effects overlap, and the named event studied as a whole.","cn":"作为单位的互动：效果重叠的变量，以及被整体研究的互动事件。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Interact is a native English compound, not a Latin verb: inter- + act. Its family is built with ordinary English suffixes -ion, -ive, -ly and -ity.","cn":"interact 是英语本土复合词，不是拉丁动词：inter- + act。它的词族用普通英语后缀 -ion、-ive、-ly、-ity 构成。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin pieces are real: inter 'between' and agere/actus 'do, drive'. Related Latin forms include actus, actio and agendas, but interact itself is English.","cn":"拉丁构件是真实的：inter“在……之间”和 agere/actus“做、驱动”。相关拉丁形式有 actus、actio、agenda，但 interact 本身是英语词。"},"items":[{"word":"interact","structure":"inter- (between) + act (do)","meaning":"to act on each other; to communicate","meaningCN":"相互作用；互动（inter- 表“之间”）","example":"The two systems interact smoothly.","exampleCN":"这两个系统互动顺畅。"},{"word":"interaction","structure":"interact + -ion (noun of action)","meaning":"mutual action or communication","meaningCN":"相互作用；互动（-ion 构成动作名词）","example":"Classroom interaction improves learning.","exampleCN":"课堂互动能促进学习。"},{"word":"interactive","structure":"interact + -ive (adjective)","meaning":"allowing or requiring two-way action","meaningCN":"互动的；交互式的（-ive 构成形容词）","example":"The museum has an interactive exhibit.","exampleCN":"博物馆有一个互动展项。"},{"word":"interactively","structure":"interactive + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"in a two-way, responsive manner","meaningCN":"互动地；交互地","example":"Students worked interactively in small groups.","exampleCN":"学生们在小组中互动学习。"},{"word":"interactivity","structure":"interactive + -ity (noun of quality)","meaning":"the quality of responding to user action","meaningCN":"互动性；交互性","example":"The app is praised for its interactivity.","exampleCN":"这个应用因交互性而受到称赞。"},{"word":"interactant","structure":"interact + -ant (one who does)","meaning":"a participant in an interaction","meaningCN":"互动参与者（-ant 表施动者）","example":"Each interactant brings a different expectation.","exampleCN":"每个互动参与者都带着不同的期待。"},{"word":"interactome","structure":"interact + -ome (complete set)","meaning":"the full set of molecular interactions in a cell","meaningCN":"相互作用组；细胞内全部分子互作（-ome 表“全体”）","example":"Researchers mapped the protein interactome.","exampleCN":"研究人员绘制了蛋白质相互作用组。"},{"word":"noninteractive","structure":"non- (not) + interactive","meaning":"not allowing two-way action","meaningCN":"非交互式的（non- 表否定）","example":"The old display was noninteractive.","exampleCN":"旧显示屏是非交互式的。"},{"word":"reinteract","structure":"re- (again) + interact","meaning":"to interact again after a break","meaningCN":"再次互动（re- 表再、又）","example":"The groups reinteracted after lunch.","exampleCN":"午饭后各组再次互动。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"inter","structure":"preposition","meaning":"between, among, during","meaningCN":"在……之间；在……之中"},{"word":"agere","structure":"verb","meaning":"to drive, do, perform","meaningCN":"驱动；做；执行"},{"word":"actus","structure":"past participle of agere","meaning":"a doing, an act","meaningCN":"行为；行动"},{"word":"actio","structure":"agere + -tio","meaning":"a doing, action, pleading","meaningCN":"行动；诉讼"}]}},{"word":"internal","ipa_uk":"/ɪnˈtɜːnl/","ipa_us":"/ɪnˈtɜːrnl/","definition_zh":"内部的；体内的；国内的；内在的","definition_en":"situated on the inside of something; inside the body; belonging to the domestic affairs of a country or the private working of an organization","core_image":"一只核桃被剖开，果仁完整地包在硬壳内部","scene":"医院影像室里，医生指着屏幕上一张身体的横切面图，那是病人体内的器官。他对学生说：This scan shows the internal organs.","sceneCN":"这里 internal 是「位于身体内部的」（第 1 个义项：体内器官）。句意：这张扫描图显示了内部器官。图中可辨识物件：扫描仪、横切面图、器官轮廓、医生与学生。","pos":[{"tag":"adj.","zh":"内部的；体内的"},{"tag":"adj.","zh":"国内的；组织内部的；内在的"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"internal organs","zh":"内脏器官"},{"phrase":"internal affairs","zh":"内政；内部事务"},{"phrase":"internal conflict","zh":"内心冲突；内部冲突"},{"phrase":"internal market","zh":"内部市场"},{"phrase":"internal medicine","zh":"内科"},{"phrase":"internal assessment","zh":"校内评估；内部评估"}],"forms":[{"label":"比较级（更多用 more 构成）","form":"more internal"},{"label":"最高级（更多用 most 构成）","form":"most internal"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"internally","pos":"adv.","zh":"在内部；内在地"},{"word":"internalize","pos":"v.","zh":"内化；使内化"},{"word":"internalization","pos":"n.","zh":"内化；内在化"},{"word":"internality","pos":"n.","zh":"内在性；内部性"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Inside the body","titleCN":"身体里面：体内的","definition":"of an organ or part, located inside the body rather than on its surface","definitionCN":"（器官或部位）位于身体内部而不是体表","example":"The X-ray showed no damage to his internal organs.","exampleCN":"X 光显示他的内脏器官没有受损。","why":"Internus is Latin for 'inward, within'. The body is the most concrete container we have, so 'internal' first names what is inside its walls.","whyCN":"internus 在拉丁语中就是“向内的、里面的”。身体是我们最具体的容器，所以 internal 最先指“在身体这堵墙里面”的东西。"},{"no":"02","title":"Inside an object or structure","titleCN":"物体或结构里面：内部的","definition":"of a part, space or surface, located within the limits of an object or building","definitionCN":"（部位、空间或表面）位于某物体或建筑的界限之内","example":"The internal walls of the house were painted white.","exampleCN":"房子内部的墙被刷成白色。","why":"Any object can be treated as a container with an inside and an outside. Internal marks the side that is enclosed by the boundary.","whyCN":"任何物体都可以被看作有内有外的容器。internal 标记的是被边界围住的那一侧。"},{"no":"03","title":"Inside a country: domestic","titleCN":"国家里面：国内的","definition":"of a country's affairs, concerning matters within its own borders rather than relations with other countries","definitionCN":"（国家事务）涉及本国边界之内的事情，而非与他国的关系","example":"The government refused to discuss internal affairs with the envoy.","exampleCN":"政府拒绝与特使讨论本国内政。","why":"A state is imagined as a bounded container. What happens inside its border is internal; what crosses the border is external or foreign.","whyCN":"国家被想象成一个有边界的容器。发生在边界之内的是 internal（内政）；跨越边界的是 external 或 foreign（对外）。"},{"no":"04","title":"Inside an organization","titleCN":"组织里面：内部的","definition":"of a company, institution or group, existing or happening within it and not open to outsiders","definitionCN":"（公司、机构或团体）存在于其内部或在其内发生，不向外人开放","example":"The company sent an internal memo about the merger.","exampleCN":"公司发了一份关于这次合并的内部备忘录。","why":"Organizations also have walls, rules and membership. An internal memo circulates inside those walls; an external one goes out.","whyCN":"组织也有墙、规则和成员资格。内部备忘录在这些墙内流传；外部备忘录则向外发出。"},{"no":"05","title":"Inside the mind","titleCN":"心灵里面：内在的、内心的","definition":"of feelings, thoughts or conflicts, existing in a person's mind and not visible to others","definitionCN":"（感受、想法或冲突）存在于一个人的内心，外人看不见","example":"She struggled with an internal conflict about leaving her job.","exampleCN":"她为是否辞职而陷入内心冲突。","why":"The mind is treated as an inner room. A conflict fought inside that room is internal, even when nothing shows on the surface.","whyCN":"心灵被当作一个内在的房间。在这个房间里进行的冲突就是内心的，即使表面上看不出任何东西。"},{"no":"06","title":"Built into a system's own logic","titleCN":"系统自身逻辑里的：内在的、固有的","definition":"of a rule, contradiction or evidence, belonging to a system or text itself rather than coming from outside","definitionCN":"（规则、矛盾或证据）属于某个系统或文本本身，而不是来自外部","example":"The theory has an internal contradiction that no experiment can fix.","exampleCN":"这个理论有一个内部矛盾，任何实验都无法修正。","why":"Here internal is about source, not location: the contradiction arises from the system's own rules. It is inside the logic, not inside a physical box.","whyCN":"这里的 internal 说的是来源，而不是位置：矛盾来自系统自身的规则。它在逻辑内部，而不在某个物理盒子里。"},{"no":"07","title":"Internal medicine","titleCN":"内科学：处理体内疾病的医学分支","definition":"the branch of medicine that deals with diseases of the internal organs, especially in adults","definitionCN":"处理内脏器官疾病、尤以成人为对象的医学分支","example":"After medical school she specialized in internal medicine.","exampleCN":"医学院毕业后，她专攻内科。","why":"The specialty is named for its object: diseases inside the body rather than on the skin or in surgery. The adjective has become part of a fixed term.","whyCN":"这个专科因它的对象而得名：处理身体内部的疾病，而不是皮肤表面或外科问题。这个形容词已成为固定术语的一部分。"},{"no":"08","title":"Taken or used inside the body","titleCN":"用于体内的：内服的、体内的","definition":"of medicine or treatment, taken into the body or applied inside it rather than to the skin","definitionCN":"（药物或治疗）进入体内或在体内使用，而不是用于皮肤表面","example":"This preparation is for internal use only.","exampleCN":"此制剂仅供内服。","why":"The same container logic applies to treatment: a drug that goes through the mouth crosses the body's boundary and acts inside.","whyCN":"同样的容器逻辑适用于治疗：经口进入的药物越过了身体的边界，在内部起作用。"},{"no":"09","title":"Assessed from within an institution","titleCN":"机构内部评定的：校内的、内部的","definition":"of an exam or assessment, set and marked by the institution itself rather than by an outside body","definitionCN":"（考试或评估）由机构自己设置和评分，而不是由外部机构进行","example":"Forty percent of the grade comes from internal assessment.","exampleCN":"成绩的百分之四十来自校内评估。","why":"The boundary is institutional rather than physical. Work marked inside the school's own walls is internal, as opposed to an external exam set beyond them.","whyCN":"这里的边界是制度性的而非物理性的。在学校自己的“墙内”评分的作业就是 internal，相对于由墙外机构设置的外部考试。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Internal comes from Medieval Latin internalis, built on Latin internus 'within, inward'. Internus is an old comparative-style form from inter 'between, among', itself from the PIE root *en 'in'. The word is thus a spatial 'inside' word before it is a medical or political one.","cn":"internal 来自中世纪拉丁语 internalis，建立在拉丁语 internus“在内部、向内”之上。internus 是由 inter“在……之间、在……之中”扩展来的古老比较级形式，而 inter 又来自原始印欧语词根 *en“在……里”。因此这个词首先是空间上的“里面”，然后才是医学或政治用语。"},"items":[{"era":"PIE *en","en":"The root *en meant 'in'. It is one of the oldest spatial roots, giving Latin in and inter, Greek en, German in, and English in itself.","cn":"词根 *en 意为“在……里”。它是最古老的空间词根之一，给出拉丁语 in 与 inter、希腊语 en、德语 in，以及英语的 in。"},{"era":"LATIN inter","en":"Inter meant 'between, among'. From the idea of being among things came the idea of being inside a group, and then simply inside.","cn":"inter 意为“在……之间、在……之中”。从“处在事物之中”的观念，发展出“在群体内部”，再进一步就是“在内部”。"},{"era":"LATIN internus","en":"Internus meant 'within, inward, internal', and figuratively 'domestic'. It was an expanded comparative form (*interos/*interus) of inter, marking the inward side rather than the boundary.","cn":"internus 意为“在内部、向内的、内部的”，引申为“国内的”。它是 inter 的扩展比较级形式（*interos/*interus），标记的是内侧而不是边界。"},{"era":"MEDIEVAL LATIN internalis","en":"Medieval Latin added the adjective suffix -alis to make internalis, a learned doublet of the older internus. English took this form rather than the classical one.","cn":"中世纪拉丁语加上形容词后缀 -alis 构成 internalis，它是更古老的 internus 的学术性双式词。英语取用的是这个形式，而不是古典形式。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, early 15c.","en":"English records internal in the early 15th century meaning 'extending toward the interior'. The sense 'situated within' is from the 1590s.","cn":"英语在 15 世纪初记录 internal，意为“向内部延伸的”。“位于内部”的义项来自 16 世纪 90 年代。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, 1795–1884","en":"The political sense 'domestic, pertaining to a country's own affairs' appears in 1795 (internal revenue). Internal-combustion, burning fuel inside the engine, is from 1884.","cn":"政治义“国内的、属于本国事务的”出现于 1795 年（internal revenue，国内税收）。internal-combustion（燃料在发动机内部燃烧）来自 1884 年。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group shares the Latin inter-/intern- family; the near-meaning group contains words for the inside, each with a different boundary in mind.","cn":"形近组共享拉丁 inter-/intern- 词族；近义组都是表示“内部”的词，但各自心中的边界不同。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"intern","ipa":"/ˈɪntɜːn/","tag":"same root, noun/verb","definition":"a trainee working under supervision, originally a resident doctor. The noun comes from French interne 'assistant doctor', from Latin internus 'within'.","definitionCN":"在监督下工作的实习生，最初指住院医师。该名词来自法语 interne“助理医生”，再上溯到拉丁语 internus“在内部”。"},{"word":"internalize","ipa":"/ɪnˈtɜːnəlaɪz/","tag":"same root, verb","definition":"to make a belief or rule part of one's own thinking. The -ize suffix turns 'inside' into 'put inside the mind'.","definitionCN":"使某种信念或规则成为自己思维的一部分。-ize 后缀把“在内部”变成“放进心里”。"},{"word":"internist","ipa":"/ɪnˈtɜːnɪst/","tag":"same root, medical noun","definition":"a doctor specializing in internal medicine. The -ist suffix marks the practitioner of the inside-of-the-body specialty.","definitionCN":"专攻内科的医生。-ist 后缀标记从事“身体内部”这一专科的人。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"inner","ipa":"/ˈɪnə/","tag":"closer to the centre","definition":"situated further inside, closer to the centre than something else. It is comparative in feel and often pairs with outer.","definitionCN":"位于更里面、比别的东西更靠近中心。它带有比较意味，常与 outer 成对使用。"},{"word":"interior","ipa":"/ɪnˈtɪəriə/","tag":"the inside region","definition":"the inside part of a building, country or object, often used as a noun. It names the region rather than describing a part.","definitionCN":"建筑、国家或物体的内部区域，常作名词。它命名区域，而不是描述某个部分。"},{"word":"inward","ipa":"/ˈɪnwəd/","tag":"direction","definition":"directed toward the inside, especially of movement or attention. It answers 'which way?', not 'where?'.","definitionCN":"朝向内部的，尤指运动或注意力方向。它回答“朝哪个方向”，而不是“在哪里”。"},{"word":"domestic","ipa":"/dəˈmestɪk/","tag":"of the household or country","definition":"relating to the home or to a country's own affairs. It overlaps with internal politics but belongs to household and home as well.","definitionCN":"与家庭或本国事务有关的。它在政治义上与 internal 重叠，但也属于“家庭、家宅”这一领域。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: Latin inter 'between' and internus 'within', the suffix -alis, and the English family internally, internalize, internist.","cn":"只用真实构件：拉丁语 inter“在……之间”、internus“在内部”，后缀 -alis，以及英语词族 internally、internalize、internist。"},"normal":[{"en":"Internal is the adjective of 'inside'. If you can draw a boundary and ask 'what is within it?', the answer can be called internal.","cn":"internal 就是“里面”的形容词。只要你能画出一条边界并问“里面有什么”，答案就可以叫 internal。"},{"en":"The opposite is external. Internal affairs stay inside the border; external affairs cross it.","cn":"反义词是 external。internal affairs 留在边界之内；external affairs 跨越边界。"},{"en":"Internalize is the mental version: take an outside rule and move it inside your own thinking.","cn":"internalize 是心理版本：把外面的规则搬进自己的思维里。"},{"en":"Internal medicine is not 'medicine taken internally' as a specialty; it is the branch that treats diseases inside the body.","cn":"internal medicine 作为一个专科，并不是“内服药”的意思；它是治疗身体内部疾病的医学分支。"},{"en":"Keep internal and interval apart: internal has internus 'within'; interval has vallum 'rampart' and means a gap, not an inside.","cn":"把 internal 和 interval 分开：internal 的词根是 internus“在内部”；interval 的词根是 vallum“壁垒”，意思是空隙，不是内部。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Every internal is defined by a boundary someone else drew: skin, walls, borders, membership or the rules of a system.","cn":"每个 internal 都由别人画的边界定义：皮肤、墙壁、国界、成员资格，或一个系统的规则。"},{"en":"The same word moves smoothly from space to society to mind, because all three are imagined as containers with an inside.","cn":"同一个词能从空间滑到社会再滑到心灵，因为这三者都被想象成有内部的容器。"},{"en":"An internal problem cannot be solved by an external fix: if the contradiction is in the rules, adding more data will not remove it.","cn":"内部问题无法用外部修补解决：如果矛盾在规则里，增加再多数据也去不掉它。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The patient suffered internal injuries in the crash.","cn":"病人在撞车中受了内伤。"},{"en":"The country will not allow foreign observers to monitor its internal affairs.","cn":"该国不允许外国观察员监督其内政。"},{"en":"Her internal struggle was invisible to everyone around her.","cn":"她内心的挣扎对周围所有人都是看不见的。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“因·特·诺”——因（为）特（别）诺（定）在里面，不出去 → internal 内部的、体内的","word":"internal"},"root":"源自拉丁语 internus“在内部、向内”，由 inter“在……之间、在……之中”扩展而来，核心是“被边界围住的内侧”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of internal, all ruled by a boundary. Skin, walls, borders, membership, the mind, a system's logic and an institution each draw a line, and internal names whatever lies on the inside of that line.","cn":"internal 的九个义项都由一条边界支配。皮肤、墙壁、国界、成员资格、心灵、系统逻辑和机构各自画出一条线，而 internal 命名线内侧的一切。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a walnut cut open, the kernel entirely enclosed by the shell.","cn":"核心意象：一只被剖开的核桃，果仁完全被外壳包住。"},"chain":["BOUNDARY","INSIDE SIDE","ENCLOSED PART","HIDDEN FROM OUTSIDE","BELONGING TO THE WHOLE","INHERENT"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S2","en":"PHYSICAL INSIDE: organs within the body and parts within a building or object.","cn":"物理上的内部：身体内的器官，以及建筑或物体内的部分。"},{"senses":"S3 · S4","en":"SOCIAL AND POLITICAL INSIDE: affairs within a country's borders or within an organization's membership.","cn":"社会与政治上的内部：国界之内的事务，或组织成员范围之内的事务。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"MENTAL INSIDE: feelings and conflicts kept within the mind's own room.","cn":"心理上的内部：被留在心灵房间里的感受与冲突。"},{"senses":"S6","en":"LOGICAL INSIDE: contradictions and evidence that arise from a system's own rules.","cn":"逻辑上的内部：由系统自身规则产生的矛盾与证据。"},{"senses":"S7 · S8 · S9","en":"INSTITUTIONAL USES: a medical specialty, medicine taken into the body, and assessment carried out within an institution.","cn":"制度性用法：医学专科、进入体内的药物，以及机构内部进行的评估。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Internal is a Latin adjective in -alis: intern- + -al. English builds its family with -ly, -ize, -ization and -ity, and borrows intern and internist from the same root.","cn":"internal 是带 -alis 的拉丁形容词：intern- + -al。英语用 -ly、-ize、-ization、-ity 构成词族，并从同一词根借来 intern 与 internist。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin set is small and spatial: inter 'between', internus 'within', internalis 'of the inside'. The English word internal is the -alis form rather than the classical internus.","cn":"拉丁词族小而偏空间：inter“在……之间”、internus“在内部”、internalis“内部的”。英语 internal 取的是 -alis 形式，而不是古典的 internus。"},"items":[{"word":"internal","structure":"intern- (within) + -al (adjective)","meaning":"of or on the inside","meaningCN":"内部的；体内的（-al 构成形容词）","example":"The internal structure was badly damaged.","exampleCN":"内部结构受损严重。"},{"word":"internally","structure":"internal + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"on or from the inside","meaningCN":"在内部；从内部（-ly 构成副词）","example":"The company is reviewing the plan internally.","exampleCN":"公司正在内部审查该计划。"},{"word":"internalize","structure":"internal + -ize (to make)","meaning":"to make a rule or belief part of oneself","meaningCN":"内化；使成为内在信念（-ize 表“使……”）","example":"Children internalize the values of their family.","exampleCN":"孩子会内化家庭的价值观。"},{"word":"internalization","structure":"internalize + -ation (noun of process)","meaning":"the process of taking something inside","meaningCN":"内化过程（-ation 构成过程名词）","example":"The internalization of norms takes years.","exampleCN":"规范的内化需要多年时间。"},{"word":"internality","structure":"internal + -ity (noun of quality)","meaning":"the quality of being internal","meaningCN":"内在性；内部性","example":"Philosophers debate the internality of mental states.","exampleCN":"哲学家争论心理状态的内在性。"},{"word":"internalism","structure":"internal + -ism (doctrine)","meaning":"a view that justification depends on what is inside the mind","meaningCN":"内在主义（认为辩护依赖心灵内部因素的学说）","example":"Internalism holds that reasons must be accessible to the agent.","exampleCN":"内在主义认为理由必须能为行动者所通达。"},{"word":"intern","structure":"French interne, from Latin internus","meaning":"a trainee working inside an institution","meaningCN":"实习生；住院医师（来自“内部”一词）","example":"She worked as an intern at the hospital.","exampleCN":"她在医院做实习生。"},{"word":"internist","structure":"intern(al) + -ist (practitioner)","meaning":"a doctor of internal medicine","meaningCN":"内科医生（-ist 表从业者）","example":"The internist ordered a full blood test.","exampleCN":"内科医生安排了全套血液检查。"},{"word":"internal-combustion","structure":"internal + combustion (compound)","meaning":"burning fuel inside the engine","meaningCN":"内燃的（燃料在发动机内部燃烧）","example":"The car has an internal-combustion engine.","exampleCN":"这辆车装的是内燃机。"},{"word":"internal affairs","structure":"internal + affairs (fixed phrase)","meaning":"matters inside a country or organization","meaningCN":"内政；内部事务","example":"The embassy does not comment on internal affairs.","exampleCN":"大使馆不评论驻在国内政。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"inter","structure":"preposition","meaning":"between, among","meaningCN":"在……之间；在……之中"},{"word":"internus","structure":"expanded form of inter","meaning":"within, inward, domestic","meaningCN":"在内部；向内的；国内的"},{"word":"internalis","structure":"internus + -alis","meaning":"of the inside, internal","meaningCN":"内部的"},{"word":"in","structure":"PIE *en","meaning":"in, into","meaningCN":"在……里；进入"}]}},{"word":"interpret","ipa_uk":"/ɪnˈtɜːprɪt/","ipa_us":"/ɪnˈtɜːrprɪt/","definition_zh":"解释；口译；理解；演绎；解读","definition_en":"to explain the meaning of something; to translate speech orally; to understand something in a particular way; to perform a role or piece of music","core_image":"一个人站在两方之间，把一边的话拆开，再用另一边能懂的方式重新讲出来","scene":"国际会议的同传间里，译员戴着耳机，一边听发言人，一边对着麦克风把话译成另一种语言。同事轻声说：She interprets for the delegation.","sceneCN":"这里 interpret 是「口译、在两种语言之间转述」（第 2、9 个义项：口头翻译、充当中间人）；句意：她为代表团做口译。图中可辨识物件：同传间、耳机、麦克风、发言屏幕。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"解释；理解；解读；演绎"},{"tag":"vi.","zh":"口译；充当中间人"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"interpret data","zh":"解读数据"},{"phrase":"interpret a text","zh":"解释文本"},{"phrase":"interpret something as","zh":"把某事物理解为"},{"phrase":"interpret for somebody","zh":"为某人做口译"},{"phrase":"interpret the law","zh":"解释法律"},{"phrase":"interpret a role","zh":"演绎一个角色"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"interprets"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"interpreted"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"interpreted"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"interpreting"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"interpretation","pos":"n.","zh":"解释；理解；口译；演绎"},{"word":"interpreter","pos":"n.","zh":"口译员；解释者；解释程序"},{"word":"interpretive","pos":"adj.","zh":"解释性的；诠释的"},{"word":"misinterpret","pos":"v.","zh":"误解；错误解释"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Opening up a meaning","titleCN":"把意思打开：解释","definition":"to explain the meaning of words, a text or a statement so that it becomes clear","definitionCN":"解释词语、文本或陈述的意思，使其变得清楚","example":"The teacher interpreted the difficult poem line by line.","exampleCN":"老师逐行解释了这首难懂的诗。","why":"Latin interpres was a 'go-between' who stood between a text and its reader. To interpret is to carry meaning across that gap and set it out clearly.","whyCN":"拉丁语 interpres 是站在文本与读者之间的“中间人”。interpret 就是把意思运过这道缝隙，并把它清楚地摆出来。"},{"no":"02","title":"Speaking between two languages","titleCN":"在两种语言之间说话：口译","definition":"to translate speech from one language into another as it is spoken","definitionCN":"在说话的同时把一种语言的口语转译成另一种语言","example":"She interpreted for the visiting delegation.","exampleCN":"她为来访代表团做口译。","why":"This is the oldest concrete role of the interpres: a person standing between two parties who do not share a language, passing meaning back and forth.","whyCN":"这是 interpres 最古老的具体角色：站在两个语言不通的方面之间，把意思来回传递。"},{"no":"03","title":"Reading something in a chosen way","titleCN":"按某种方式理解：把……理解为","definition":"to understand or explain an action, event or remark in a particular way","definitionCN":"以某种特定方式理解或解释一个动作、事件或话语","example":"She interpreted his silence as a sign of agreement.","exampleCN":"她把他的沉默理解为同意的表示。","why":"Every act of understanding places a meaning on an event. Interpret stresses that the meaning is supplied by the reader, not printed on the event itself.","whyCN":"每一次理解都是把某种意义放到事件上。interpret 强调意义是由读者提供的，而不是印在事件表面的。"},{"no":"04","title":"Bringing a score or role to life","titleCN":"让乐谱或角色活起来：演绎","definition":"to perform a piece of music or a dramatic role in a way that expresses one's understanding of it","definitionCN":"以表达自己理解的方式演奏乐曲或表演戏剧角色","example":"The pianist interpreted the sonata with unusual tenderness.","exampleCN":"这位钢琴家以非同寻常的温柔演绎了这首奏鸣曲。","why":"A score is not the music itself but a set of instructions. The performer stands between the marks and the sound and decides how they should be understood.","whyCN":"乐谱不是音乐本身，而是一组指令。演奏者站在符号与声音之间，决定它们应当被怎样理解。"},{"no":"05","title":"Reading the law","titleCN":"解读法律：司法解释","definition":"of a court or official, to decide the meaning and application of a law, rule or constitution","definitionCN":"（法院或官员）裁定法律、规则或宪法的含义与适用方式","example":"The court interpreted the clause narrowly.","exampleCN":"法院对该条款作了狭义解释。","why":"Legal texts are written once and applied many times. Judges must stand between the fixed words and a new case and say what the words mean here.","whyCN":"法律文本写一次、用无数次。法官必须站在固定的文字与新案件之间，说明这些文字在这里是什么意思。"},{"no":"06","title":"Reading signs and faces","titleCN":"读懂信号与表情：解读","definition":"to read the meaning of a look, gesture, signal or natural sign","definitionCN":"读懂眼神、手势、信号或自然迹象的含义","example":"He interpreted her frown as disapproval.","exampleCN":"他把她的皱眉解读为不赞成。","why":"A face or a signal carries no dictionary. The observer must supply the meaning, so the verb shifts from 'explain words' to 'read signs'.","whyCN":"一张脸或一个信号没有字典。观察者必须自己提供意义，于是这个动词从“解释词语”转为“读取信号”。"},{"no":"07","title":"Making numbers speak","titleCN":"让数字说话：解读数据","definition":"to explain what a set of results, figures or measurements means in context","definitionCN":"结合背景说明一组结果、数字或测量值意味着什么","example":"Researchers interpreted the drop in sales as a seasonal effect.","exampleCN":"研究人员把销量下降解读为季节性影响。","why":"Data by itself is only marks on a page. Interpretation is the act of placing those marks in a context where they acquire meaning.","whyCN":"数据本身只是纸上的符号。解释就是把这些符号放进一个能产生意义的背景里。"},{"no":"08","title":"Running code line by line","titleCN":"逐行运行代码：解释执行","definition":"of a computer program, to read source code and carry out its instructions directly, rather than compiling it first","definitionCN":"（计算机程序）直接读取源代码并执行其指令，而不是先编译","example":"This language is interpreted rather than compiled.","exampleCN":"这种语言是解释执行而不是编译执行的。","why":"The interpreter program stands between human-readable code and the machine, translating each instruction as it goes. The computing sense keeps the 'go-between' role.","whyCN":"解释器程序站在人类可读的代码与机器之间，边运行边翻译每一条指令。计算机义保留了“中间人”的角色。"},{"no":"09","title":"Standing between two parties","titleCN":"站在两方之间：充当中间人、斡旋","definition":"to act as a go-between who explains each side to the other","definitionCN":"充当中间人，把每一方的意思解释给另一方","example":"He interpreted between the two families during the dispute.","exampleCN":"争执期间，他在两家之间充当中间人。","why":"Before it meant 'explain', interpres meant 'negotiator, agent'. The original picture is a person physically placed between two sides, which is why the same word covers translation and mediation.","whyCN":"在表示“解释”之前，interpres 的意思是“谈判者、代理人”。最初的画面是一个人实实在在地站在两方之间，所以同一个词既覆盖翻译，也覆盖斡旋。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Interpret comes from Latin interpretari 'explain, expound', from interpres (genitive interpretis) 'agent, go-between, translator'. The first element is inter 'between'. The second element is genuinely uncertain: it is often linked to pretium 'price', but etymologists also propose a PIE root *per- 'to traffic in, sell' or 'to lead, pass over'. Treat the pretium story as a plausible tradition, not a proven fact.","cn":"interpret 来自拉丁语 interpretari“解释、阐述”，其名词是 interpres（属格 interpretis）“代理人、中间人、译者”。第一成分是 inter“在……之间”。第二成分确实存疑：常被联系到 pretium“价格”，但词源学家也提出原始印欧语 *per-“买卖”或“引导、越过”的可能。应把 pretium 之说看作一个合理的传统解释，而不是已证事实。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN inter","en":"Inter 'between' is the same first element found in interval, intervene and internal. Here it marks a person standing between two sides.","cn":"inter“在……之间”与 interval、intervene、internal 的第一成分相同。这里它标记的是站在两方之间的一个人。"},{"era":"LATIN interpres","en":"Interpres meant 'agent, negotiator, go-between, translator, expounder'. It covered trade, diplomacy and the explaining of texts, all roles of a middleman.","cn":"interpres 意为“代理人、谈判者、中间人、译者、解释者”。它覆盖贸易、外交和文本解释，全都是中间人的角色。"},{"era":"SECOND ELEMENT, uncertain","en":"The second part of interpres is disputed. One tradition connects it with pretium 'price, value', picturing a person who negotiates a price between buyers and sellers. Watkins instead suggests PIE *per- 'to traffic in, sell'; de Vaan prefers *per- 'to lead, pass over' and compares Greek poros 'passage'. The pretium link is therefore 'generally supposed', not established.","cn":"interpres 的第二部分有争议。一种传统把它与 pretium“价格、价值”联系起来，想象一个在买卖双方之间议价的人。Watkins 则提出原始印欧语 *per-“买卖”；de Vaan 更倾向于 *per-“引导、越过”，并比较希腊语 poros“通道”。因此 pretium 之说只能写作“一般认为”，并未确立。"},{"era":"LATIN interpretari","en":"Interpretari meant 'to explain, expound, understand'. It turned the middleman noun into the act of carrying meaning across a gap.","cn":"interpretari 意为“解释、阐述、理解”。它把“中间人”名词变成了“把意义运过缝隙”的动作。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH → ENGLISH, late 14c.","en":"Old French interpreter 'explain; translate' (13c.) carried the word into English in the late 14th century, first of explaining texts and then of oral translation.","cn":"古法语 interpreter“解释；翻译”（13 世纪）在 14 世纪晚期把这个词带入英语，先用于解释文本，后用于口头翻译。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, modern branches","en":"Performance ('interpret a sonata') and computing ('interpreted language') are later extensions: in both, a middle layer turns fixed symbols into a living result.","cn":"表演义（interpret a sonata）与计算机义（interpreted language）都是后来的延伸：两者都是中间层把固定符号变成活的结果。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group is built on interpret itself; the near-meaning group contains verbs of explanation and transfer, each with a different distance between the source and the audience.","cn":"形近组都建立在 interpret 本身；近义组是解释与转换类动词，各自预设的“源—受众”距离不同。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"interpreter","ipa":"/ɪnˈtɜːprɪtə/","tag":"same verb, person","definition":"a person who translates speech, or a program that runs code directly. The -er suffix marks the one doing the between-work.","definitionCN":"做口译的人，或直接运行代码的程序。-er 后缀标记做“中间工作”的那一方。"},{"word":"interpretation","ipa":"/ˌɪntɜːprɪˈteɪʃn/","tag":"same verb, noun","definition":"the meaning given to something, or the act of explaining it. It is the -ation noun of the verb.","definitionCN":"赋予某事物的意义，或解释它的行为。它是该动词的 -ation 名词。"},{"word":"misinterpret","ipa":"/ˌmɪsɪnˈtɜːprɪt/","tag":"negative prefix","definition":"to understand or explain something wrongly. Mis- 'wrongly' reverses the success of the between-work.","definitionCN":"错误地理解或解释。mis-“错误地”把中间工作的成功反转了。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"explain","ipa":"/ɪkˈspleɪn/","tag":"make clear","definition":"to make something clear by giving details or reasons. It focuses on clarity for a listener, not on the interpreter's position between parties.","definitionCN":"通过给出细节或原因使某事清楚。它关注的是对听者而言的清晰度，而不是解释者所处的中间位置。"},{"word":"translate","ipa":"/trænzˈleɪt/","tag":"move across languages","definition":"to turn written or spoken words into another language. It names the language transfer itself; interpret is the live, oral version.","definitionCN":"把书面或口头的话转换成另一种语言。它命名语言转换本身；interpret 是现场的口头版本。"},{"word":"decipher","ipa":"/dɪˈsaɪfə/","tag":"decode a code","definition":"to read something whose signs are unclear or in code. It implies resistance in the text, which interpret does not always require.","definitionCN":"读懂符号不清楚或经过编码的东西。它暗示文本本身有阻力，而 interpret 并不总是需要这种阻力。"},{"word":"construe","ipa":"/kənˈstruː/","tag":"formal reading","definition":"to understand or interpret words or actions in a particular, often formal or legal, way. It is close to interpret but narrower and more formal.","definitionCN":"以某种方式（常为正式或法律方式）理解或解释言辞与行为。它与 interpret 相近，但更窄、更正式。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: inter- 'between' and interpres 'go-between', plus the ordinary family interpretation, interpreter, interpretive, misinterpret. The second element of interpres is uncertain; do not invent a certain root.","cn":"只用真实构件：inter-“在……之间”与 interpres“中间人”，以及常用词族 interpretation、interpreter、interpretive、misinterpret。interpres 的第二成分存疑，不要编造一个确定的词根。"},"normal":[{"en":"The core picture is a person standing between two sides. Whether the sides are two languages, a text and a reader, or a score and an audience, the job is the same: carry meaning across.","cn":"核心画面是一个人站在两方之间。无论两方是两种语言、文本与读者，还是乐谱与听众，工作都一样：把意义运过去。"},{"en":"Interpret is not 'repeat'. It always adds a decision about what the words mean here, which is why two interpreters can give different readings of the same sentence.","cn":"interpret 不是“重复”。它总会加上一个判断：这些话在这里是什么意思。所以两个解释者可能对同一句话给出不同读法。"},{"en":"The four inter- words are siblings with different second roots: interpret (uncertain, perhaps pretium 'price'), interval (vallum 'rampart'), intervene (venire 'come'), internal (internus 'within').","cn":"四个 inter- 词是同一前缀下的兄弟，但第二词根不同：interpret（存疑，或与 pretium“价格”有关）、interval（vallum“壁垒”）、intervene（venire“来”）、internal（internus“在内部”）。"},{"en":"Interpreter is the person, interpretation is the product, misinterpret is the failure. The -er, -ation and mis- pieces do all the work.","cn":"interpreter 是人，interpretation 是产物，misinterpret 是失败。-er、-ation 和 mis- 这三块构件承担了全部区别。"},{"en":"In law and data, the fixed phrases are interpret the law and interpret the data; in performance, interpret a role or a piece.","cn":"在法律与数据领域，固定搭配是 interpret the law 和 interpret the data；在表演领域是 interpret a role 或 a piece。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Meaning is never simply transferred; it is rebuilt on the other side. An interpreter is a builder of a second version, not a courier of a parcel.","cn":"意义从来不是简单搬运，而是在另一边重建。解释者是第二版本的建造者，而不是包裹的快递员。"},{"en":"The gap between parties is the reason the role exists. The wider the gap, the more interpretation becomes creation rather than transmission.","cn":"两方之间的缝隙正是这个角色存在的原因。缝隙越宽，解释就越接近创造，而不是传递。"},{"en":"Every interpretation is also a choice: to read a silence as consent is to place a meaning that the silence itself does not contain.","cn":"每一种解释同时也是一次选择：把沉默读成同意，就是把一个沉默本身并不包含的意义放了进去。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"It is easy to misinterpret a short message sent without context.","cn":"一条没有上下文而发出的短消息很容易被误解。"},{"en":"The court must interpret the rule in the light of its purpose.","cn":"法院必须结合规则的目的来解释它。"},{"en":"She interprets for the hospital's foreign patients.","cn":"她为医院的外国病人做口译。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“因·特·普瑞特”——因（为）特（地）普瑞特（把）两边的话翻清楚 → interpret 解释、口译","word":"interpret"},"root":"来自拉丁语 interpres“中间人、译者、解释者”，由 inter“在……之间”加一个存疑的第二成分构成（常与 pretium“价格”相联系，但未确立），核心是“站在两方之间把意思运过去”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of interpret, all versions of one job: stand between a source and an audience and carry meaning across. Text, speech, behaviour, music, law, data and code each create that gap in a different material.","cn":"interpret 的九个义项都是同一项工作的不同版本：站在源与受众之间，把意义运过去。文本、口语、行为、音乐、法律、数据和代码，各自在不同的材料里制造出这道缝隙。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a go-between standing in the gap, speaking each side's meaning to the other.","cn":"核心意象：一个中间人站在缝隙里，把每一方的意思说给另一方听。"},"chain":["TWO SIDES","GAP BETWEEN","GO-BETWEEN","CARRY MEANING","REBUILD ON OTHER SIDE","MAKE IT CLEAR"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S9","en":"THE ORIGINAL MIDDLEMAN: explaining a text or standing between two parties and passing meaning both ways.","cn":"最初的中间人：解释文本，或站在两方之间双向传递意义。"},{"senses":"S2 · S8","en":"LANGUAGE TRANSFER: live oral translation between languages, and the interpreter program that translates code as it runs.","cn":"语言转换：语言之间的现场口译，以及边运行边翻译代码的解释程序。"},{"senses":"S3 · S6","en":"READING A SIGN: supplying a meaning to a remark, a face or a gesture that does not carry a dictionary.","cn":"读取信号：给话语、表情或手势补上一个它们本身没有字典的意义。"},{"senses":"S4","en":"PERFORMANCE: standing between a score and an audience and deciding how the marks should sound.","cn":"表演：站在乐谱与听众之间，决定这些符号应当怎样发声。"},{"senses":"S5 · S7","en":"INSTITUTIONAL READING: courts applying fixed words to new cases, and researchers turning figures into meaning.","cn":"制度性解读：法院把固定文字适用于新案件，研究者把数字变成意义。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Interpret is a Latin verb borrowed whole, not an English compound. Its family uses -ation, -er, -ive, and the negative and repetitive prefixes mis- and re-.","cn":"interpret 是整体借入的拉丁动词，不是英语复合词。它的词族使用 -ation、-er、-ive，以及否定前缀 mis- 和重复前缀 re-。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin set is inter 'between', interpres 'go-between', interpretari 'explain'. A pretium link is often suggested but not established, so it is listed with a warning.","cn":"拉丁词族是 inter“在……之间”、interpres“中间人”、interpretari“解释”。pretium 的联系常被提出但未确立，所以列出时带有存疑标注。"},"items":[{"word":"interpret","structure":"Latin interpretari, from interpres","meaning":"to explain, translate or understand meaning","meaningCN":"解释；口译；理解","example":"How do you interpret this sentence?","exampleCN":"你怎么解释这句话？"},{"word":"interpretation","structure":"interpret + -ation (noun of action)","meaning":"an explanation or the meaning assigned","meaningCN":"解释；诠释（-ation 构成动作名词）","example":"Her interpretation of the poem surprised me.","exampleCN":"她对这首诗的诠释让我吃惊。"},{"word":"interpreter","structure":"interpret + -er (agent)","meaning":"one who translates speech, or a code-running program","meaningCN":"口译员；解释程序（-er 表施动者）","example":"The interpreter spoke three languages.","exampleCN":"这名口译员会说三种语言。"},{"word":"interpretive","structure":"interpret + -ive (adjective)","meaning":"relating to interpretation; explaining rather than literal","meaningCN":"解释性的；诠释的（-ive 构成形容词）","example":"The exhibit has an interpretive guide.","exampleCN":"这个展览配有解说指南。"},{"word":"interpretative","structure":"interpret + -ative (variant adjective)","meaning":"the older variant of interpretive, common in music and law","meaningCN":"解释性的（interpretive 的较旧变体，常用于音乐与法律）","example":"The piece calls for an interpretative approach.","exampleCN":"这首曲子需要一种诠释性的处理。"},{"word":"misinterpret","structure":"mis- (wrongly) + interpret","meaning":"to understand or explain wrongly","meaningCN":"误解；错误解释（mis- 表错误）","example":"He misinterpreted her silence.","exampleCN":"他误解了她的沉默。"},{"word":"misinterpretation","structure":"misinterpret + -ation","meaning":"a wrong explanation or reading","meaningCN":"误解；错误诠释","example":"The misunderstanding was caused by a misinterpretation.","exampleCN":"这场误会是由一次错误解读造成的。"},{"word":"reinterpret","structure":"re- (again) + interpret","meaning":"to interpret again, often in a new light","meaningCN":"重新解释；重新诠释（re- 表再、重新）","example":"Later scholars reinterpreted the evidence.","exampleCN":"后来的学者重新解释了这些证据。"},{"word":"reinterpretation","structure":"reinterpret + -ation","meaning":"a fresh reading of something already explained","meaningCN":"重新诠释","example":"The book offers a reinterpretation of the war.","exampleCN":"这本书对那场战争提出了重新诠释。"},{"word":"interpretable","structure":"interpret + -able (can be)","meaning":"capable of being explained or understood","meaningCN":"可解释的；可理解的（-able 表“能……”）","example":"The result is interpretable as a simple average.","exampleCN":"这个结果可以解释为一个简单平均值。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"inter","structure":"preposition","meaning":"between, among","meaningCN":"在……之间；在……之中"},{"word":"interpres","structure":"inter + uncertain second element","meaning":"agent, go-between, translator, expounder","meaningCN":"代理人；中间人；译者；解释者（第二成分存疑）"},{"word":"interpretari","structure":"verb from interpres","meaning":"to explain, expound, understand","meaningCN":"解释；阐述；理解"},{"word":"pretium","structure":"Latin noun","meaning":"price, value (often linked to interpres, but not proven)","meaningCN":"价格；价值（常被联系到 interpres，但未证实）"}]}},{"word":"interval","ipa_uk":"/ˈɪntəvl/","ipa_us":"/ˈɪntərvl/","definition_zh":"间隔；间歇；幕间休息；音程；区间","definition_en":"a period of time between two events; a pause or break; a space between two points; a difference in pitch between two notes","core_image":"两根木桩之间空出的一段距离，中间什么都没有，两头却有明确的界线","scene":"剧院里，幕布落下，观众起身去走廊喝饮料。舞台监督看着表说：The interval is over in five minutes.","sceneCN":"这里 interval 是「幕间休息、两段演出之间的空档」（第 2 个义项：活动中的暂停）；句意：幕间休息还有五分钟结束。图中可辨识物件：幕布、走廊、饮料杯、怀表。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"间隔；间歇；幕间休息；音程；区间"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"（两点之间的）空隙；间距"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"at regular intervals","zh":"每隔固定时间；按固定间隔"},{"phrase":"a short interval","zh":"短暂的间隔"},{"phrase":"the interval between","zh":"……之间的间隔"},{"phrase":"during the interval","zh":"在幕间休息期间"},{"phrase":"confidence interval","zh":"置信区间"},{"phrase":"interval training","zh":"间歇训练"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（多于一个）","form":"intervals"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"intervallic","pos":"adj.","zh":"间隔的；音程的"},{"word":"intervalometer","pos":"n.","zh":"定时拍摄器；间隔计时器"},{"word":"interlude","pos":"n.","zh":"插曲；幕间节目（近义近形词，非同源）"},{"word":"interleave","pos":"v.","zh":"交错插入；交替排列（结构相近，非同源）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Time between two events","titleCN":"两个事件之间的时间：间隔","definition":"a period of time separating two events, actions or points","definitionCN":"把两个事件、动作或时间点隔开的一段时间","example":"There was a long interval before she answered.","exampleCN":"过了很长一段时间她才回答。","why":"Intervallum originally meant the empty space between two ramparts. Time is imagined as a line with posts on it, and the stretch between two posts is the interval.","whyCN":"intervallum 最初指两道壁垒之间的空地。时间被想象成一条插着桩的线，两根桩之间的那一段就是 interval。"},{"no":"02","title":"A planned break","titleCN":"安排好的暂停：幕间休息、中场","definition":"a break between two parts of a performance, sports match or long activity","definitionCN":"演出、体育比赛或长时间活动两部分之间的休息","example":"We bought ice cream during the interval.","exampleCN":"幕间休息时我们去买了冰淇淋。","why":"A performance is divided into two stretches. The empty stretch deliberately left between them is the same 'space between' as in Latin, now built into the schedule.","whyCN":"一场演出被分成两段。两段之间故意留出的空白，仍是拉丁语里那个“之间”，只是现在被写进了日程。"},{"no":"03","title":"Distance in pitch","titleCN":"音高的距离：音程","definition":"in music, the difference in pitch between two notes","definitionCN":"音乐中两个音在音高上的距离","example":"The melody jumps by a wide interval.","exampleCN":"这段旋律以一个很大的音程跳跃。","why":"Two notes are pictured as two points on a scale; the distance between them is an interval. Music borrowed the spatial word because pitch can be drawn as a line.","whyCN":"两个音被想象成音阶上的两个点，它们之间的距离就是音程。音乐借用这个空间词，因为音高可以画成一条线。"},{"no":"04","title":"A set of numbers between two limits","titleCN":"两个界限之间的一串数：区间","definition":"in mathematics, the set of all numbers lying between two given values","definitionCN":"数学中位于两个给定值之间的所有数构成的集合","example":"The solution holds for every value in the interval from 0 to 1.","exampleCN":"该解对 0 到 1 这个区间内的每个值都成立。","why":"Mathematics made the metaphor exact: the two posts become endpoints and the space between them becomes a set of points. The image is unchanged, only formalized.","whyCN":"数学把这个比喻精确化：两根桩变成端点，桩之间的空间变成点的集合。意象没变，只是被形式化了。"},{"no":"05","title":"A gap in space","titleCN":"空间中的空隙：间距","definition":"a space or distance between two objects or places","definitionCN":"两个物体或地点之间的空间或距离","example":"Trees were planted at intervals of ten metres.","exampleCN":"树每隔十米种一棵。","why":"This is the original physical sense: the space between stakes or ramparts. English kept it alongside the newer senses of time and pitch.","whyCN":"这是最原始的具体义：木桩或壁垒之间的空间。英语把它与后来的时间义、音高义一起保留了下来。"},{"no":"06","title":"Repeated with spacing","titleCN":"按间隔重复：每隔……","definition":"in the phrase at intervals, happening repeatedly with a regular or irregular space between occurrences","definitionCN":"在短语 at intervals 中，指事件之间隔着一段时间或距离反复发生","example":"A bell rang at regular intervals throughout the night.","exampleCN":"整夜都有钟声按固定间隔响起。","why":"Once a gap is a measurable unit, it can be repeated. 'At intervals' treats each gap as a slot in a rhythm rather than as a single pause.","whyCN":"一旦空隙成为可测量的单位，它就可以被重复。“at intervals”把每个空隙当作节奏中的一个槽位，而不是一次单独的暂停。"},{"no":"07","title":"Confidence interval","titleCN":"置信区间：统计学的估计范围","definition":"in statistics, a range of values within which a true value is estimated to lie with a given probability","definitionCN":"统计学中，以给定概率估计真值所处的数值范围","example":"The survey reported a 95% confidence interval.","exampleCN":"这项调查报告了 95% 的置信区间。","why":"Statisticians needed a word for the band between a lower and an upper estimate. Interval supplied the ready-made 'space between two limits'.","whyCN":"统计学家需要一个词来表示上下估计值之间的带状范围。interval 正好提供了现成的“两个界限之间的空间”。"},{"no":"08","title":"Lucid interval","titleCN":"清醒间歇：病情之间的清醒期","definition":"in medicine, a period of clear consciousness between episodes of illness or delirium","definitionCN":"医学中，疾病或谵妄发作之间意识清醒的一段时间","example":"The patient had a lucid interval before the fever returned.","exampleCN":"在发热再次出现之前，病人有一段清醒间歇。","why":"Illness is pictured as episodes separated by gaps. A lucid interval is the clear stretch between two clouds, using the same temporal 'space between'.","whyCN":"疾病被想象成被空隙隔开的一次次发作。清醒间歇就是两片乌云之间的晴朗一段，用的仍是时间上的“之间”。"},{"no":"09","title":"Interval training","titleCN":"间歇训练：运动与休息交替","definition":"in exercise, a method that alternates bursts of intense effort with short recovery periods","definitionCN":"运动中把高强度发力与短暂恢复期交替安排的方法","example":"Interval training improved her speed more than steady running did.","exampleCN":"间歇训练比匀速跑更能提高她的速度。","why":"The workout is cut into alternating stretches. Each intense burst and each rest is an interval, so the method is named after its repeated gaps.","whyCN":"训练被切成交替的几段。每次高强度爆发和每次休息都是一个 interval，所以这种方法以它反复出现的间隔命名。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Interval comes from Latin intervallum, literally 'space between ramparts or palisades', from inter 'between' + vallum 'rampart, wall'. Latin already used it for gaps in time, and English took both the physical and temporal senses. The root is vallum, not venire or internus.","cn":"interval 来自拉丁语 intervallum，字面是“壁垒或栅栏之间的空地”，由 inter“在……之间”加 vallum“壁垒、墙”构成。拉丁语已经用它表示时间上的间隔，英语同时继承了具体义与时间义。它的词根是 vallum，不是 venire，也不是 internus。"},"items":[{"era":"PIE *walso-","en":"The reconstructed root *walso- meant 'a post'. It also underlies English wall, and the picture is a line of stakes forming a defensive boundary.","cn":"重建的词根 *walso- 意为“桩”。它也是英语 wall 的来源，画面是一排木桩构成的防御边界。"},{"era":"LATIN vallum / vallus","en":"Vallus was a single stake; vallum was the collective rampart or palisade made of them. A Roman camp was ringed by such stakes.","cn":"vallus 是单根木桩；vallum 是由这些木桩构成的集体壁垒或栅栏。罗马军营周围就围着一圈这样的木桩。"},{"era":"LATIN intervallum","en":"Intervallum first meant 'the space between palisades or ramparts'. From a gap in a fortification it spread to any space between two things, and then to time between events.","cn":"intervallum 最初指“栅栏或壁垒之间的空地”。它从防御工事中的空隙扩展到任何两物之间的空间，再扩展到事件之间的时间。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH intervalle","en":"Old French intervalle (14c.), earlier entreval (13c.), carried the word to English. The French form kept both the spatial and temporal senses.","cn":"古法语 intervalle（14 世纪，较早作 entreval，13 世纪）把这个词带入英语。法语形式同时保留了空间义与时间义。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, early 14c.","en":"English first records interval early in the 14th century as 'time elapsed between two actions'. By c.1400 it also meant 'a pause or interruption in an activity'.","cn":"英语最早在 14 世纪初记录 interval，意为“两个行动之间流逝的时间”。到约 1400 年，它也指“活动中的暂停或中断”。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, 1600 onward","en":"The musical sense 'difference in pitch between two tones' is from c.1600. Mathematics and statistics later formalized the 'set or range between two limits'.","cn":"音乐义“两个音之间的音高差”来自约 1600 年。数学与统计学后来把“两个界限之间的集合或范围”形式化。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group shares inter- or the -val shape but not the same second root; the near-meaning group contains words for gaps, each measured in a different dimension.","cn":"形近组共享 inter- 或 -val 外形，但第二词根不同；近义组都是表示“空隙”的词，各自在不同的维度上测量。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"intervene","ipa":"/ˌɪntəˈviːn/","tag":"same prefix, different root","definition":"to come between events or parties, often to change what happens. Its second element is venire 'come', not vallum 'rampart'.","definitionCN":"来到事件或各方之间，常为改变结果。它的第二成分是 venire“来”，不是 vallum“壁垒”。"},{"word":"interlude","ipa":"/ˈɪntəluːd/","tag":"near meaning, different root","definition":"a short piece or period between two main parts, especially in a performance. It comes from inter- + ludus 'play', not from vallum.","definitionCN":"两部分主体之间的短曲或短时段，尤用于演出。它来自 inter- 加 ludus“游戏、表演”，并非来自 vallum。"},{"word":"intervallic","ipa":"/ˌɪntəˈvælɪk/","tag":"same word, adjective","definition":"relating to an interval, especially a musical one. The -ic suffix turns the noun into an adjective.","definitionCN":"与间隔有关的，尤指音乐音程。-ic 后缀把名词变成形容词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"gap","ipa":"/ɡæp/","tag":"empty space","definition":"an empty space or hole between two things. It is more physical and less scheduled than interval.","definitionCN":"两物之间的空白或缺口。它比 interval 更具体，也不带有日程安排意味。"},{"word":"pause","ipa":"/pɔːz/","tag":"brief stop","definition":"a short stop in speech or action before continuing. It stresses the stopping, not the measured distance between two points.","definitionCN":"说话或行动在继续之前的短暂停止。它强调“停”，而不是两点之间被测量的距离。"},{"word":"break","ipa":"/breɪk/","tag":"rest period","definition":"a period of rest between periods of work or activity. It is the everyday word for the theatre interval and the sports half-time.","definitionCN":"工作或活动之间的休息时段。它是剧院幕间休息和体育中场的日常说法。"},{"word":"span","ipa":"/spæn/","tag":"whole extent","definition":"the full length or duration from one end to the other. It measures the whole stretch, while interval measures the space between.","definitionCN":"从一端到另一端的完整长度或持续时间。它测量整段，而 interval 测量中间的空隙。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: inter- 'between' and vallum 'rampart', plus the ordinary plural intervals and the adjective intervallic. Do not confuse vallum with venire or internus.","cn":"只用真实构件：inter-“在……之间”与 vallum“壁垒”，以及普通复数 intervals 和形容词 intervallic。不要把 vallum 与 venire 或 internus 混为一谈。"},"normal":[{"en":"Picture two rows of stakes around a Roman camp. The empty ground between the rows is an intervallum. That empty ground is the whole word.","cn":"想象罗马军营周围两排木桩。两排之间那块空地就是 intervallum。这块空地就是整个词的含义。"},{"en":"The same gap can be measured in space (ten metres), in time (ten minutes), in pitch (a fifth) or in numbers (0 to 1). English uses one word for all four.","cn":"同一个空隙可以用空间量（十米）、时间量（十分钟）、音高量（一个五度）或数值量（0 到 1）来测。英语用同一个词覆盖这四种。"},{"en":"In British theatres the interval is the break; in American English the same break is usually the intermission.","cn":"英式英语里剧院的休息叫 interval；美式英语里同样的休息通常叫 intermission。"},{"en":"The four inter- words have different second roots: interval (vallum 'rampart'), intervene (venire 'come'), internal (internus 'within'), interpret (uncertain, perhaps pretium 'price').","cn":"四个 inter- 词的第二个词根不同：interval（vallum“壁垒”）、intervene（venire“来”）、internal（internus“在内部”）、interpret（存疑，或与 pretium“价格”有关）。"},{"en":"Fixed patterns: at regular intervals, in the interval between, and interval training.","cn":"固定搭配：at regular intervals（按固定间隔）、in the interval between（在……之间的间隔里）、interval training（间歇训练）。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"An interval is defined by its two ends and by the nothing in the middle. Remove either end and it stops being measurable.","cn":"间隔由它的两端和中间的空无来定义。拿掉任何一端，它就不再可测量。"},{"en":"Time feels long or short according to what fills the interval, not according to its measured length.","cn":"时间显得长或短，取决于间隔里被什么填满，而不是取决于它被量出的长度。"},{"en":"Every rhythm, musical or biological, is a pattern of intervals: the rests are as structural as the beats.","cn":"一切节奏，无论音乐的还是生物的，都是间隔的模式：休止与拍子同样具有结构性。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The bus arrives at intervals of twenty minutes.","cn":"公交车每隔二十分钟到一班。"},{"en":"There was a brief interval between the two speeches.","cn":"两场演讲之间有一个短暂的间隔。"},{"en":"The data fall within a narrow interval around the mean.","cn":"数据落在均值附近一个很窄的区间内。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“因特·瓦尔”——因（为）特（意）瓦尔（在）两墙之间留出一条空道 → interval 间隔、空隙","word":"interval"},"root":"源自拉丁语 intervallum“壁垒之间的空地”，由 inter“在……之间”加 vallum“壁垒、栅栏”（单数为 vallus“木桩”）构成，核心是“两端之间空出来的那一段”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of interval, all one shape: two ends with an empty stretch between them. Time, theatre breaks, pitch, number sets, physical gaps, statistics and training schedules are all measured by that same between-space.","cn":"interval 的九个义项都是同一个形状：两端之间空出的一段。时间、剧院休息、音高、数集、物理空隙、统计范围和训练日程，都用这同一个“之间”来测量。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: two posts with deliberately empty ground between them.","cn":"核心意象：两根木桩，中间故意留出一块空地。"},"chain":["TWO POSTS","EMPTY SPACE","MEASURABLE DISTANCE","TIME BETWEEN","BREAK IN ACTIVITY","REPEATED SPACING"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S5","en":"SPACE AND TIME BETWEEN: the original empty ground between stakes, and the stretch between two events.","cn":"空间与时间上的之间：木桩之间最初的空地，以及两个事件之间的一段时间。"},{"senses":"S2","en":"SCHEDULED BREAK: a deliberate empty stretch written into a performance or match.","cn":"安排好的暂停：写进演出或比赛日程的一段故意留白。"},{"senses":"S3 · S4","en":"MEASURED ON A SCALE: distance between two pitches, and the set of numbers between two limits.","cn":"在尺度上测量：两个音高之间的距离，以及两个界限之间的数集。"},{"senses":"S6 · S9","en":"REPEATED INTERVALS: spacing that recurs as a rhythm, in bells, buses and interval training.","cn":"反复出现的间隔：作为节奏重复出现的间距，见于钟声、公交车与间歇训练。"},{"senses":"S7 · S8","en":"PROFESSIONAL RANGES: a statistical band of estimates, and a clear period between episodes of illness.","cn":"专业领域中的范围：统计估计的带状区间，以及疾病发作之间的清醒期。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Interval is a borrowed Latin noun, not an English compound. Its English family is thin: a plural, an adjective in -ic, and technical compounds such as intervalometer.","cn":"interval 是借入的拉丁名词，不是英语复合词。它的英语词族较薄：复数、-ic 形容词，以及 intervalometer 这类技术复合词。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin set is inter 'between', vallus 'stake', vallum 'rampart', intervallum 'space between ramparts'. The root is vall-, the same one that gives English wall.","cn":"拉丁词族是 inter“在……之间”、vallus“木桩”、vallum“壁垒”、intervallum“壁垒之间的空地”。词根是 vall-，也是英语 wall 的来源。"},"items":[{"word":"interval","structure":"inter- (between) + vallum (rampart)","meaning":"a space or period between two things","meaningCN":"间隔；空隙（字面“壁垒之间”）","example":"The interval between the two tests was two weeks.","exampleCN":"两次测试之间的间隔是两周。"},{"word":"intervals","structure":"interval + -s (plural)","meaning":"more than one gap or period","meaningCN":"多个间隔（复数形式）","example":"The lights flashed at intervals.","exampleCN":"灯光间隔闪烁。"},{"word":"intervallic","structure":"interval + -ic (adjective)","meaning":"relating to an interval, especially in music","meaningCN":"间隔的；音程的（-ic 构成形容词）","example":"The composer explored wide intervallic leaps.","exampleCN":"这位作曲家探索了大幅度的音程跳跃。"},{"word":"intervalometer","structure":"interval + -o- + meter (measuring device)","meaning":"a device that triggers a camera at set intervals","meaningCN":"定时拍摄器；间隔计时器（meter 表测量装置）","example":"He used an intervalometer for the time-lapse.","exampleCN":"他用定时拍摄器拍延时。"},{"word":"interval training","structure":"interval + training (compound noun)","meaning":"exercise that alternates intense bursts with recovery","meaningCN":"间歇训练（高强度与恢复交替）","example":"Interval training is hard but effective.","exampleCN":"间歇训练很辛苦但有效。"},{"word":"inter-","structure":"Latin prefix","meaning":"between, among","meaningCN":"在……之间；在……之中（前缀）","example":"Inter- appears in interval, intervene and internal.","exampleCN":"inter- 出现在 interval、intervene 和 internal 中。"},{"word":"vall-","structure":"Latin root vallus/vallum","meaning":"stake, rampart, wall","meaningCN":"木桩；壁垒；墙（词根）","example":"The vall- root also gives English wall.","exampleCN":"vall- 词根也是英语 wall 的来源。"},{"word":"-al","structure":"Latin adjective/noun suffix -alis","meaning":"forming adjectives or nouns from stems","meaningCN":"构成形容词或名词的后缀","example":"Interval itself came through the Latin noun, not through a live English -al suffix.","exampleCN":"interval 本身是经由拉丁名词传入的，不是由英语中活的 -al 后缀构成。"},{"word":"intermission","structure":"inter- + mission (sending)","meaning":"a break between parts of a show; the American word for the theatre interval","meaningCN":"幕间休息；美式英语中对应英式 interval 的词（结构相近，非同源）","example":"We talked during the intermission.","exampleCN":"幕间休息时我们聊了聊。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"inter","structure":"preposition","meaning":"between, among","meaningCN":"在……之间；在……之中"},{"word":"vallus","structure":"noun","meaning":"a stake, post","meaningCN":"木桩"},{"word":"vallum","structure":"collective of vallus","meaning":"rampart, palisade, wall","meaningCN":"壁垒；栅栏；墙"},{"word":"intervallum","structure":"inter + vallum","meaning":"space between ramparts; interval","meaningCN":"壁垒之间的空地；间隔"}]}},{"word":"intervene","ipa_uk":"/ˌɪntəˈviːn/","ipa_us":"/ˌɪntərˈviːn/","definition_zh":"干预；介入；调停；介于其间；插话","definition_en":"to come between two things or parties, often in order to change what is happening; to happen between two events","core_image":"一只手从两侧之间伸进来，隔开两样正要撞上的东西","scene":"急诊室里，监护仪突然报警，主治医生立即决定手术。护士对家属说：The surgeon decided to intervene.","sceneCN":"这里 intervene 是「（医生）介入、采取干预措施」（第 3 个义项：医疗干预）；句意：外科医生决定介入手术。图中可辨识物件：监护仪、手术灯、病床、医护人员。","pos":[{"tag":"vi.","zh":"干预；介入；调停"},{"tag":"vi.","zh":"介于其间；发生在其间"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"intervene in","zh":"干预；介入（某事）"},{"phrase":"intervene to prevent","zh":"出面阻止"},{"phrase":"intervene on behalf of","zh":"为……出面干预"},{"phrase":"government intervention","zh":"政府干预"},{"phrase":"in the intervening years","zh":"在其间的那些年里"},{"phrase":"early intervention","zh":"早期干预"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"intervenes"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"intervened"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"intervened"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"intervening"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"intervention","pos":"n.","zh":"干预；介入；调停"},{"word":"interventionist","pos":"adj./n.","zh":"干预主义的；干预主义者"},{"word":"intervening","pos":"adj.","zh":"介于其间的；插入的"},{"word":"nonintervention","pos":"n.","zh":"不干预；不干涉"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Stepping into the middle","titleCN":"走进中间：介入、干预","definition":"to become involved in a situation in order to change its course","definitionCN":"介入某个局面，以改变其发展方向","example":"The teacher intervened before the argument became a fight.","exampleCN":"争吵快要变成打架之前，老师介入了。","why":"Intervenire is inter 'between' + venire 'come': literally 'to come between'. The word begins with a body moving into the space between two sides.","whyCN":"intervenire 是 inter“在……之间”加 venire“来”，字面就是“来到中间”。这个词最初就是一个身体进入两方之间的空间。"},{"no":"02","title":"Interfering where one is not wanted","titleCN":"不请自来地插手：干涉","definition":"to involve oneself in other people's affairs, often without invitation or welcome","definitionCN":"介入他人的事务，常常未经邀请或不受欢迎","example":"Her mother intervenes in every decision she makes.","exampleCN":"她母亲干预她做的每一个决定。","why":"Coming between two sides can be rescue or intrusion, depending on whether the sides asked for help. The same physical move carries both judgments.","whyCN":"来到两方之间，既可能是救援，也可能是侵入，取决于两方是否求助。同一个物理动作承载了两种评价。"},{"no":"03","title":"Medical intervention","titleCN":"医疗干预：介入治疗","definition":"of a doctor or treatment, to act actively to stop or change a disease process","definitionCN":"（医生或治疗）主动采取行动以阻止或改变疾病进程","example":"Doctors intervened quickly when the patient's heart stopped.","exampleCN":"病人心脏停止时，医生迅速进行了干预。","why":"A disease has its own course; treatment comes between the disease and its expected outcome. The medical sense is the 'coming between' made urgent.","whyCN":"疾病有自己的进程；治疗插在疾病与它预期的结果之间。医学义就是“来到中间”被赋予了紧迫性。"},{"no":"04","title":"The years in between","titleCN":"中间那些年：介于其间发生","definition":"of a period or event, to occur between two named points in time","definitionCN":"（一段时间或事件）发生在两个明确的时间点之间","example":"In the intervening years, the village changed completely.","exampleCN":"在其间的那些年里，村庄彻底变了样。","why":"Time is a line with two marked points. What happens on the stretch between them 'comes between' the two points, so the verb describes position in time rather than action.","whyCN":"时间是一条标了两个点的线。发生在两点之间那一段的事情，就是“来到两点之间”，所以这个动词在这里描述的是时间位置，而不是动作。"},{"no":"05","title":"Pleading on someone's behalf","titleCN":"替人求情：说情、斡旋","definition":"to speak to a person in authority on behalf of someone else, asking for help or mercy","definitionCN":"代表他人向掌权者说话，请求帮助或宽恕","example":"She intervened with the judge on her brother's behalf.","exampleCN":"她替弟弟向法官求情。","why":"The person in need and the person with power are separated by a gap. The intercessor comes between them and carries a request across.","whyCN":"需要帮助的人与掌权者之间隔着一道缝隙。求情者来到中间，把请求运过去。"},{"no":"06","title":"The state steps into the market","titleCN":"国家走进市场：政府干预","definition":"of a government or central bank, to act in an economy or market to influence prices, credit or stability","definitionCN":"（政府或中央银行）在经济的市场中采取行动，以影响价格、信贷或稳定","example":"The central bank intervened to support the currency.","exampleCN":"中央银行出手干预以支撑本币。","why":"Markets are imagined as a space where buyers and sellers meet. An outside authority enters that space and changes the terms, which is intervention in its political-economic form.","whyCN":"市场被想象成买卖双方相遇的空间。一个外部权威进入这个空间并改变条件，这就是政治经济意义上的干预。"},{"no":"07","title":"A third party enters a lawsuit","titleCN":"第三方加入诉讼：诉讼参加","definition":"in law, of a third party, to join a case because one's interests are affected by its outcome","definitionCN":"法律中，第三方因自身利益受案件结果影响而加入诉讼","example":"The insurer intervened in the case to protect its position.","exampleCN":"保险公司加入诉讼以保护自己的立场。","why":"A lawsuit is a contest between two sides. A third party whose interests lie in the middle asks to 'come between' them and be heard.","whyCN":"诉讼是两方之间的较量。利益夹在中间的第三方请求“来到他们之间”并发言。"},{"no":"08","title":"Physically getting between","titleCN":"身体挡在中间：隔开","definition":"to place oneself physically between two people or things, especially to separate them","definitionCN":"把自己身体放在两个人或物之间，尤为了隔开他们","example":"He intervened between the two men before a punch was thrown.","exampleCN":"在拳头挥出之前，他挡在了两个男人中间。","why":"This is the literal scene behind all the other senses: a body occupying the gap so that the two sides can no longer reach each other.","whyCN":"这是其他所有义项背后的字面场景：一个身体占据空隙，使两边再也够不到对方。"},{"no":"09","title":"An intervening variable","titleCN":"中间变量：介于因果之间的因素","definition":"in research, a factor that lies between a cause and its observed effect and helps explain the link","definitionCN":"研究中位于原因与观察到的结果之间、有助于解释二者联系的因素","example":"Sleep quality is an intervening variable between stress and illness.","exampleCN":"睡眠质量是压力与疾病之间的中间变量。","why":"Statistics borrowed the word for a variable that sits on the path between cause and effect. It literally comes between them in the causal chain.","whyCN":"统计学借用这个词，指位于因果路径上的变量。它在因果链中确实“来到两者之间”。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Intervene comes from Latin intervenire 'to come between, interrupt, hinder', from inter 'between' + venire 'to come'. Venire goes back to PIE *gwa- 'to go, come'. English first used intervention, then back-formed the verb in the 1580s.","cn":"intervene 来自拉丁语 intervenire“来到中间、打断、阻碍”，由 inter“在……之间”加 venire“来”构成。venire 可追溯到原始印欧语 *gwa-“去、来”。英语先使用名词 intervention，16 世纪 80 年代再由它逆构出动词。"},"items":[{"era":"PIE *gwa-","en":"The root *gwa- meant 'to go, come'. It is the deep source of Latin venire and appears in English words such as convene, invent and prevent.","cn":"词根 *gwa- 意为“去、来”。它是拉丁语 venire 的深层来源，也出现在英语 convene、invent、prevent 等词中。"},{"era":"LATIN venire","en":"Venire meant 'to come'. Joined with inter, it produced intervenire, literally 'to come between'.","cn":"venire 意为“来”。与 inter 结合，产生 intervenire，字面就是“来到中间”。"},{"era":"LATIN intervenire","en":"Intervenire meant 'to come between, intervene; interrupt; stand in the way, oppose, hinder'. The senses of helping and hindering were both present from the start.","cn":"intervenire 意为“来到中间、介入；打断；挡路、反对、阻碍”。帮助与阻碍这两种意味从一开始就都存在。"},{"era":"ENGLISH intervention, early 15c.","en":"English first recorded the noun intervention in the early 15th century, originally in the religious sense of intercession or intercessory prayer.","cn":"英语最早在 15 世纪初记录名词 intervention，最初是宗教意义上的“代祷、求情”。"},{"era":"ENGLISH intervene, 1580s","en":"The verb intervene is a 1580s back-formation from intervention, or a direct borrowing from Latin. Its first English sense was 'intercept', now obsolete.","cn":"动词 intervene 是 16 世纪 80 年代由 intervention 逆构而成，或直接借自拉丁语。它最早的英语义是“拦截”，现已废弃。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, c.1600–1640s","en":"The sense 'of events, come or fall between' is from c.1600; 'interfere or act as a mediator' is from the 1640s. Modern political, medical and legal uses follow from these.","cn":"“（事件）发生于其间”的义项来自约 1600 年；“干涉或充当调停者”来自 17 世纪 40 年代。现代的政治、医疗和法律用法都由此发展而来。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group shares the intervene/venire family; the near-meaning group contains verbs of stepping into a situation, each with a different motive or method.","cn":"形近组共享 intervene/venire 词族；近义组都是“进入某个局面”的动词，动机或方式各不相同。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"intervention","ipa":"/ˌɪntəˈvenʃn/","tag":"same verb, noun","definition":"the act of becoming involved in a situation to change it. It is the -ion noun and was recorded in English before the verb.","definitionCN":"介入局面以改变它的行为。它是 -ion 名词，在英语中的记录早于动词。"},{"word":"intervening","ipa":"/ˌɪntəˈviːnɪŋ/","tag":"same verb, participle/adjective","definition":"coming between two points, especially in time, as in the intervening years. It describes position rather than action.","definitionCN":"位于两点之间的，尤指时间上，如 the intervening years。它描述位置而不是动作。"},{"word":"convene","ipa":"/kənˈviːn/","tag":"same root, different prefix","definition":"to bring people together for a meeting, or to meet. It uses con- 'together' + venire 'come', literally 'come together'.","definitionCN":"召集人们开会，或集合。它由 con-“一起”加 venire“来”构成，字面是“一起来”。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"interfere","ipa":"/ˌɪntəˈfɪə/","tag":"unwanted involvement","definition":"to get involved in a situation that does not concern you, often causing damage. It is usually negative, while intervene can be neutral or heroic.","definitionCN":"介入与你无关的局面，常造成损害。它通常带负面色彩，而 intervene 可以是中性的甚至是英雄式的。"},{"word":"intercede","ipa":"/ˌɪntəˈsiːd/","tag":"plead for someone","definition":"to speak to a powerful person on behalf of another. It is the specific 'pleading' sense of intervene, made into its own verb.","definitionCN":"代表他人向有权者说话。它是 intervene 中“求情”这一特定义项独立成的动词。"},{"word":"mediate","ipa":"/ˈmiːdieɪt/","tag":"help two sides talk","definition":"to help two sides in a dispute reach an agreement. It stresses the neutral helper's role rather than the act of entering.","definitionCN":"帮助争执双方达成协议。它强调中立帮助者的角色，而不是“进入”的动作。"},{"word":"step in","ipa":"/step ɪn/","tag":"phrasal, informal","definition":"to take action to help in a situation. It is the everyday spoken equivalent of intervene, without the formal or political weight.","definitionCN":"采取行动帮助某个局面。它是 intervene 的日常口语对应说法，没有正式或政治分量。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: inter- 'between' and venire 'come', plus the ordinary family intervention, interventionist, intervening, nonintervention.","cn":"只用真实构件：inter-“在……之间”和 venire“来”，以及常用词族 intervention、interventionist、intervening、nonintervention。"},"normal":[{"en":"Inter- = between, venire = come. Intervene is literally 'come between': a third body enters the gap and changes what the two sides can do.","cn":"inter- = 在……之间，venire = 来。intervene 字面就是“来到中间”：第三个身体进入空隙，改变了两边能做的事。"},{"en":"The same move can be rescue or intrusion. 'Intervene' is neutral; 'interfere' usually carries the complaint.","cn":"同一个动作可能是救援，也可能是侵入。intervene 是中性的；interfere 通常带有抱怨。"},{"en":"Intervention is the noun and came first; intervene is the later back-formation from it.","cn":"intervention 是名词，而且先出现；intervene 是后来由它逆构出的动词。"},{"en":"The four inter- words split by second root: intervene (venire 'come'), interval (vallum 'rampart'), internal (internus 'within'), interpret (uncertain, perhaps pretium 'price').","cn":"四个 inter- 词按第二词根区分：intervene（venire“来”）、interval（vallum“壁垒”）、internal（internus“在内部”）、interpret（存疑，或与 pretium“价格”有关）。"},{"en":"Fixed patterns: intervene in a dispute, intervene to prevent something, and in the intervening years.","cn":"固定搭配：intervene in a dispute（介入争端）、intervene to prevent something（出面阻止某事）、in the intervening years（在其间的那些年）。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Every intervention assumes a course that would have continued without it. To intervene is to introduce a second possible future.","cn":"每一次干预都预设了一条本来会继续下去的进程。干预就是引入第二种可能的未来。"},{"en":"The ethics of intervention live in the gap between 'they need help' and 'they did not ask'. The same act can be care or control.","cn":"干预的伦理就住在“他们需要帮助”与“他们没开口”之间的缝隙里。同一个行为可以是关怀，也可以是控制。"},{"en":"In time, intervention is invisible: the intervening years are simply the stretch that separated two named moments.","cn":"在时间中，干预是隐形的：intervening years 不过是隔开两个被命名时刻的那一段。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The referee intervened when the players began to push each other.","cn":"球员开始推搡时，裁判介入了。"},{"en":"The government intervened to keep the banks from failing.","cn":"政府出手干预，以防止银行倒闭。"},{"en":"Much had changed in the intervening decade.","cn":"在其间的十年里，许多事情都变了。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“因特·维恩”——因（为）特（地）维恩（护）中间秩序，才走进两边 → intervene 介入、干预","word":"intervene"},"root":"源自拉丁语 intervenire“来到中间、打断”，由 inter“在……之间”加 venire“来”构成，核心是“第三方走进两方之间的空隙”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of intervene, all one movement: a third thing comes between two sides. A teacher, a doctor, a government, a court, a pleading relative or a statistical variable can each occupy that gap and change the outcome.","cn":"intervene 的九个义项都是同一个动作：第三个东西来到两方之间。老师、医生、政府、法院、求情的亲属或统计变量，都可以占据那道空隙并改变结果。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a hand entering the gap between two things about to collide.","cn":"核心意象：一只手伸进两样即将相撞的东西之间的空隙。"},"chain":["TWO SIDES","OPEN GAP","THIRD PARTY COMES","OCCUPIES BETWEEN","CHANGES THE COURSE","NEW OUTCOME"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S8","en":"PHYSICAL AND GENERAL ENTRY: a body or a person steps into the middle to separate or redirect.","cn":"物理与一般性的进入：一个身体或一个人走进中间，隔开或改变方向。"},{"senses":"S2","en":"UNWANTED ENTRY: the same movement becomes interference when the sides did not ask for help.","cn":"不受欢迎的进入：当两方并未求助时，同一个动作就变成干涉。"},{"senses":"S3 · S5","en":"HELPING ENTRY: medical treatment enters a disease's course, and an intercessor carries a plea across the gap.","cn":"援助性的进入：医疗进入疾病的进程，求情者把请求运过缝隙。"},{"senses":"S4 · S9","en":"POSITION IN A CHAIN: events or variables that sit between two named points, in time or in a causal path.","cn":"链条中的位置：位于两个明确点之间的事件或变量，或在时间上，或在因果路径上。"},{"senses":"S6 · S7","en":"INSTITUTIONAL ENTRY: a state enters a market, and a third party enters a lawsuit to protect its interests.","cn":"制度性的进入：国家进入市场，第三方为保护自身利益加入诉讼。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Intervene is a Latin verb borrowed into English. Its family is built with -tion, -ist, -ing and the negative prefix non-.","cn":"intervene 是借入英语的拉丁动词。它的词族用 -tion、-ist、-ing 和否定前缀 non- 构成。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin set is inter 'between', venire 'come', intervenire 'come between', and interventionem 'a coming between'.","cn":"拉丁词族是 inter“在……之间”、venire“来”、intervenire“来到中间”、interventionem“来到中间的行为”。"},"items":[{"word":"intervene","structure":"inter- (between) + ven- (come) + -e","meaning":"to come between; to step into a situation","meaningCN":"介入；干预（字面“来到中间”）","example":"The UN intervened to stop the fighting.","exampleCN":"联合国介入以停止战斗。"},{"word":"intervenes","structure":"intervene + -s (third person singular)","meaning":"steps into a situation","meaningCN":"介入（第三人称单数）","example":"She intervenes whenever the debate turns personal.","exampleCN":"每当辩论变成人身攻击，她就会介入。"},{"word":"intervened","structure":"intervene + -ed (past)","meaning":"stepped into a situation in the past","meaningCN":"介入（过去式）","example":"The court intervened last year.","exampleCN":"法院去年介入了。"},{"word":"intervening","structure":"intervene + -ing (participle/adjective)","meaning":"coming between, especially in time","meaningCN":"介于其间的（尤指时间上）","example":"The intervening months were quiet.","exampleCN":"其间的几个月很平静。"},{"word":"intervention","structure":"intervene + -tion (noun of action)","meaning":"the act of stepping in to change a situation","meaningCN":"干预；介入（-tion 构成动作名词）","example":"Early intervention saved the project.","exampleCN":"早期干预挽救了这个项目。"},{"word":"interventionist","structure":"intervention + -ist (person or doctrine)","meaning":"favoring active intervention, especially by the state","meaningCN":"干预主义的；干预主义者","example":"The party adopted an interventionist policy.","exampleCN":"该党采取了干预主义政策。"},{"word":"interventional","structure":"intervention + -al (adjective)","meaning":"relating to intervention, especially in medicine","meaningCN":"介入性的（尤用于医学）","example":"He underwent an interventional procedure.","exampleCN":"他接受了一次介入手术。"},{"word":"nonintervention","structure":"non- (not) + intervention","meaning":"the policy of not stepping in","meaningCN":"不干预；不干涉（non- 表否定）","example":"The country maintained a policy of nonintervention.","exampleCN":"该国坚持不干预政策。"},{"word":"counterintervention","structure":"counter- (against) + intervention","meaning":"an intervention made to oppose another intervention","meaningCN":"反干预；对抗性干预","example":"The second move was a counterintervention.","exampleCN":"第二步是对抗性干预。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"inter","structure":"preposition","meaning":"between, among","meaningCN":"在……之间；在……之中"},{"word":"venire","structure":"PIE *gwa- 'go, come'","meaning":"to come","meaningCN":"来"},{"word":"intervenire","structure":"inter + venire","meaning":"to come between, interrupt, hinder","meaningCN":"来到中间；打断；阻碍"},{"word":"interventio","structure":"intervenire + -tio","meaning":"a coming between; intercession","meaningCN":"来到中间；代祷；干预"}]}},{"word":"investigate","ipa_uk":"/ɪnˈvestɪɡeɪt/","ipa_us":"/ɪnˈvestɪɡeɪt/","definition_zh":"调查；侦查；研究；探究","definition_en":"to examine a matter carefully in order to discover the facts; to study something systematically","core_image":"侦探低着头，沿着泥地上的一串脚印一路追下去","scene":"雨后的空地上，刑侦人员蹲在泥边，用手电照着一串脚印。主管对同伴说：We need to investigate the scene.","sceneCN":"这里 investigate 是「调查、追查现场」（第 1、2 个义项：系统查证、刑侦调查）；句意：我们需要调查这个现场。图中可辨识物件：手电、脚印、泥地、警戒带。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"调查；侦查；研究"},{"tag":"vi.","zh":"进行调查；做研究"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"investigate a crime","zh":"调查一桩犯罪"},{"phrase":"investigate the cause of","zh":"调查……的原因"},{"phrase":"investigate a complaint","zh":"调查投诉"},{"phrase":"investigate thoroughly","zh":"彻底调查"},{"phrase":"investigate allegations","zh":"调查指控"},{"phrase":"investigate the possibility of","zh":"探究……的可能性"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"investigates"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"investigated"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"investigated"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"investigating"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"investigation","pos":"n.","zh":"调查；侦查；研究"},{"word":"investigator","pos":"n.","zh":"调查者；侦查员"},{"word":"investigative","pos":"adj.","zh":"调查性的；侦查的"},{"word":"investigatory","pos":"adj.","zh":"调查的；侦查的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Following the facts to their source","titleCN":"顺着事实追到源头：调查","definition":"to examine a matter carefully and systematically in order to discover the truth","definitionCN":"仔细而有系统地查证一件事，以发现真相","example":"The company investigated the cause of the accident.","exampleCN":"公司调查了事故的原因。","why":"Latin vestigium means 'footprint'. Investigare is 'to follow the footprints', and the English word still carries that picture: you do not guess, you trace.","whyCN":"拉丁语 vestigium 意为“脚印”。investigare 就是“跟着脚印走”，英语这个词仍带着这幅画面：不是猜，而是循迹。"},{"no":"02","title":"The police follow a trail","titleCN":"警方循线追查：侦查","definition":"of the police or authorities, to examine a crime or suspect in order to gather evidence","definitionCN":"（警方或当局）为收集证据而查证犯罪或嫌疑人","example":"Detectives investigated the robbery for months.","exampleCN":"侦探对这起抢劫案调查了数月。","why":"A criminal leaves traces: footprints, fingerprints, records. The investigative image of following marks is at its most literal in police work.","whyCN":"犯罪会留下痕迹：脚印、指纹、记录。在警务工作中，“跟着痕迹走”的意象最接近字面。"},{"no":"03","title":"Science as organised tracing","titleCN":"科学作为有组织的追踪：研究","definition":"to study a natural phenomenon systematically through observation and experiment","definitionCN":"通过观察与实验系统地研究自然现象","example":"The team investigated how the virus spreads.","exampleCN":"团队研究了这种病毒如何传播。","why":"Science follows nature's traces: signals, correlations, effects. The word's core action, tracing something back, fits the experimental method exactly.","whyCN":"科学追踪自然的痕迹：信号、相关性、效应。这个词的核心动作“回溯追踪”，正好契合实验方法。"},{"no":"04","title":"Journalism looks into wrongdoing","titleCN":"新闻追踪不法：调查报道","definition":"of a journalist, to look into possible wrongdoing and gather evidence for publication","definitionCN":"（记者）查证可能存在的不法行为，并为发表收集证据","example":"The reporter investigated the company's hidden payments.","exampleCN":"记者调查了这家公司的隐秘付款。","why":"A story is followed the way a trail is followed: one lead points to the next. Investigative journalism keeps the metaphor of the trail.","whyCN":"一条新闻线索被追踪的方式，就像追踪脚印：一个线索指向下一个。调查报道保留了“追踪”的比喻。"},{"no":"05","title":"Checking a person's background","titleCN":"查一个人的底细：审查","definition":"to examine someone's background, conduct or records, often before trusting them","definitionCN":"查证某人的背景、行为或记录，通常在信任他们之前","example":"The agency investigated the applicant's history.","exampleCN":"该机构调查了申请人的过往。","why":"A person also leaves a trail in documents and records. Investigating a person is following that paper trail to see where it leads.","whyCN":"一个人也会在文件和记录里留下轨迹。调查一个人，就是沿着这条纸面轨迹看它通向哪里。"},{"no":"06","title":"Exploring a subject","titleCN":"探究一个题目：钻研","definition":"to study or explore a question, subject or possibility in depth","definitionCN":"深入钻研或探索一个问题、主题或可能性","example":"We are investigating whether the method can be improved.","exampleCN":"我们正在研究这个方法能否改进。","why":"Not every investigation begins with a crime. Any unknown can be treated as a trail whose end has not yet been reached.","whyCN":"并非每次调查都从犯罪开始。任何未知都可以被当作一条尚未走到尽头的线索。"},{"no":"07","title":"A formal inquiry","titleCN":"正式调查：委员会查证","definition":"of a committee, regulator or official body, to hold a formal inquiry into a matter","definitionCN":"（委员会、监管机构或官方机构）对某事进行正式调查","example":"An independent committee investigated the failure.","exampleCN":"一个独立委员会调查了这次事故。","why":"Institutions need a word for the slow, documented version of following a trail. The formal inquiry is investigation with procedure attached.","whyCN":"机构需要一个词来表示“循迹”的缓慢、留档版本。正式调查就是附带了程序的 investigation。"},{"no":"08","title":"Probing a hypothesis","titleCN":"检验一个假设：探查","definition":"to test or probe a hypothesis, explanation or claim by looking for evidence","definitionCN":"通过寻找证据来检验或探查一个假设、解释或主张","example":"They investigated the hypothesis that stress weakens immunity.","exampleCN":"他们检验了压力会削弱免疫力这一假设。","why":"A hypothesis predicts traces. To investigate it is to go looking for those traces and see whether they are actually there.","whyCN":"假设会预言某些痕迹。调查一个假设，就是去找这些痕迹，看它们是否真的存在。"},{"no":"09","title":"Tracing an outbreak to its origin","titleCN":"追查源头：溯源","definition":"to trace the origin or spread of a problem, disease or phenomenon","definitionCN":"追溯一个问题、疾病或现象的来源或传播路径","example":"Health workers investigated the source of the outbreak.","exampleCN":"卫生工作者追查了这次疫情的源头。","why":"This is the oldest image made modern: something has passed through a place and left marks, and the investigator walks the marks backward to the first one.","whyCN":"这是最古老的意象被现代化：某物经过一个地方并留下痕迹，调查者沿着痕迹往回走，直到第一处。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Investigate comes from Latin investigare 'to trace out, search after', from in- 'in, into' + vestigare 'to track', from vestigium 'footprint, track'. The word literally means 'to follow the footprints into something'.","cn":"investigate 来自拉丁语 investigare“追踪出来、搜寻”，由 in-“进入”加 vestigare“追踪”构成，后者来自 vestigium“脚印、痕迹”。这个词字面上就是“跟着脚印走进某事里去”。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN vestigium","en":"Vestigium meant 'footprint, track, mark'. It is also the source of English vestige 'a remaining trace'. The whole word family is about marks left behind.","cn":"vestigium 意为“脚印、足迹、痕迹”。它也是英语 vestige“残留痕迹”的来源。整个词族都与留下的痕迹有关。"},{"era":"LATIN vestigare","en":"Vestigare meant 'to track, trace'. It turned the noun for a footprint into the action of following one.","cn":"vestigare 意为“追踪、循迹”。它把表示脚印的名词变成了“跟着脚印走”的动作。"},{"era":"LATIN investigare","en":"With in- 'in, into', investigare meant 'to trace out, search after', figuratively 'search into, investigate'. The prefix adds direction: follow the tracks into the matter.","cn":"加上 in-“进入”，investigare 意为“追踪出来、搜寻”，引申为“深入查究”。前缀增加了方向：跟着痕迹走进事情内部。"},{"era":"ENGLISH investigation, early 15c.","en":"English first recorded the noun investigation in the early 15th century, borrowed through Old French from Latin investigatio.","cn":"英语最早在 15 世纪初记录名词 investigation，经由古法语借自拉丁语 investigatio。"},{"era":"ENGLISH investigate, c.1500","en":"The verb investigate is either a back-formation from investigation or a direct borrowing of the Latin past participle investigatus. It is recorded from about 1500.","cn":"动词 investigate 要么是由 investigation 逆构而成，要么是直接借用拉丁语过去分词 investigatus。记录于约 1500 年。"},{"era":"MODERN SPECIALISATIONS","en":"Police, science, journalism and regulation each developed their own procedures for investigation, but all keep the original action: follow the traces until the source is reached.","cn":"警务、科学、新闻和监管各自发展出自己的调查程序，但都保留了最初的动作：沿着痕迹走，直到抵达源头。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group shares the vestig- 'track' root; the near-meaning group contains verbs of careful looking, each with a different method or purpose.","cn":"形近组共享 vestig-“痕迹”词根；近义组都是“仔细查看”的动词，方法与目的各不相同。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"investigation","ipa":"/ɪnˌvestɪˈɡeɪʃn/","tag":"same verb, noun","definition":"a careful examination to discover the facts. It is the -ion noun and was recorded before the verb.","definitionCN":"为查明事实而进行的仔细查证。它是 -ion 名词，记录早于动词。"},{"word":"investigative","ipa":"/ɪnˈvestɪɡətɪv/","tag":"same verb, adjective","definition":"relating to or suited for investigation, as in investigative journalism. The -ive suffix marks a method or purpose.","definitionCN":"与调查有关的或适合调查的，如调查报道。-ive 后缀标记方法或目的。"},{"word":"vestige","ipa":"/ˈvestɪdʒ/","tag":"same root, noun","definition":"a small remaining trace of something that once existed. It is the bare Latin vestigium without the in- prefix.","definitionCN":"曾经存在之物的微小残留痕迹。它是去掉 in- 前缀后裸露的拉丁语 vestigium。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"examine","ipa":"/ɪɡˈzæmɪn/","tag":"look closely","definition":"to look at something closely and carefully. It focuses on inspection of the thing in front of you, not on following a trail to a source.","definitionCN":"仔细地看某物。它关注对眼前事物的检查，而不是沿着线索追到源头。"},{"word":"probe","ipa":"/prəʊb/","tag":"push into","definition":"to investigate something closely, often by asking difficult questions. It suggests pressure and penetration rather than systematic tracing.","definitionCN":"仔细调查某事，常通过提出尖锐问题。它暗示施压与深入，而不是系统性的循迹。"},{"word":"scrutinize","ipa":"/ˈskruːtənaɪz/","tag":"critical inspection","definition":"to examine something very carefully and critically. It stresses suspicion and detail, often of documents or accounts.","definitionCN":"非常仔细且挑剔地检查。它强调怀疑与细节，常用于文件或账目。"},{"word":"inquire","ipa":"/ɪnˈkwaɪə/","tag":"ask questions","definition":"to ask for information. It is the questioning step within an investigation, not the whole process.","definitionCN":"询问信息。它是调查中的提问环节，而不是整个过程。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: in- 'into' and vestigium 'footprint', plus the ordinary family investigation, investigator, investigative, investigatory.","cn":"只用真实构件：in-“进入”与 vestigium“脚印”，以及常用词族 investigation、investigator、investigative、investigatory。"},"normal":[{"en":"Vestigium = footprint. Investigate = follow the footprints into the matter. The detective image is not a mnemonic trick; it is the literal etymology.","cn":"vestigium = 脚印。investigate = 跟着脚印走进事情里。侦探的画面不是记忆技巧，而是字面词源。"},{"en":"Vestige is the same root without in-: a vestige is a trace that remains, while investigate is the act of following that trace.","cn":"vestige 是去掉 in- 的同一词根：vestige 是留下的痕迹，investigate 是跟着痕迹走的动作。"},{"en":"Investigation is the noun and came first; investigate is the later verb. The pair behaves like many Latin borrowings in English.","cn":"investigation 是名词而且先出现；investigate 是后来的动词。这一对的行为像英语中许多拉丁借词。"},{"en":"Different fields investigate different trails: police follow physical traces, scientists follow causal traces, journalists follow documentary traces.","cn":"不同领域追踪不同的痕迹：警察追踪物理痕迹，科学家追踪因果痕迹，记者追踪文件痕迹。"},{"en":"Fixed patterns: investigate a crime, investigate the cause of something, investigate allegations, and investigate whether something is possible.","cn":"固定搭配：investigate a crime（调查犯罪）、investigate the cause of something（调查某事的原因）、investigate allegations（调查指控）、investigate whether something is possible（研究某事是否可能）。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"An investigation is a path, not a leap. It moves from trace to trace, and every answer must point to the next trace.","cn":"调查是一条路径，而不是一次跳跃。它从一个痕迹走到下一个，每个答案都必须指向下一个痕迹。"},{"en":"The same word covers finding a criminal, finding a cause and finding a meaning, because all three are forms of walking backward along marks.","cn":"同一个词覆盖抓罪犯、找原因和找意义，因为这三者都是沿着痕迹往回走的形式。"},{"en":"An investigation ends not when all questions are answered but when the trail reaches a point that leaves no further mark.","cn":"调查的结束不是在所有问题都被回答时，而是在痕迹走到一个不再留下任何标记的点时。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The police are investigating a series of burglaries.","cn":"警方正在调查一系列入室盗窃案。"},{"en":"Scientists are investigating why the bees are disappearing.","cn":"科学家正在研究蜜蜂为什么会消失。"},{"en":"The committee was set up to investigate the allegations.","cn":"该委员会是为调查这些指控而设立的。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“因·外斯提·给特”——因（为）外斯提（提着）给特（别的）灯，照着脚印一路查 → investigate 调查、侦查","word":"investigate"},"root":"源自拉丁语 investigare“追踪出来、搜寻”，由 in-“进入”加 vestigare“追踪”构成，vestigare 又来自 vestigium“脚印、痕迹”，核心是“跟着痕迹走进去查”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of investigate, all one action: follow the traces. Police, scientists, reporters, committees and health workers each walk a different kind of trail, but every sense keeps the original footprint at its centre.","cn":"investigate 的九个义项都是同一个动作：跟着痕迹走。警察、科学家、记者、委员会和卫生工作者各自沿着不同类型的痕迹走，但每个义项的中心都保留着最初的那枚脚印。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a detective following a line of footprints across wet ground.","cn":"核心意象：侦探沿着湿地上的一串脚印往前走。"},"chain":["A MARK IS LEFT","SOMEONE NOTICES","FOLLOW THE TRACE","GATHER EVIDENCE","RECONSTRUCT THE PATH","REACH THE SOURCE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S7","en":"SYSTEMATIC INQUIRY: a careful, documented following of facts, whether by a company or a formal committee.","cn":"系统查证：对事实进行仔细、留档的追踪，无论由公司还是正式委员会进行。"},{"senses":"S2","en":"CRIMINAL TRACING: physical traces such as footprints, fingerprints and records lead police to a suspect.","cn":"刑事追踪：脚印、指纹和记录等物理痕迹把警方引向嫌疑人。"},{"senses":"S3 · S8","en":"SCIENTIFIC TRACING: observed effects are followed back to causes, and hypotheses are tested by looking for predicted traces.","cn":"科学追踪：从观察到的效果回溯原因，并通过寻找预测中的痕迹来检验假设。"},{"senses":"S4 · S5","en":"DOCUMENTARY TRACING: reporters follow leads and institutions follow paper records to check a person or a claim.","cn":"文件追踪：记者追踪线索，机构追踪纸面记录，以核查一个人或一项主张。"},{"senses":"S6 · S9","en":"OPEN-ENDED TRACING: exploring any unknown, and walking an outbreak backward to its first case.","cn":"开放式的追踪：探究任何未知，以及把一次疫情往回走到第一例。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Investigate is a Latin verb borrowed into English, built from in- + vestig- + -ate. Its family uses -tion, -or, -ive and -ory.","cn":"investigate 是借入英语的拉丁动词，由 in- + vestig- + -ate 构成。它的词族使用 -tion、-or、-ive、-ory。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin set is vestigium 'footprint', vestigare 'to track', investigare 'to trace out', and investigatio 'a searching into'.","cn":"拉丁词族是 vestigium“脚印”、vestigare“追踪”、investigare“追踪出来”、investigatio“查究”。"},"items":[{"word":"investigate","structure":"in- (into) + vestig- (track) + -ate (verb)","meaning":"to follow traces in order to find the facts","meaningCN":"调查；侦查（字面“跟着痕迹走进去”）","example":"They investigated the source of the noise.","exampleCN":"他们调查了噪音的来源。"},{"word":"investigates","structure":"investigate + -s (third person singular)","meaning":"carries out an investigation","meaningCN":"调查（第三人称单数）","example":"She investigates every complaint personally.","exampleCN":"她亲自调查每一起投诉。"},{"word":"investigated","structure":"investigate + -ed (past)","meaning":"examined in the past","meaningCN":"调查了（过去式）","example":"The matter was investigated last month.","exampleCN":"这件事上个月被调查过。"},{"word":"investigating","structure":"investigate + -ing (participle)","meaning":"currently examining","meaningCN":"正在调查（现在分词）","example":"The team is investigating the failure.","exampleCN":"团队正在调查这次故障。"},{"word":"investigation","structure":"investigate + -tion (noun of action)","meaning":"a careful examination to find the facts","meaningCN":"调查；侦查（-tion 构成动作名词）","example":"The investigation took six months.","exampleCN":"调查花了六个月。"},{"word":"investigator","structure":"investigate + -or (agent)","meaning":"a person who carries out an investigation","meaningCN":"调查者；侦查员（-or 表施动者）","example":"The investigator interviewed ten witnesses.","exampleCN":"调查员询问了十名证人。"},{"word":"investigative","structure":"investigate + -ive (adjective)","meaning":"relating to or used for investigation","meaningCN":"调查性的；侦查的（-ive 构成形容词）","example":"She is known for investigative reporting.","exampleCN":"她以调查报道闻名。"},{"word":"investigatory","structure":"investigate + -ory (adjective)","meaning":"of or for investigation, often formal","meaningCN":"调查的；侦查的（-ory 构成形容词，较正式）","example":"The agency has investigatory powers.","exampleCN":"该机构拥有调查权。"},{"word":"reinvestigate","structure":"re- (again) + investigate","meaning":"to investigate again after new evidence","meaningCN":"重新调查（re- 表再、重新）","example":"The case was reinvestigated in 2020.","exampleCN":"该案在 2020 年被重新调查。"},{"word":"vestige","structure":"Latin vestigium (same root, no prefix)","meaning":"a remaining trace of something gone","meaningCN":"残留痕迹；遗迹（同词根，无前缀）","example":"Only a vestige of the old wall remains.","exampleCN":"旧墙只剩下一丝遗迹。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"vestigium","structure":"Latin noun","meaning":"footprint, track, mark","meaningCN":"脚印；足迹；痕迹"},{"word":"vestigare","structure":"verb from vestigium","meaning":"to track, trace","meaningCN":"追踪；循迹"},{"word":"investigare","structure":"in- + vestigare","meaning":"to trace out, search after, investigate","meaningCN":"追踪出来；搜寻；调查"},{"word":"investigatio","structure":"investigare + -tio","meaning":"a searching into","meaningCN":"查究；调查"}]}},{"word":"involve","ipa_uk":"/ɪnˈvɒlv/","ipa_us":"/ɪnˈvɑːlv/","definition_zh":"涉及；包含；使参与；牵连；需要","definition_en":"to include as a necessary part; to make someone take part; to affect or implicate someone; to require","core_image":"一块布从外向内卷起，把里面的东西一层层裹住","scene":"厨房里，厨师把馅料铺在面皮上，再一点点卷起来。他对学徒说：Making this dish involves three hours of work.","sceneCN":"这里 involve 是「需要、包含（工作）」（第 1、6 个义项：把某物作为必要部分包含进来、需要）；句意：做这道菜需要三个小时的工作。图中可辨识物件：面皮、馅料、擀面杖、操作台。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"涉及；包含；使参与；需要"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"牵连；使卷入"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"be involved in","zh":"参与；卷入"},{"phrase":"involve somebody in","zh":"让某人参与"},{"phrase":"involve a risk","zh":"带有风险"},{"phrase":"what does it involve","zh":"这需要做些什么"},{"phrase":"be involved with","zh":"与……有牵连；与……有恋爱关系"},{"phrase":"involve a lot of work","zh":"需要大量工作"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"involves"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"involved"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"involved"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"involving"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"involvement","pos":"n.","zh":"参与；牵连；投入"},{"word":"involved","pos":"adj.","zh":"参与的；牵连的；复杂的"},{"word":"involute","pos":"adj.","zh":"内卷的；错综复杂的（同词根）"},{"word":"involution","pos":"n.","zh":"内卷；回旋；退化（同词根）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Wrapped into the whole","titleCN":"被卷进整体：包含、涉及","definition":"to include something as a necessary part of a whole","definitionCN":"把某物作为整体的必要部分包含进来","example":"The job involves a lot of travelling.","exampleCN":"这份工作需要大量出差。","why":"Latin involvere is in- 'in' + volvere 'to roll'. The image is a cloth rolled around something: whatever is inside the roll is included in it.","whyCN":"拉丁语 involvere 是 in-“进入”加 volvere“卷”。画面是一块布把某物卷在里面：凡是被卷进去的，就都属于它。"},{"no":"02","title":"Bringing someone into the roll","titleCN":"把人卷进来：使参与","definition":"to make someone take part in an activity or process","definitionCN":"使某人参加某项活动或过程","example":"They involved local residents in the planning.","exampleCN":"他们让当地居民参与了规划。","why":"The cloth does not only enclose things; it can be made to enclose a new person. To involve someone is to add them to what is wrapped inside the activity.","whyCN":"布不只是包住东西，也可以被拉过来包住一个新的人。involve 某人，就是把他加进活动所包裹的范围里。"},{"no":"03","title":"It touches you whether you like it or not","titleCN":"不管你愿不愿意都被牵涉：与……有关","definition":"of a matter, to affect or concern someone","definitionCN":"（事情）影响到或关系到某人","example":"This decision involves every member of the team.","exampleCN":"这个决定关系到团队的每一位成员。","why":"When a matter is rolled up, it can catch people who happen to lie within its folds. Being involved here is being inside the affected area.","whyCN":"一件事被卷起来时，会把它褶皱里的人一并卷住。这里的 be involved 就是处在这个受影响的范围之内。"},{"no":"04","title":"Caught in a wrongdoing","titleCN":"被卷进坏事：牵连","definition":"to show that someone took part in a crime, scandal or questionable activity","definitionCN":"表明某人参与了犯罪、丑闻或可疑活动","example":"Two officials were involved in the corruption case.","exampleCN":"两名官员卷入了这起腐败案。","why":"The same enclosure becomes a trap: once a person is wrapped into the case, the case holds them. English inherited this darker shade from the 'implicated' sense.","whyCN":"同一个包裹变成了陷阱：一个人一旦被卷进案件，案件就抓住了他。英语从“被牵连”这一义继承了这层更暗的色彩。"},{"no":"05","title":"Emotionally entangled","titleCN":"情感上卷入：投入、有恋爱关系","definition":"to be emotionally committed to someone or something, including a romantic relationship","definitionCN":"在情感上投入某人或某事，包括恋爱关系","example":"He is seriously involved with someone he met at work.","exampleCN":"他和一个在工作中认识的人认真交往着。","why":"Emotional involvement is being wrapped in another person's life. The phrase be involved with keeps the 'enclosures' metaphor for closeness.","whyCN":"情感上的 involvement 就是被另一个人的生活包裹住。be involved with 这个短语用“包裹”的比喻来表达亲近。"},{"no":"06","title":"What the task requires","titleCN":"任务需要什么：牵涉到、意味着","definition":"of a task or plan, to require something as part of doing it","definitionCN":"（任务或计划）作为完成它的一部分而需要某物","example":"Setting up the lab involved buying new equipment.","exampleCN":"建立实验室需要购买新设备。","why":"Whatever is required is necessarily inside the task. 'Involves' answers the question 'what is wrapped up in doing this?'","whyCN":"凡是被需要的，必定在任务里面。“involves”回答的正是“做这件事到底裹进了哪些东西”。"},{"no":"07","title":"Literally rolled around","titleCN":"字面意义上的卷：包裹、笼罩","definition":"of a covering, to wrap or envelop something; used literally and in technical writing","definitionCN":"（覆盖物）把某物包住或笼罩；用于字面义和技术性写作","example":"Mist involved the whole valley at dawn.","exampleCN":"黎明时雾气笼罩了整个山谷。","why":"This is the oldest sense, kept alive in poetry: fog or cloud rolls around a landscape and hides it. All the abstract senses are shadows of this physical roll.","whyCN":"这是最古老的义项，保留在诗歌中：雾或云把一片景色卷住并藏起来。所有抽象义都是这个物理“卷”的影子。"},{"no":"08","title":"Logically entailed","titleCN":"逻辑上蕴含：必然带出","definition":"of a statement or concept, to imply or entail something as a consequence","definitionCN":"（陈述或概念）作为结果蕴含或必然带出某物","example":"The claim involves a contradiction.","exampleCN":"这个主张蕴含着一个矛盾。","why":"In logic, one proposition can contain another the way a rolled cloth contains what is inside it. The consequence is not separate; it is already folded in.","whyCN":"在逻辑中，一个命题可以像卷起的布包住里面的东西那样包含另一个命题。结论不是分离的，它早已被折在里面。"},{"no":"09","title":"The adjective: complicated","titleCN":"involved：被卷得复杂的","definition":"of a description, plot or situation, complicated and difficult to follow because many parts are folded together","definitionCN":"（描述、情节或局面）因许多部分折在一起而复杂难懂","example":"The plot is so involved that I lost track of who was who.","exampleCN":"情节太复杂，我分不清谁是谁了。","why":"A cloth rolled many times has many folds. The adjective involved (from the 17th century) names that many-folded quality, which is why it also means 'complicated'.","whyCN":"一块布卷了很多层就有很多褶皱。形容词 involved（17 世纪起）命名了这种多褶的状态，所以它也有“复杂”的意思。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Involve comes from Latin involvere 'to envelop, surround, overwhelm', literally 'to roll into', from in- 'in' + volvere 'to roll'. English first used it of wrapping and clouding, then of inclusion, participation and implication.","cn":"involve 来自拉丁语 involvere“包住、围住、压倒”，字面是“卷进去”，由 in-“进入”加 volvere“卷”构成。英语先用于包裹与遮蔽，再发展出包含、参与和牵连等义。"},"items":[{"era":"PIE *wel-","en":"The root *wel- meant 'to turn, revolve'. It lies behind Latin volvere and English words such as revolve, evolve and volume.","cn":"词根 *wel- 意为“转、旋转”。它是拉丁语 volvere 以及英语 revolve、evolve、volume 等词的深层来源。"},{"era":"LATIN volvere","en":"Volvere meant 'to roll, turn over, wind'. A scroll was rolled; a snake coils; a wave turns over. The root is about circular motion.","cn":"volvere 意为“卷、翻转、缠绕”。卷轴被卷起；蛇盘绕；浪翻卷。这个词根讲的是圆周运动。"},{"era":"LATIN involvere","en":"Involvere meant 'to envelop, surround, overwhelm', literally 'to roll into'. The prefix in- adds direction: roll something into the cover.","cn":"involvere 意为“包住、围住、压倒”，字面是“卷进去”。前缀 in- 增加方向：把某物卷进覆盖物里。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, late 14c.","en":"English records involve in the late 14th century meaning 'envelop, surround; make cloudy or obscure'. The physical roll came first.","cn":"英语在 14 世纪晚期记录 involve，意为“包住、围住；使模糊”。物理上的“卷”先出现。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, mid-15c. to c.1600","en":"From the mid-15th century it meant 'concern oneself'; by c.1600 it had the sense 'take in, include'. The movement from wrapping to including is natural: what is rolled in is inside.","cn":"从 15 世纪中期起，它表示“使自己卷入”；到约 1600 年已有“包含、纳入”的义项。从“包裹”到“包含”的转变很自然：卷进去的就在里面。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, 17c.","en":"The adjective involved developed the sense 'complicated' in the 1640s, from the picture of many folds. Earlier it meant 'spirally curved'.","cn":"形容词 involved 在 17 世纪 40 年代发展出“复杂”义，来自“许多褶皱”的画面。更早时它意为“螺旋弯曲的”。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group shares the volvere 'roll' root or the involve family; the near-meaning group contains verbs of inclusion and connection, each with a different strength.","cn":"形近组共享 volvere“卷”词根或 involve 词族；近义组是包含与关联类动词，强度各不相同。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"involvement","ipa":"/ɪnˈvɒlvmənt/","tag":"same verb, noun","definition":"the state of taking part in, or being connected with, something. It is involve + -ment.","definitionCN":"参与或与某事有关联的状态。它是 involve 加 -ment。"},{"word":"involved","ipa":"/ɪnˈvɒlvd/","tag":"same verb, adjective","definition":"taking part in something, connected with it, or complicated. The past participle became an adjective with both a social and a structural sense.","definitionCN":"参与其中、与之有关，或复杂的。过去分词变成形容词，同时具有社会义与结构义。"},{"word":"evolve","ipa":"/ɪˈvɒlv/","tag":"same root, different prefix","definition":"to develop gradually. It uses e- 'out' + volvere 'roll', literally 'roll out', the opposite direction from involve.","definitionCN":"逐渐发展。它由 e-“向外”加 volvere“卷”构成，字面是“卷出来”，方向与 involve 相反。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"include","ipa":"/ɪnˈkluːd/","tag":"have as a part","definition":"to have something as part of a whole. It is the plain word for membership, without the sense of entanglement or consequence.","definitionCN":"把某物作为整体的一部分。它是最朴素的“包含”词，没有牵连或后果的意味。"},{"word":"entail","ipa":"/ɪnˈteɪl/","tag":"make necessary","definition":"to involve something as a necessary consequence. It is close to involve in the 'require' sense but more formal and more strictly causal.","definitionCN":"作为必然结果而牵涉某物。它在“需要”义上与 involve 接近，但更正式、因果性更强。"},{"word":"engage","ipa":"/ɪnˈɡeɪdʒ/","tag":"draw into activity","definition":"to attract someone into taking part. It stresses the act of drawing a person in, not the state of being wrapped into a whole.","definitionCN":"吸引某人参与。它强调把人拉进来的动作，而不是被包进整体的状态。"},{"word":"implicate","ipa":"/ˈɪmplɪkeɪt/","tag":"show to be involved","definition":"to show that someone is connected with a crime or wrongdoing. It is the specific legal and moral sense of involve.","definitionCN":"表明某人与犯罪或不当行为有关。它是 involve 在法律与道德上的特定义项。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: in- 'in' and volvere 'roll', plus the ordinary family involvement, involved, evolve and the technical involute.","cn":"只用真实构件：in-“进入”与 volvere“卷”，以及常用词族 involvement、involved、evolve 和技术词 involute。"},"normal":[{"en":"In- = in, volvere = roll. Involve is 'roll in': wrap something into a cover. Everything inside the roll is included.","cn":"in- = 进入，volvere = 卷。involve 就是“卷进去”：把某物包进覆盖物。卷在里面的一切都被包含。"},{"en":"Evolve is the opposite direction: e- 'out' + volvere 'roll' = roll out. Involve rolls in; evolve rolls out.","cn":"evolve 是相反方向：e-“向外”加 volvere“卷”= 卷出来。involve 往里卷；evolve 往外卷。"},{"en":"The word moves easily from cloth to work to people: a task involves hours, a plan involves staff, a case involves suspects.","cn":"这个词很容易从布转到工作再转到人：任务 involves 时间，计划 involves 人员，案件 involves 嫌疑人。"},{"en":"Be involved in is neutral or positive (participation); be involved in a crime is negative (implication). The preposition does not decide the tone; the noun does.","cn":"be involved in 可以是中性或积极（参与）；be involved in a crime 则是负面（牵连）。决定语气的是名词，不是介词。"},{"en":"Fixed patterns: be involved in, involve somebody in, and what does it involve?","cn":"固定搭配：be involved in（参与；卷入）、involve somebody in（让某人参与）、what does it involve?（这需要做些什么？）。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Involvement is always a partial loss of boundary: to be wrapped into something is to have some of your edges become its edges.","cn":"involvement 总是边界的部分丧失：被卷进某事，就是让你的某些边缘变成它的边缘。"},{"en":"The same roll can be protection or trap. A cause can wrap you in purpose; a scandal can wrap you in blame.","cn":"同一个卷裹既可以是保护，也可以是陷阱。一个事业可以把你裹进意义里；一桩丑闻可以把你裹进罪责里。"},{"en":"A complicated plot is called involved because complexity is many folds: the more times the story is rolled, the harder it is to see the surface.","cn":"复杂的情节叫 involved，因为复杂就是许多褶皱：故事被卷的次数越多，越难看到表面。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The project involves close cooperation between three departments.","cn":"这个项目需要三个部门密切合作。"},{"en":"She was involved in the accident but was not hurt.","cn":"她卷入了那场事故，但没有受伤。"},{"en":"The explanation was so involved that nobody could follow it.","cn":"这个解释太复杂，没人能跟上。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“因·沃尔夫”——因（为）沃尔夫（把）东西一层层卷进包里 → involve 包含、使卷入","word":"involve"},"root":"源自拉丁语 involvere“包住、卷进去”，由 in-“进入”加 volvere“卷”构成，核心是“把某物卷进覆盖物里，使它成为整体的一部分”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of involve, all built on one physical act: rolling something into a cover. What is rolled in is included, required, affected, implicated or emotionally enclosed, and many folds make the result complicated.","cn":"involve 的九个义项都建立在一个物理动作上：把某物卷进覆盖物。被卷进去的，就被包含、被需要、被影响、被牵连或在情感上被围住；褶皱多了，结果就变得复杂。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a cloth rolled around an object, so that the object is inside its folds.","cn":"核心意象：一块布绕着某物卷起来，使该物落在它的褶皱里。"},"chain":["ROLL IN","ENCLOSE","INCLUDE","REQUIRE","CONCERN SOMEONE","GET ENTANGLED"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S6","en":"INCLUSION AND REQUIREMENT: whatever is rolled into a task is part of it and must be done.","cn":"包含与需要：凡是被卷进任务的，就是任务的一部分，必须被完成。"},{"senses":"S2 · S3","en":"PARTICIPATION AND CONCERN: a person can be brought inside an activity, or caught inside its area of effect.","cn":"参与与关系：一个人可以被带进活动内部，也可以被它影响的范围卷住。"},{"senses":"S4 · S5","en":"ENTANGLEMENT: implication in wrongdoing and emotional commitment both wrap a person into something larger than themselves.","cn":"卷入：罪责上的牵连与情感上的投入，都把一个人裹进比他自身更大的东西里。"},{"senses":"S7","en":"THE LITERAL ROLL: fog or cloth physically wraps and hides what is inside.","cn":"字面的卷：雾或布在物理上包住并遮住里面的东西。"},{"senses":"S8 · S9","en":"FOLDED MEANING: a logical consequence is already folded into its premise, and many folds make a description involved or complicated.","cn":"折叠的意义：逻辑结论早已被折进前提里；褶皱太多，描述就变得复杂难懂。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Involve is a Latin verb borrowed into English: in- + volv- + -e. Its family uses -ment, participial -ed, and the technical suffixes -ute and -ution.","cn":"involve 是借入英语的拉丁动词：in- + volv- + -e。它的词族使用 -ment、分词 -ed，以及技术性后缀 -ute 和 -ution。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin set is volvere 'roll', involvere 'roll in, envelop', involutus 'wrapped, intricate', and involutio 'a rolling'. The volv- root also gives revolve and evolve.","cn":"拉丁词族是 volvere“卷”、involvere“卷进去、包住”、involutus“被包裹的、错综的”、involutio“卷绕”。volv- 词根也给出 revolve 与 evolve。"},"items":[{"word":"involve","structure":"in- (in) + volv- (roll) + -e","meaning":"to roll in; to include, require or implicate","meaningCN":"包含；需要；使卷入（字面“卷进去”）","example":"The role involves speaking to clients.","exampleCN":"这个职位需要与客户交谈。"},{"word":"involves","structure":"involve + -s (third person singular)","meaning":"includes or requires","meaningCN":"包含；需要（第三人称单数）","example":"The job involves long hours.","exampleCN":"这份工作时间很长。"},{"word":"involved","structure":"involve + -ed (past participle/adjective)","meaning":"taking part; implicated; complicated","meaningCN":"参与的；受牵连的；复杂的","example":"The involved parties met to talk.","exampleCN":"相关各方会面商谈。"},{"word":"involving","structure":"involve + -ing (participle)","meaning":"including or requiring","meaningCN":"包含；需要（现在分词）","example":"It was a difficult task involving many steps.","exampleCN":"这是一项包含许多步骤的艰难任务。"},{"word":"involvement","structure":"involve + -ment (noun of state)","meaning":"participation, connection or commitment","meaningCN":"参与；牵连；投入（-ment 构成状态名词）","example":"Parental involvement helps children learn.","exampleCN":"父母的参与有助于孩子学习。"},{"word":"uninvolved","structure":"un- (not) + involved","meaning":"not taking part; not implicated","meaningCN":"未参与的；未受牵连的（un- 表否定）","example":"He remained uninvolved in the dispute.","exampleCN":"他始终没有卷入这场争端。"},{"word":"involute","structure":"Latin involutus (rolled up)","meaning":"curled inward; intricately folded","meaningCN":"内卷的；错综复杂的（同词根形容词）","example":"The shell has an involute shape.","exampleCN":"这种贝壳呈内卷形。"},{"word":"involution","structure":"Latin involutio (a rolling)","meaning":"a rolling inward; complexity; regression","meaningCN":"内卷；回旋；退化（同词根名词）","example":"Biologists study involution in cells.","exampleCN":"生物学家研究细胞的内卷现象。"},{"word":"revolve","structure":"re- (again/back) + volvere (roll)","meaning":"to turn around a centre","meaningCN":"旋转；环绕（同根，不同前缀）","example":"The Earth revolves around the Sun.","exampleCN":"地球绕太阳旋转。"},{"word":"evolve","structure":"e- (out) + volvere (roll)","meaning":"to develop gradually, literally 'roll out'","meaningCN":"逐渐发展；进化（字面“卷出来”，与 involve 方向相反）","example":"Species evolve over long periods.","exampleCN":"物种在漫长的时间里进化。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"volvere","structure":"PIE *wel- 'turn'","meaning":"to roll, turn, wind","meaningCN":"卷；转；缠绕"},{"word":"involvere","structure":"in- + volvere","meaning":"to roll in, envelop, surround","meaningCN":"卷进去；包住；围住"},{"word":"involutus","structure":"past participle of involvere","meaning":"wrapped, rolled up, intricate","meaningCN":"被包裹的；卷起的；错综的"},{"word":"involutio","structure":"involvere + -tio","meaning":"a rolling in, convolution","meaningCN":"卷绕；回旋"}]}},{"word":"isolate","ipa_uk":"/ˈaɪsəleɪt/","ipa_us":"/ˈaɪsəleɪt/","definition_zh":"隔离；孤立；使分离；分离出","definition_en":"to set something apart from others; to keep a person or thing separate; to separate a substance or factor for study","core_image":"一座小岛被海水从四周隔开，四面都是水，只有岛自己","scene":"化验室里，研究员从一份混合样本中培养出一株单独的细菌。她指着培养皿说：We managed to isolate the bacterium.","sceneCN":"这里 isolate 是「分离出、单独提取」（第 4 个义项：从混合物中分离出某物）；句意：我们成功分离出了这种细菌。图中可辨识物件：培养皿、接种环、显微镜、样本管。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"隔离；孤立；使分离"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"分离出；单独提取"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"isolate from","zh":"与……隔离；从……中分离"},{"phrase":"isolate a virus","zh":"分离出病毒"},{"phrase":"isolate a variable","zh":"分离出一个变量"},{"phrase":"isolate oneself","zh":"自我孤立"},{"phrase":"be isolated from","zh":"与……隔绝"},{"phrase":"self-isolate","zh":"自我隔离"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"isolates"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"isolated"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"isolated"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"isolating"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"isolated","pos":"adj.","zh":"孤立的；偏僻的；单独的"},{"word":"isolation","pos":"n.","zh":"隔离；孤立；分离"},{"word":"isolationism","pos":"n.","zh":"孤立主义"},{"word":"isolator","pos":"n.","zh":"隔离器；绝缘体"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Put apart from everything else","titleCN":"被放到一边：使隔离、使孤立","definition":"to place a person or thing apart from others so that it is alone","definitionCN":"把一个人或物放到别处，使其独自一处","example":"The village was isolated by the flood.","exampleCN":"洪水把村庄与外界隔绝了。","why":"Isolate comes from Latin insula 'island'. To isolate is to make something an island: surround it with distance so that nothing else reaches it.","whyCN":"isolate 来自拉丁语 insula“岛”。使某物 isolate，就是把它变成一座岛：用距离把它围住，使别的东西够不到它。"},{"no":"02","title":"Kept apart to stop spread","titleCN":"为阻断传播而隔开：隔离","definition":"in medicine, to keep a sick person or infected material away from others","definitionCN":"医学中，把病人或受感染材料与他人隔开","example":"Patients with the virus were isolated in a separate ward.","exampleCN":"感染该病毒的患者被隔离在单独病房。","why":"An island is protected by water on every side. In medicine the water becomes walls and distance, and isolation keeps the infection from crossing.","whyCN":"岛被四周的水保护着。在医学中，水变成墙壁与距离，隔离阻止感染越过边界。"},{"no":"03","title":"Cut off socially","titleCN":"社会意义上的隔绝：孤立","definition":"to keep a person or group apart from social contact, often causing loneliness","definitionCN":"使人或群体脱离社会接触，常导致孤独","example":"The illness left him isolated from his friends.","exampleCN":"这场病使他与朋友们隔绝了。","why":"Social life is a mainland of connections. A person who is isolated has become an island: physically present but unreachable.","whyCN":"社交生活是一片充满联系的大陆。一个被 isolate 的人变成了一座岛：人还在，却无法抵达。"},{"no":"04","title":"Separating a substance in the lab","titleCN":"实验室里分离物质：分离出","definition":"in science, to separate a substance, organism or cell from a mixture so that it can be studied alone","definitionCN":"科学中，把某种物质、生物或细胞从混合物中分离出来，以便单独研究","example":"The team isolated the gene responsible for the disease.","exampleCN":"团队分离出了导致该疾病的基因。","why":"A mixture is a mainland of many things. To isolate one component is to make it an island, alone and therefore visible.","whyCN":"混合物是包含许多东西的大陆。分离出其中一个组分，就是把它变成一座岛，独自存在，因而清晰可见。"},{"no":"05","title":"Isolating a variable","titleCN":"分离变量：控制其他因素","definition":"in research, to separate one factor from others so that its effect can be measured","definitionCN":"研究中把一个因素与其他因素分开，以便测量它的作用","example":"The experiment isolates temperature as the only changing factor.","exampleCN":"这个实验把温度分离为唯一变化的因素。","why":"To see one cause clearly, you must remove the others. Isolating a variable is making that factor an island with no bridges to other causes.","whyCN":"要看清一个原因，必须移除其他原因。分离变量，就是让那个因素成为一座没有桥连向其他原因的岛。"},{"no":"06","title":"Withdrawing into oneself","titleCN":"把自己关起来：自我孤立","definition":"to keep oneself apart from other people, often deliberately","definitionCN":"使自己与他人保持距离，常常是刻意为之","example":"After the loss, she isolated herself for weeks.","exampleCN":"失去亲人后，她把自己封闭了好几周。","why":"Here the person is both the island and the one who builds the water around it. Self-isolation is an act, not only a condition.","whyCN":"这里的人既是岛，也是那个在岛周围造水的人。自我孤立是一个动作，而不只是一种状态。"},{"no":"07","title":"Chemical separation","titleCN":"化学上的分离：提纯","definition":"in chemistry, to obtain a pure substance by separating it from other substances","definitionCN":"化学中，通过把它与其他物质分开而获得纯净物","example":"The acid was isolated from the solution by filtration.","exampleCN":"通过过滤从溶液中分离出了这种酸。","why":"Chemistry needs one substance without neighbours. The island image is practical here: no other molecules may remain on the same ground.","whyCN":"化学需要一种没有邻居的物质。这里的岛意象很实用：同一块地面上不能留下别的分子。"},{"no":"08","title":"Separating a problem from the rest","titleCN":"把问题单独拎出来：定位、分离","definition":"to identify a problem or effect separately from others so that it can be dealt with","definitionCN":"把一个问题或效应与其他问题分开识别，以便处理","example":"Technicians isolated the fault to a single cable.","exampleCN":"技术人员把故障定位到一根电缆上。","why":"A system is a mainland of interacting parts. 'Isolating the fault' means cutting away everything that is working until only the broken island remains.","whyCN":"系统是一片由相互作用部件构成的大陆。“隔离故障”就是把一切正常的部分切掉，直到只剩那座坏掉的岛。"},{"no":"09","title":"The adjective: cut off and alone","titleCN":"isolated：被隔开的、孤独的","definition":"of a place, person or thing, separated from others and therefore remote or lonely","definitionCN":"（地点、人或物）与别处隔开，因而偏远或孤独","example":"They live in an isolated farmhouse miles from the road.","exampleCN":"他们住在一座离公路数英里远的孤立农舍里。","why":"The past participle became an adjective: a thing that has been made an island simply is isolated. The word describes the result of the act.","whyCN":"过去分词变成了形容词：一个已经被变成岛的东西，就是 isolated。这个词描述的是动作的结果。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Isolate is a back-formation from isolated, which came into English from French isolé, from Italian isolato, from Latin insulatus 'made into an island', from insula 'island'. The word's whole history is the image of an island.","cn":"isolate 是由 isolated 逆构而来的；isolated 经法语 isolé、意大利语 isolato，上溯到拉丁语 insulatus“被造成一座岛”，而 insula 意为“岛”。这个词的整个历史就是一座岛的意象。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN insula","en":"Insula meant 'island' and also 'a block of buildings' in a city. English isle, island, insular and peninsula all trace back to it or to its family.","cn":"insula 意为“岛”，也指城市中的“一个街区”。英语 isle、island、insular、peninsula 都可追溯到它或其词族。"},{"era":"LATIN insulatus","en":"Insulatus meant 'made into an island'. The suffix -atus marks the result of an action: something has been turned into an island.","cn":"insulatus 意为“被造成一座岛的”。后缀 -atus 标记动作的结果：某物已经被变成岛。"},{"era":"ITALIAN isolato","en":"Italian isolato meant 'isolated, detached', literally 'islanded'. Italian turned the Latin idea into an everyday adjective for things standing alone.","cn":"意大利语 isolato 意为“孤立的、分离的”，字面是“被岛化的”。意大利语把拉丁观念变成日常形容词，用于独自立着的东西。"},{"era":"FRENCH isolé","en":"French isolé (17c.) carried the word into French. English at first borrowed the French adjective as isole or isolated in the 18th century.","cn":"法语 isolé（17 世纪）把这个词带入法语。英语在 18 世纪先借入法语形容词，写作 isole 或 isolated。"},{"era":"ENGLISH isolated, 1740","en":"English isolated is recorded from 1740, meaning 'standing detached from others of its kind'. The adjective arrived before the verb.","cn":"英语 isolated 记录于 1740 年，意为“与其同类分离而独处的”。形容词先于动词出现。"},{"era":"ENGLISH isolate, 1786","en":"The verb isolate is a back-formation from isolated, recorded by 1786. A critic in 1799 called it an unnecessary French import, which shows how new it still felt.","cn":"动词 isolate 是由 isolated 逆构的，记录于 1786 年。1799 年有一位批评家称它是多余的法国借词，可见当时人们还觉得它很新。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group shares the insula 'island' root or the isolate family; the near-meaning group contains verbs of separation, each with a different reason and degree.","cn":"形近组共享 insula“岛”词根或 isolate 词族；近义组是分离类动词，原因与程度各不相同。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"isolated","ipa":"/ˈaɪsəleɪtɪd/","tag":"same verb, adjective","definition":"separated from others; remote or lonely. The past participle became the adjective, and the verb was back-formed from it.","definitionCN":"与别处隔离的；偏远或孤独的。过去分词成为形容词，动词又由它逆构而来。"},{"word":"isolation","ipa":"/ˌaɪsəˈleɪʃn/","tag":"same verb, noun","definition":"the state or act of being set apart. It is the -ion noun and covers medical, social and scientific separation.","definitionCN":"被隔开的状态或行为。它是 -ion 名词，覆盖医学、社会与科学上的分离。"},{"word":"insular","ipa":"/ˈɪnsjʊlə/","tag":"same root, adjective","definition":"relating to an island; narrow-minded or cut off from outside influence. It comes directly from Latin insula, without the French route.","definitionCN":"与岛有关的；狭隘的、与外界隔绝的。它直接来自拉丁语 insula，没有经过法语。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"separate","ipa":"/ˈsepəreɪt/","tag":"divide","definition":"to divide or move things apart. It is the general word and does not imply distance or loneliness.","definitionCN":"把东西分开或移开。它是最一般的词，不暗示距离或孤独。"},{"word":"segregate","ipa":"/ˈseɡrɪɡeɪt/","tag":"keep groups apart","definition":"to keep different groups or races apart, often by policy. It adds a social or institutional rule to separation.","definitionCN":"把不同群体或种族分开，常通过政策。它在“分离”之上加了社会或制度规则。"},{"word":"detach","ipa":"/dɪˈtætʃ/","tag":"unfasten","definition":"to remove something from what it is attached to. It focuses on the physical connection being cut, not on the resulting island.","definitionCN":"把某物从它所附着的东西上取下。它关注被切断的物理连接，而不是最终形成的岛。"},{"word":"quarantine","ipa":"/ˈkwærəntiːn/","tag":"medical separation","definition":"to keep people or animals apart for a period to prevent disease spread. It is the public-health procedure that uses isolation.","definitionCN":"把人或动物隔开一段时间以防疾病传播。它是使用隔离手段的公共卫生程序。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: Latin insula 'island', insulatus 'made into an island', and the ordinary English family isolated, isolation, isolationism, isolator.","cn":"只用真实构件：拉丁语 insula“岛”、insulatus“被造成岛”，以及常用英语词族 isolated、isolation、isolationism、isolator。"},"normal":[{"en":"Insula = island. To isolate is to make an island: put water on every side so that nothing else can reach.","cn":"insula = 岛。isolate 就是造一座岛：在四周放满水，使别的东西都够不到。"},{"en":"The adjective isolated came first (1740), and the verb isolate was cut back from it in 1786. The island existed before the act of islanding.","cn":"形容词 isolated 先出现（1740 年），动词 isolate 于 1786 年由它逆构。岛先于“造岛”的动作存在。"},{"en":"Insular is the same root without the French detour: insular means 'of an island', and figuratively 'narrow, cut off'.","cn":"insular 是同一词根，但没有绕经法语：insular 意为“岛的”，引申为“狭隘的、与世隔绝的”。"},{"en":"The same word covers a sick ward, a lonely person, a pure chemical and a single variable: in each case, one thing alone with no neighbours.","cn":"同一个词覆盖病房、孤独的人、纯净化学品和单个变量：每一种情况都是一样东西独自待着，没有邻居。"},{"en":"Fixed patterns: isolate from, isolate a virus, isolate a variable, and self-isolate.","cn":"固定搭配：isolate from（与……隔离；从……中分离）、isolate a virus（分离病毒）、isolate a variable（分离变量）、self-isolate（自我隔离）。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Isolation is defined by what is removed, not by what remains. The island is the shape left after the mainland is taken away.","cn":"隔离由被移除的东西定义，而不是由留下的东西定义。岛是大陆被拿走之后剩下的形状。"},{"en":"The same separation can heal or harm: a quarantined patient is protected from others, and an isolated person is deprived of them.","cn":"同一种分离既能疗愈也能伤害：被隔离的病人受到保护，而被孤立的人则被剥夺了他人。"},{"en":"Science needs islands: to understand one cause, you must cut it away from all the others and see what it does alone.","cn":"科学需要岛：要理解一个原因，必须把它从所有其他原因中切出来，看它独自做什么。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The island is isolated from the mainland for most of the winter.","cn":"这座岛在冬季的大部分时间里与大陆隔绝。"},{"en":"Scientists isolated the compound from the plant's roots.","cn":"科学家从这种植物的根中分离出了该化合物。"},{"en":"He felt isolated after moving to a new city.","cn":"搬到新城市后，他感到孤立。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“爱·搜·累特”——爱（把）搜（到的）累特（别东西）单独放到一座小岛上 → isolate 隔离、孤立","word":"isolate"},"root":"源自拉丁语 insula“岛”，经 insulatus“被造成一座岛”、意大利语 isolato、法语 isolé 进入英语，核心是“用距离把某物围成一座孤岛”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of isolate, all one image: an island. A village, a patient, a lonely person, a gene, a variable, a chemical, a fault and the adjective isolated are each a piece of land with water on every side.","cn":"isolate 的九个义项都是同一个意象：一座岛。村庄、病人、孤独的人、基因、变量、化学品、故障，以及形容词 isolated，都是四面环水的一块陆地。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a small island with water on every side, reachable by nothing.","cn":"核心意象：一座四面环水、什么都够不到的小岛。"},"chain":["ONE THING","CUT CONNECTIONS","SURROUND WITH DISTANCE","BECOME AN ISLAND","ALONE AND SEPARATE","STUDY OR PROTECT IT"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S3","en":"GEOGRAPHICAL AND SOCIAL ISLAND: a place cut off by distance, and a person cut off from contact.","cn":"地理与社会的岛：被距离隔开的地方，以及被切断联系的人。"},{"senses":"S2 · S6","en":"PROTECTIVE OR DELIBERATE SEPARATION: medical isolation keeps infection away, and self-isolation is chosen withdrawal.","cn":"保护性或刻意性的分离：医学隔离阻断感染，自我隔离则是主动退开。"},{"senses":"S4 · S7","en":"SUBSTANCE ON ITS OWN: a gene, organism or chemical separated from its mixture and made pure.","cn":"独自存在的物质：从混合物中分离出来并变得纯净的基因、生物或化学品。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"CONTROLLED EXPERIMENT: one variable made an island so that its effect can be seen without interference.","cn":"受控实验：把一个变量变成岛，以便在没有干扰的情况下看清它的作用。"},{"senses":"S8 · S9","en":"DIAGNOSIS AND RESULT: a fault identified apart from the working system, and the adjective describing what has been made an island.","cn":"诊断与结果：从正常系统中单独识别出的故障，以及描述“已被变成岛”的形容词。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Isolate is an English back-formation from isolated, which came through French and Italian from Latin insulatus. English builds its family with -ed, -ion, -ism and -or.","cn":"isolate 是由 isolated 逆构的英语词，而 isolated 经法语、意大利语来自拉丁语 insulatus。英语用 -ed、-ion、-ism、-or 构成词族。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin set is insula 'island', insulatus 'made into an island', and insulanus 'islander'. The Italian and French forms isolato and isolé are the bridge to English.","cn":"拉丁词族是 insula“岛”、insulatus“被造成岛”、insulanus“岛民”。意大利语 isolato 与法语 isolé 是通向英语的桥。"},"items":[{"word":"isolate","structure":"back-formed from isolated; Latin insula (island)","meaning":"to set apart; to separate for study","meaningCN":"隔离；孤立；分离出","example":"Doctors isolated the patient at once.","exampleCN":"医生立即隔离了病人。"},{"word":"isolates","structure":"isolate + -s (third person singular)","meaning":"sets apart","meaningCN":"隔离（第三人称单数）","example":"The device isolates the faulty circuit.","exampleCN":"这个装置隔离了故障电路。"},{"word":"isolated","structure":"isolate + -ed (past participle/adjective)","meaning":"set apart; remote; lonely","meaningCN":"被隔离的；偏僻的；孤独的","example":"The house stands in an isolated valley.","exampleCN":"这座房子位于一个偏僻的山谷里。"},{"word":"isolating","structure":"isolate + -ing (participle)","meaning":"currently setting apart","meaningCN":"正在隔离（现在分词）","example":"They are isolating the affected area.","exampleCN":"他们正在隔离受影响区域。"},{"word":"isolation","structure":"isolate + -ion (noun of action)","meaning":"the act or state of being set apart","meaningCN":"隔离；孤立（-ion 构成动作或状态名词）","example":"Isolation slowed the spread of the disease.","exampleCN":"隔离减缓了疾病的传播。"},{"word":"isolationism","structure":"isolation + -ism (policy)","meaning":"a policy of keeping one's country apart from others","meaningCN":"孤立主义（-ism 表主义、政策）","example":"The country turned to isolationism after the war.","exampleCN":"战后该国转向孤立主义。"},{"word":"isolationist","structure":"isolation + -ist (person or adjective)","meaning":"favoring isolationism","meaningCN":"孤立主义的；孤立主义者","example":"Isolationist voices grew louder.","exampleCN":"孤立主义的声音越来越大。"},{"word":"isolator","structure":"isolate + -or (device or agent)","meaning":"a device that separates or insulates","meaningCN":"隔离器；绝缘体（-or 表装置或施动者）","example":"The isolator protects the circuit from surges.","exampleCN":"隔离器保护电路免受浪涌。"},{"word":"self-isolate","structure":"self- + isolate (compound verb)","meaning":"to keep oneself apart voluntarily","meaningCN":"自我隔离（self- 表自我）","example":"Travellers were asked to self-isolate.","exampleCN":"旅客被要求自我隔离。"},{"word":"insular","structure":"Latin insula + -ar (adjective)","meaning":"of an island; narrow and cut off","meaningCN":"岛屿的；狭隘隔绝的（同根形容词）","example":"The community remained insular for decades.","exampleCN":"这个社区几十年来一直与外界隔绝。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"insula","structure":"Latin noun","meaning":"island; a block of buildings","meaningCN":"岛；城市街区"},{"word":"insulatus","structure":"insula + -atus","meaning":"made into an island, isolated","meaningCN":"被造成一座岛的；孤立的"},{"word":"insulanus","structure":"insula + -anus","meaning":"islander, of an island","meaningCN":"岛民；岛上的"}]}},{"word":"issue","ipa_uk":"/ˈɪʃuː/","ipa_us":"/ˈɪʃuː/","definition_zh":"问题；议题；期号；发行；发布；结果","definition_en":"an important topic or problem; one edition of a publication; the act of officially releasing something; a result or outcome","core_image":"水从一道出口涌出去，越过门槛，流向外面","scene":"报社印刷车间，一摞刚印好的报纸从传送带上下来。编辑看着头版说：The new issue comes out tomorrow.","sceneCN":"这里 issue 是「（报刊的）一期、期号」（第 2 个义项：出版物的一期）；句意：新一期明天出版。图中可辨识物件：印刷机、传送带、报纸、头版。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"问题；议题；期号；发行物"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"发布；发行；发放"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"the issue of","zh":"……的问题"},{"phrase":"a key issue","zh":"关键问题"},{"phrase":"issue a statement","zh":"发表声明"},{"phrase":"the latest issue","zh":"最新一期"},{"phrase":"take issue with","zh":"对……提出异议"},{"phrase":"at issue","zh":"正在讨论的；争议中的"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（多于一个）","form":"issues"},{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"issues"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"issued"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"issued"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"issuing"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"issuance","pos":"n.","zh":"发行；发放"},{"word":"issuer","pos":"n.","zh":"发行者；发行人"},{"word":"reissue","pos":"v./n.","zh":"重新发行；再版"},{"word":"issueless","pos":"adj.","zh":"无子女的；无结果的（较罕见）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"The question that needs deciding","titleCN":"需要被决定的问题：议题","definition":"an important topic or problem that people discuss, debate or need to solve","definitionCN":"人们讨论、辩论或需要解决的重要话题或问题","example":"Climate change is the central issue of our time.","exampleCN":"气候变化是我们这个时代的核心议题。","why":"Issue began as 'an exit' and then 'an outcome'. A disputed matter is something that must 'come out' one way or another, so it becomes the issue to be decided.","whyCN":"issue 最初是“出口”，后来是“结果”。一个有争议的事情必须“出来”一个结果，于是它就成了待决的 issue。"},{"no":"02","title":"One edition of a publication","titleCN":"出版物的一期：期号","definition":"one number or edition of a magazine, newspaper or journal, published at a particular time","definitionCN":"杂志、报纸或期刊在某一时间出版的一期","example":"Her article appeared in the March issue.","exampleCN":"她的文章发表在三月那一期。","why":"Publishing is a flow: each edition 'goes out' to readers on a date. The edition is the unit that issues forth, so the word names one release.","whyCN":"出版是一条流：每一期都在某一天“发出去”到读者手里。这一期就是被发出的单位，所以这个词命名一次发行。"},{"no":"03","title":"Officially sending something out","titleCN":"正式发出：发布、发放","definition":"to officially give, supply or release something such as documents, money or a statement","definitionCN":"正式给予、提供或发布文件、资金或声明等","example":"The government issued new passports to the refugees.","exampleCN":"政府向难民发放了新护照。","why":"The verb keeps the oldest spatial sense: something is made to go out from an authority to recipients. The exit is now official.","whyCN":"动词保留了最古老的空间义：某物被从权威那里发出去，送到接受者手中。出口此时变成了官方程序。"},{"no":"04","title":"Flowing out from a source","titleCN":"从源头涌出：冒出、流出","definition":"of a liquid, gas or sound, to come or flow out from a place","definitionCN":"（液体、气体或声音）从某处出来或流出","example":"Smoke issued from the chimney all morning.","exampleCN":"整个上午烟都从烟囱里冒出来。","why":"This is the literal picture: exire is 'to go out', and issue is the going-out itself. Water, smoke or blood leaves a container through its opening.","whyCN":"这是字面画面：exire 就是“出去”，而 issue 就是“出去”这件事本身。水、烟或血通过开口离开容器。"},{"no":"05","title":"How it turns out","titleCN":"事情的结果：结局、结果","definition":"the result or outcome of an action, event or process, especially in formal writing","definitionCN":"行动、事件或过程的结果，尤用于正式写作","example":"The issue of the negotiations remains uncertain.","exampleCN":"谈判的结果仍不确定。","why":"Old French issue meant 'a going out, exit; final event'. An event's exit is how it leaves the stage, which is its outcome.","whyCN":"古法语 issue 意为“出去、出口；最终事件”。一个事件的“出口”就是它离开舞台的方式，也就是它的结果。"},{"no":"06","title":"Children as the family's outcome","titleCN":"后代：子嗣（法律、旧用法）","definition":"in law and older usage, offspring or descendants, especially in the phrase die without issue","definitionCN":"法律和旧用法中指子女或后代，尤见于 die without issue（死时无子嗣）","example":"He died without issue, so the estate passed to his nephew.","exampleCN":"他死时没有子嗣，遗产便传给了侄子。","why":"A family line 'goes out' into the future through children. The biological sense treats offspring as what proceeds or issues from a person.","whyCN":"家族的血脉通过子女“走向”未来。生物义把后代看作从一个人身上流出的东西。"},{"no":"07","title":"Taking issue: disagreeing","titleCN":"提出异议：take issue with","definition":"in the phrase take issue with, to disagree with someone or challenge a statement","definitionCN":"在短语 take issue with 中，表示不同意某人或质疑某种说法","example":"I take issue with the claim that the cost was unavoidable.","exampleCN":"我对“这笔成本不可避免”的说法有异议。","why":"A dispute is a point that must come out. To take issue is to seize that point and make it the matter to be decided, rather than letting it pass.","whyCN":"争议是一个必须“出来”的点。take issue 就是抓住这个点，让它成为待决之事，而不是让它溜过去。"},{"no":"08","title":"The point under dispute","titleCN":"争议中的要点：at issue","definition":"in the phrase at issue, being discussed or disputed at the present moment","definitionCN":"在短语 at issue 中，指当前正在被讨论或争议的事情","example":"The question at issue is whether the contract is valid.","exampleCN":"争议中的问题是这份合同是否有效。","why":"The issue is the point that has come out into the open between the parties. 'At issue' marks that point as the live centre of the argument.","whyCN":"issue 就是已经公开来到双方面前的那个点。“at issue”标记的就是争论当前活跃的中心。"},{"no":"09","title":"A point for trial","titleCN":"法庭上待裁定的争点","definition":"in law, a point of fact or law that the parties dispute and the court must decide","definitionCN":"法律中，双方争议、须由法院裁定的一个事实或法律要点","example":"The court narrowed the issues to two questions of law.","exampleCN":"法院把争点缩小为两个法律问题。","why":"Legal pleading ends with the points that remain disputed; these 'come out' of the pleadings as the issues for trial. The modern legal sense grew from this procedure.","whyCN":"诉状程序最终留下仍有争议的要点；这些要点从诉状中“出来”，成为待审的 issue。现代法律义正是从这一程序发展来的。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Issue comes from Old French issue 'a going out, exit; final event', from the feminine past participle of issir 'to go out', from Latin exire 'to go out, go forth', from ex- 'out' + ire 'to go'. The root is ire 'go', not any prefix meaning 'problem'.","cn":"issue 来自古法语 issue“出去、出口；最终事件”，是 issir“出去”的阴性过去分词，再上溯到拉丁语 exire“出去、向前走”，由 ex-“向外”加 ire“走”构成。它的词根是 ire“走”，而不是任何表示“问题”的前缀。"},"items":[{"era":"PIE *ei-","en":"The root *ei- meant 'to go'. It underlies Latin ire and appears in English words such as itinerant and ambition.","cn":"词根 *ei- 意为“走”。它是拉丁语 ire 的深层来源，也出现在英语 itinerant、ambition 等词中。"},{"era":"LATIN exire","en":"Exire meant 'to go out, go forth; become public; flow, gush, pour forth'. The senses of leaving, becoming known and flowing out were all present.","cn":"exire 意为“出去、向前走；变得公开；流出、涌出”。离开、公开、流出这三种意味从一开始就都有。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH issue","en":"The feminine past participle of issir gave the noun issue, meaning 'a way out, a going out, exit; final event'. English borrowed it c.1300 as 'an exit'.","cn":"issir 的阴性过去分词给出名词 issue，意为“出路、出去、出口；最终事件”。英语约 1300 年借入，最初意为“出口”。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, 14c.","en":"By the late 14th century issue also meant 'offspring, children' and 'outcome, consequence'. Both are things that 'come out' of a person or an event.","cn":"到 14 世纪晚期，issue 也指“后代、子女”和“结果、后果”。两者都是从一个人或一个事件中“出来”的东西。"},{"era":"ENGLISH LEGAL, 14c.–15c.","en":"Legal usage developed from 'the end or result of pleadings', hence 'the controversy over facts in a trial' and then 'a point of contention between two parties'.","cn":"法律用法从“诉状的终点或结果”发展而来，因而指“审判中关于事实的争议”，再指“双方之间的争点”。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, 1833–1990","en":"The publishing sense 'action of sending into publication or circulation' is from 1833. 'To have issues' meaning to have unresolved conflicts is from about 1990.","cn":"出版义“送交出版或发行”来自 1833 年。“to have issues”表示有未解决的心理冲突，来自约 1990 年。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group shares the issue family or a misleading resemblance; the near-meaning group contains words for topics, releases and outcomes, each from a different angle.","cn":"形近组共享 issue 词族或具有误导性的相似外形；近义组是话题、发布与结果类词，角度各不相同。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"issuer","ipa":"/ˈɪʃuːə/","tag":"same word, person","definition":"a person or organization that officially issues something, such as passports or shares. The -er suffix marks the source.","definitionCN":"正式发放某物（如护照或股票）的个人或组织。-er 后缀标记来源方。"},{"word":"issuance","ipa":"/ˈɪʃuːəns/","tag":"same word, formal noun","definition":"the official act of issuing something. It is the formal noun used in law, finance and government.","definitionCN":"正式发放某物的行为。它是法律、金融和政府领域使用的正式名词。"},{"word":"tissue","ipa":"/ˈtɪʃuː/","tag":"look-alike, different word","definition":"the material forming animal or plant cells, or a soft paper. It comes from French tissu 'woven', from Latin texere 'to weave', not from issue.","definitionCN":"构成动植物细胞的物质，或柔软的纸。它来自法语 tissu“编织物”，再上溯到拉丁语 texere“编织”，与 issue 无关。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"matter","ipa":"/ˈmætə/","tag":"subject under consideration","definition":"a subject or situation being considered or dealt with. It is broader and less contentious than issue.","definitionCN":"正在被考虑或处理的主题或情况。它比 issue 更宽泛，争议性更弱。"},{"word":"topic","ipa":"/ˈtɒpɪk/","tag":"subject of talk","definition":"a subject being discussed or written about. It names the content, not the dispute or the need for a decision.","definitionCN":"正在被讨论或写作的主题。它命名内容，而不强调争议或需要决定。"},{"word":"release","ipa":"/rɪˈliːs/","tag":"make available","definition":"to make something available to the public, or the thing made available. It overlaps with issue as a verb but stresses freeing rather than sending out.","definitionCN":"使某物向公众开放，或被开放的东西。它作动词时与 issue 重叠，但强调“释放”而非“发出”。"},{"word":"outcome","ipa":"/ˈaʊtkʌm/","tag":"result","definition":"the way a situation turns out. It is the plain modern word for the 'result' sense of issue.","definitionCN":"事情最终变成的样子。它是 issue 的“结果”义在现代英语中的常用对应词。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: Latin ex- 'out' + ire 'go', the French noun issue, and the ordinary family issuance, issuer, reissue.","cn":"只用真实构件：拉丁语 ex-“向外”加 ire“走”，法语名词 issue，以及常用词族 issuance、issuer、reissue。"},"normal":[{"en":"Ex- = out, ire = go. Issue is literally 'a going out': something leaves its source and becomes visible to others.","cn":"ex- = 向外，ire = 走。issue 字面就是“一次走出去”：某物离开源头，变得对别人可见。"},{"en":"A magazine issue is a batch that goes out on a date; an official issue is a document that goes out from an authority; an outcome is how an event goes out of existence.","cn":"杂志的一期是在某天发出去的一批；官方 issue 是从权威那里发出去的文件；结果是一个事件退出存在的方式。"},{"en":"A public 'issue' is a matter that must come out one way or another. That is why the same word means both 'topic' and 'result'.","cn":"公共的 issue 是一件必须“出来”一个结果的事情。所以同一个词既能表示“议题”，也能表示“结果”。"},{"en":"Do not confuse issue with tissue: issue is from ire 'go'; tissue is from texere 'weave'. They only look alike.","cn":"不要把 issue 和 tissue 混淆：issue 来自 ire“走”；tissue 来自 texere“编织”。它们只是外形相似。"},{"en":"Fixed patterns: the issue of something, issue a statement, take issue with, and at issue.","cn":"固定搭配：the issue of something（……的问题）、issue a statement（发表声明）、take issue with（对……提出异议）、at issue（争议中的）。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Every issue is a fork in a road. It exists because something has not yet gone out, and a decision is needed for it to leave.","cn":"每个 issue 都是路上的一个岔口。它之所以存在，是因为某事尚未“出去”，需要一次决定才能离开。"},{"en":"The same word covers flow, offspring and results because all three are what proceeds from a source into the world.","cn":"同一个词覆盖流动、后代和结果，因为这三者都是从源头进入世界的东西。"},{"en":"A society's issues are its unresolved exits: problems that have not yet found a way out.","cn":"一个社会的 issue 就是它尚未解决的出口：还没有找到出去之路的问题。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Housing is the most urgent issue facing the city.","cn":"住房是该市面临的最紧迫问题。"},{"en":"The magazine's April issue features three young poets.","cn":"这本杂志的四月号重点介绍了三位年轻诗人。"},{"en":"The bank issued a new card to every customer.","cn":"银行为每位客户发行了一张新卡。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“伊·书”——伊（把）书（一本本）发出去，问题也就摆出来 → issue 发行；问题","word":"issue"},"root":"源自拉丁语 exire“出去、向前走”，由 ex-“向外”加 ire“走”构成，核心是“从源头出去”：出口、发行、流出、结果，都是同一个“出去”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of issue, all one movement: something goes out. A topic goes out into public debate, an edition goes out to readers, a document goes out from an authority, smoke goes out of a chimney, and an event goes out into its result.","cn":"issue 的九个义项都是同一个动作：某物出去。议题进入公共讨论，一期杂志送到读者手中，文件从权威机构发出，烟从烟囱冒出，事件走向它的结果。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: water passing through an opening and flowing out beyond the threshold.","cn":"核心意象：水穿过一个开口，越过门槛流到外面。"},"chain":["SOURCE","OPENING","GOING OUT","BECOMING VISIBLE","REACHING OTHERS","OUTCOME"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S7 · S8","en":"THE MATTER THAT MUST COME OUT: a disputed topic, a challenge to a claim, and the point currently under dispute.","cn":"必须“出来”的事情：有争议的议题、对说法的质疑，以及当前争议中的要点。"},{"senses":"S2 · S3","en":"PUBLISHING AND OFFICIAL RELEASE: one edition goes out to readers, and documents or money go out from an authority.","cn":"出版与官方发布：一期出版物送到读者手中，文件或资金从权威机构发出。"},{"senses":"S4 · S6","en":"WHAT FLOWS FROM A SOURCE: smoke from a chimney, and children as a family line's outward continuation.","cn":"从源头流出的东西：烟囱里的烟，以及作为家族血脉向外延续的子女。"},{"senses":"S5","en":"THE EXIT OF AN EVENT: how a process or negotiation finally leaves the stage, which is its result.","cn":"事件的出口：一个过程或谈判最终如何离开舞台，也就是它的结果。"},{"senses":"S9","en":"THE LEGAL POINT: the disputed question that comes out of the pleadings and must be decided by a court.","cn":"法律争点：从诉状中出来、必须由法院裁定的争议问题。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Issue is a borrowed French noun that English also uses as a verb. Its family is built with -ance, -er, and the prefixes re- and self-.","cn":"issue 是借入的法语名词，英语也把它用作动词。它的词族用 -ance、-er，以及前缀 re-、self- 构成。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin set is ire 'go', exire 'go out', exitus 'a going out, exit', and exitium 'destruction'. The root is movement, not dispute.","cn":"拉丁词族是 ire“走”、exire“出去”、exitus“出去、出口”、exitium“毁灭”。词根是运动，不是争论。"},"items":[{"word":"issue","structure":"Latin ex- (out) + ire (go); via French issue","meaning":"a going out; a topic; a release; an outcome","meaningCN":"问题；发行；结果（字面“出去”）","example":"The issue was settled quickly.","exampleCN":"这个问题很快解决了。"},{"word":"issues","structure":"issue + -s (plural or third person)","meaning":"topics, editions, or the act of releasing","meaningCN":"问题（复数）；发布（第三人称单数）","example":"The report raises several issues.","exampleCN":"报告提出了几个问题。"},{"word":"issued","structure":"issue + -ed (past)","meaning":"officially released in the past","meaningCN":"发布了（过去式）","example":"The office issued the permit yesterday.","exampleCN":"办公室昨天签发了许可证。"},{"word":"issuing","structure":"issue + -ing (participle)","meaning":"releasing or flowing out","meaningCN":"发布；流出（现在分词）","example":"The bank is issuing new notes.","exampleCN":"银行正在发行新纸币。"},{"word":"issuance","structure":"issue + -ance (noun of action)","meaning":"the official act of issuing","meaningCN":"发行；发放（正式名词）","example":"The issuance of visas was delayed.","exampleCN":"签证的发放被延迟了。"},{"word":"issuer","structure":"issue + -er (agent)","meaning":"the party that issues something","meaningCN":"发行者；发放机构","example":"The issuer of the bond is a large bank.","exampleCN":"这只债券的发行者是一家大银行。"},{"word":"reissue","structure":"re- (again) + issue","meaning":"to publish or supply again","meaningCN":"重新发行；再版（re- 表再、重新）","example":"The album was reissued on vinyl.","exampleCN":"这张专辑以黑胶形式重新发行。"},{"word":"back issue","structure":"back + issue (compound noun)","meaning":"an earlier edition of a publication","meaningCN":"过刊；旧的一期","example":"She collected back issues of the journal.","exampleCN":"她收集了这份期刊的过刊。"},{"word":"issueless","structure":"issue + -less (without)","meaning":"without offspring; without result","meaningCN":"无子女的；无结果的（-less 表没有，较罕见）","example":"The heir died issueless.","exampleCN":"这位继承人死时没有子嗣。"},{"word":"exit","structure":"Latin exitus, from exire","meaning":"a way out; the act of leaving","meaningCN":"出口；退出（同词根名词）","example":"Take the second exit on the left.","exampleCN":"走左边第二个出口。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"ire","structure":"PIE *ei- 'go'","meaning":"to go","meaningCN":"走；去"},{"word":"exire","structure":"ex- + ire","meaning":"to go out, go forth, flow out","meaningCN":"出去；向前走；流出"},{"word":"exitus","structure":"exire + -tus","meaning":"a going out, exit, outcome","meaningCN":"出去；出口；结果"}]}},{"word":"item","ipa_uk":"/ˈaɪtəm/","ipa_us":"/ˈaɪtəm/","definition_zh":"项目；物品；条款；一则（新闻）；条目","definition_en":"a single object, entry or piece of information in a list, set or report","core_image":"清单上一行一行写着的条目，每一条独立占据一行，彼此分开","scene":"超市收银台，收银员把购物车里的东西一件件放到扫描台上，屏幕上的清单逐行增加。她说：Every item is scanned.","sceneCN":"这里 item 是「清单上的一件物品、一个条目」（第 1、4 个义项：单件物品、清单条目）；句意：每一件商品都要扫描。图中可辨识物件：扫描台、购物车、收银屏幕、商品。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"物品；项目；条目；条款"},{"tag":"n.","zh":"一则（新闻、消息）"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"a single item","zh":"单件物品"},{"phrase":"item on the agenda","zh":"议程上的项目"},{"phrase":"news item","zh":"一则新闻"},{"phrase":"line item","zh":"（账目中的）行列项"},{"phrase":"item by item","zh":"逐项地"},{"phrase":"an item of clothing","zh":"一件衣物"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（多于一个）","form":"items"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"itemize","pos":"v.","zh":"逐项列出；分项列记"},{"word":"itemized","pos":"adj.","zh":"逐项列出的；分项的"},{"word":"itemization","pos":"n.","zh":"逐项列记；分项"},{"word":"subitem","pos":"n.","zh":"子项；分项"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"One thing in a list","titleCN":"清单上的一件：条目、项目","definition":"a single thing in a list, set or collection, treated as a separate unit","definitionCN":"清单、集合或收藏中被当作独立单位的一件东西","example":"Please check each item on the list.","exampleCN":"请核对清单上的每一项。","why":"Latin item was the adverb 'likewise, also', written before each new line of an inventory. The word that introduced each entry became the name for the entry itself.","whyCN":"拉丁语 item 是副词“同样地、还有”，写在清单每一项之前。这个用来引出条目的词，最后变成了条目本身的名称。"},{"no":"02","title":"One piece of news","titleCN":"一则新闻：一条消息","definition":"a single report or piece of information in a newspaper, broadcast or news feed","definitionCN":"报纸、广播或新闻推送中的一则报道或一条信息","example":"The flood was the lead item on the evening news.","exampleCN":"洪水是晚间新闻的头条。","why":"A news programme is a list of separate reports. Each report is one entry in that sequence, so it is an item.","whyCN":"新闻节目是一串分开的报道。每一则报道都是这个序列中的一个条目，所以它叫 item。"},{"no":"03","title":"One point on an agenda","titleCN":"议程上的一项：议题条目","definition":"a single matter to be discussed or decided at a meeting","definitionCN":"会议上要讨论或决定的一件单独事项","example":"The budget is the last item on the agenda.","exampleCN":"预算是议程上的最后一项。","why":"A meeting works through a written list. Each matter is introduced in turn, exactly as Latin item introduced each line, so each becomes an item.","whyCN":"会议按一份书面清单逐项进行。每件事依次被引出，正如拉丁语 item 引出每一行，于是每一件都成为一个 item。"},{"no":"04","title":"One article for sale","titleCN":"待售的一件物品：商品","definition":"a single article or product, especially one among many offered for sale","definitionCN":"单件物品或产品，尤指众多待售商品中的一件","example":"The shop sells hundreds of items, from pins to furniture.","exampleCN":"这家店出售成百上千种商品，从别针到家具。","why":"A shop's stock is an inventory, and an inventory is a list. Each product is one line in that list, hence one item.","whyCN":"商店的存货就是一份清单，而清单就是一张列表。每件产品都是列表中的一行，因此是一个 item。"},{"no":"05","title":"One line in an account","titleCN":"账目上的一行：行项","definition":"in accounting, a single entry or line in a budget, invoice or financial statement","definitionCN":"会计中预算、发票或财务报表里的一笔单独记录或一行","example":"Every line item must be supported by a receipt.","exampleCN":"每个行项都必须有收据支持。","why":"Accounting is the most literal form of listing: money is recorded line by line. 'Line item' makes the original list-entry sense visible.","whyCN":"会计是最字面意义上的列清单：钱被一行一行记录下来。“line item”让最初的“清单条目”义变得可见。"},{"no":"06","title":"One question in a test","titleCN":"试题中的一道：题目","definition":"a single question or task in a test, questionnaire or exercise","definitionCN":"测验、问卷或练习中的一道题或一项任务","example":"Item 12 asks you to choose the best answer.","exampleCN":"第 12 题要求你选出最佳答案。","why":"A test is a numbered list of tasks. Each task is one entry, and standardized testing calls them items because they are countable units.","whyCN":"测验是一份编号的任务清单。每项任务都是一个条目，标准化测试称它们为 item，因为它们是可计数的单位。"},{"no":"07","title":"One entry in a data list","titleCN":"数据列表中的一条：数据项","definition":"in computing, a single element in a list, menu, database or data set","definitionCN":"计算机中列表、菜单、数据库或数据集里的单个元素","example":"Select the item you want from the menu.","exampleCN":"从菜单中选择你想要的那一项。","why":"A computer list is literally a sequence of units. Each unit is addressed separately, so computing kept the original 'one entry' meaning almost unchanged.","whyCN":"计算机列表字面上就是一串单位。每个单位都被单独寻址，所以计算机领域几乎原封不动地保留了“一个条目”的意思。"},{"no":"08","title":"Two people as one gossip entry","titleCN":"八卦里的一对：情侣（口语）","definition":"in informal usage, two people who are romantically involved, especially as a subject of gossip","definitionCN":"非正式用法中指处于恋爱关系的两个人，尤作为八卦话题","example":"The magazine says they are an item.","exampleCN":"杂志说他们在谈恋爱。","why":"Gossip columns list celebrity couples as single entries. A couple treated as one line in that list becomes 'an item'.","whyCN":"八卦专栏把名人情侣作为单独条目列出来。一对被当作清单中一行来对待的情侣，就成了“an item”。"},{"no":"09","title":"The old adverb: likewise","titleCN":"古副词义：同样、还有","definition":"in archaic legal or formal lists, the adverb item introduces another point, meaning 'likewise' or 'also'","definitionCN":"在古旧的法律或正式清单中，副词 item 引出另一点，意为“同样地”或“还有”","example":"Item, that the defendant shall appear on the first day.","exampleCN":"又一项：被告应于第一日到庭。","why":"This is the word's original part of speech. The noun exists because the adverb stood at the head of every line, and readers began to treat the marker as the thing marked.","whyCN":"这是这个词最初词性。名词之所以存在，是因为这个副词站在每一行的开头，读者逐渐把标记本身当成了被标记的东西。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Item is Latin item (adverb) 'likewise, just so, moreover', probably from ita 'thus' + an adverbial ending, related to id 'it'. It was used to introduce each new entry in a list, and English turned that list-marker into a noun meaning 'one entry'.","cn":"item 是拉丁语副词 item“同样地、正是如此、还有”，可能由 ita“如此”加副词词尾构成，与 id“它”有关。它被用来引出清单中的每一个新条目，英语把这个清单标记变成了名词，意为“一个条目”。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN ita / id","en":"Ita meant 'thus, so'; id meant 'it'. The adverb item probably combined ita with an ending, giving 'in the same way, likewise'.","cn":"ita 意为“如此、这样”；id 意为“它”。副词 item 可能由 ita 加一个词尾构成，得到“以同样的方式、同样地”。"},{"era":"LATIN item, adverb","en":"Item was used to introduce a new fact or statement, much like modern 'also' or 'furthermore'. In inventories it stood before every article.","cn":"item 用于引出一个新事实或新陈述，很像现代的“还有”或“此外”。在清单中，它站在每一条物品之前。"},{"era":"FRENCH / ENGLISH LISTS, 14c.","en":"In French and then English, item was written before every article in an enumeration, such as an inventory or a bill. The marker became a familiar part of the list.","cn":"在法语、随后在英语中，item 被写在枚举（如清单或账单）的每一条之前。这个标记成了清单中熟悉的一部分。"},{"era":"ENGLISH NOUN, 1570s","en":"This practice led to the noun sense 'an article of any kind' in the 1570s. Readers reinterpreted the introductory word as the name of the thing introduced.","cn":"这一习惯在 16 世纪 70 年代导致名词义“任何种类的物品”出现。读者把那个引导词重新理解成了被引导之物的名称。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, 1819","en":"The sense 'a detail of information, especially in a newspaper' is from 1819, when newspapers were organized as lists of separate reports.","cn":"“一条信息细节、尤指报纸中的一则”这一义项来自 1819 年，当时报纸正是按一则则独立报道来组织的。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, 1970","en":"The informal sense 'a romantically linked couple' is from 1970, probably from the idea of being an entry in the gossip columns.","cn":"“有恋爱关系的一对”这一非正式义项来自 1970 年，可能来自“成为八卦专栏中的一个条目”这一想法。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group is the item family; the near-meaning group contains words for single units, each used in a different kind of list or collection.","cn":"形近组是 item 词族；近义组是表示单个单位的词，各自用于不同类型的清单或集合。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"itemize","ipa":"/ˈaɪtəmaɪz/","tag":"same word, verb","definition":"to list things one by one. The -ize suffix turns the noun into the act of making a list of items.","definitionCN":"逐项列出。 -ize 后缀把名词变成“列出条目”的动作。"},{"word":"itemized","ipa":"/ˈaɪtəmaɪzd/","tag":"same verb, adjective","definition":"listed with each charge or entry shown separately, as in an itemized bill.","definitionCN":"逐项列出的，每笔费用或条目单独显示，如分项账单。"},{"word":"itemization","ipa":"/ˌaɪtəmaɪˈzeɪʃn/","tag":"same verb, noun","definition":"the act or result of listing things separately. It is the -ation noun of itemize.","definitionCN":"逐项列出的行为或结果。它是 itemize 的 -ation 名词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"article","ipa":"/ˈɑːtɪkl/","tag":"thing or piece of writing","definition":"a particular object, or a piece of writing in a publication. It is close to item but often larger or more formal.","definitionCN":"特定的物品，或出版物中的一篇文章。它与 item 相近，但通常更大或更正式。"},{"word":"entry","ipa":"/ˈentri/","tag":"one record in a list","definition":"one item written in a list, diary or database. It focuses on the act of writing something in, rather than the thing itself.","definitionCN":"写在清单、日记或数据库中的一条。它关注“写进去”的动作，而不是物品本身。"},{"word":"object","ipa":"/ˈɒbdʒɪkt/","tag":"physical thing","definition":"a material thing that can be seen and touched. It is broader and more physical than item.","definitionCN":"看得见、摸得着的实物。它比 item 更宽泛，也更强调物理性。"},{"word":"detail","ipa":"/ˈdiːteɪl/","tag":"small part of information","definition":"a small fact or feature belonging to a larger whole. It stresses smallness and belonging, not separate listing.","definitionCN":"属于更大整体的小事实或细节。它强调细小与从属，而不是单独列出。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: the Latin adverb item 'likewise', plus the ordinary family itemize, itemized, itemization, subitem.","cn":"只用真实构件：拉丁语副词 item“同样地”，以及常用词族 itemize、itemized、itemization、subitem。"},"normal":[{"en":"Latin item meant 'likewise' and stood at the start of every list line. English listeners turned the marker into the thing: each line became an item.","cn":"拉丁语 item 意为“同样地”，站在每一行清单的开头。英语使用者把标记变成了被标记之物：每一行都成了一个 item。"},{"en":"A list is the home of the word. An item is anything that can occupy one line: a product, a question, a news report, a charge, a data field.","cn":"清单是这个词的家。凡是能占据一行的东西都是 item：产品、问题、新闻报道、费用、数据字段。"},{"en":"Itemize means to break a whole into lines. An itemized bill shows each charge; a lump-sum bill does not.","cn":"itemize 就是把整体拆成一行一行。分项账单显示每笔费用；打包总价的账单则不显示。"},{"en":"The gossip sense 'they are an item' works because a celebrity couple occupies one line in a gossip column.","cn":"八卦义“they are an item”成立，是因为一对名人情侣在八卦专栏里占据一行。"},{"en":"Fixed patterns: item on the agenda, news item, line item, and item by item.","cn":"固定搭配：item on the agenda（议程项目）、news item（一则新闻）、line item（行项）、item by item（逐项地）。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"A list is a way of making the world countable. Item is the unit that a list creates, not a property the thing had before it was listed.","cn":"清单是让世界变得可计数的一种方式。item 是清单创造出来的单位，而不是事物在被列出之前就有的属性。"},{"en":"The same object can be a thing, a product, a charge or a question depending on which list it enters.","cn":"同一个对象可以是物品、商品、费用或问题，取决于它进入哪一份清单。"},{"en":"Attention works by items: we can only hold a few lines at once, which is why a long list feels heavy.","cn":"注意力是按条目运作的：我们一次只能握住几行，所以一份长清单会让人感到沉重。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The first item on the agenda is the annual budget.","cn":"议程上的第一项是年度预算。"},{"en":"She packed every item carefully in the box.","cn":"她把每一件物品都小心地装进箱子。"},{"en":"The newspaper printed a short item about the discovery.","cn":"报纸刊登了一则关于这项发现的短讯。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“爱·腾”——爱（把）腾（出的）东西一件件列在清单上 → item 项目、物品","word":"item"},"root":"源自拉丁语副词 item“同样地、还有”，它原本写在清单每一条之前，英语把这条“清单标记”变成了名词，核心是“清单中独立的一行”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of item, all one unit: one line in a list. Products, news reports, agenda points, accounting entries, test questions, data fields and even a celebrity couple are items because each can occupy a separate line.","cn":"item 的九个义项都是同一个单位：清单上的一行。商品、新闻报道、议程事项、会计记录、试题、数据字段，甚至一对名人情侣，都是 item，因为每一个都能占据单独的一行。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: one written line in a list, separated from the lines above and below.","cn":"核心意象：清单上的一行字，与上下行分开。"},"chain":["A LIST","A NEW LINE","INTRODUCTORY WORD","ONE SEPARATE UNIT","COUNTABLE THING","NAMED ENTRY"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S4 · S5","en":"MATERIAL AND COMMERCIAL UNITS: a single object, a product for sale, and one line in an account.","cn":"实物与商业单位：单件物品、待售商品，以及账目上的一行。"},{"senses":"S2 · S3 · S6","en":"INFORMATION UNITS: one news report, one agenda point, and one question in a test.","cn":"信息单位：一则新闻、一个议程事项、一道试题。"},{"senses":"S7","en":"DATA UNIT: one element in a menu, list or database, addressed separately.","cn":"数据单位：菜单、列表或数据库中可单独寻址的一个元素。"},{"senses":"S8","en":"SOCIAL UNIT: a couple treated as one entry in a gossip column.","cn":"社会单位：在八卦专栏中被当作一个条目的一对情侣。"},{"senses":"S9","en":"THE ORIGINAL MARKER: the adverb 'likewise' that once introduced every line.","cn":"最初的标记：曾经引出每一行的副词“同样地”。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Item is a borrowed Latin adverb that became an English noun. Its family is built with -ize, -ized, -ization and the prefix sub-.","cn":"item 是借入的拉丁语副词，后来变成英语名词。它的词族用 -ize、-ized、-ization 和前缀 sub- 构成。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin background is small: item 'likewise', ita 'thus', id 'it'. There is no Latin noun item; the noun is an English development.","cn":"拉丁语背景很简单：item“同样地”、ita“如此”、id“它”。拉丁语中没有名词 item；名词义是英语发展出来的。"},"items":[{"word":"item","structure":"Latin adverb item 'likewise', reinterpreted as a noun","meaning":"one entry or object in a list","meaningCN":"项目；物品；条目","example":"Each item has a price.","exampleCN":"每件商品都有价格。"},{"word":"items","structure":"item + -s (plural)","meaning":"more than one entry or object","meaningCN":"多个项目或物品","example":"The list contains twelve items.","exampleCN":"这份清单包含十二项。"},{"word":"itemize","structure":"item + -ize (to make or treat)","meaning":"to list things one by one","meaningCN":"逐项列出（-ize 表“使……化”）","example":"Please itemize the expenses.","exampleCN":"请把费用逐项列出。"},{"word":"itemized","structure":"itemize + -ed (past participle/adjective)","meaning":"listed separately, charge by charge","meaningCN":"逐项列出的；分项的","example":"We received an itemized receipt.","exampleCN":"我们收到了一张分项收据。"},{"word":"itemizing","structure":"itemize + -ing (participle)","meaning":"the act of listing separately","meaningCN":"逐项列出（现在分词）","example":"She spent the evening itemizing the costs.","exampleCN":"她花了一晚上逐项列出成本。"},{"word":"itemization","structure":"itemize + -ation (noun of action)","meaning":"a detailed list of separate entries","meaningCN":"逐项列记；分项明细（-ation 构成名词）","example":"The invoice includes a full itemization.","exampleCN":"发票附有完整的分项明细。"},{"word":"subitem","structure":"sub- (under) + item","meaning":"a smaller item within a larger one","meaningCN":"子项；分项（sub- 表下属）","example":"Each subitem has its own code.","exampleCN":"每个子项都有自己的代码。"},{"word":"line item","structure":"line + item (compound noun)","meaning":"a single entry on a financial statement","meaningCN":"行项；账目中的单独一行","example":"The software cost is a separate line item.","exampleCN":"软件费用是一个单独的行项。"},{"word":"news item","structure":"news + item (compound noun)","meaning":"a short report in a newspaper or broadcast","meaningCN":"一则新闻；一条消息","example":"The fire was a small news item.","exampleCN":"那场火灾只是一则小新闻。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"item","structure":"Latin adverb","meaning":"likewise, just so, moreover","meaningCN":"同样地；正是如此；还有"},{"word":"ita","structure":"Latin adverb","meaning":"thus, so","meaningCN":"如此；这样"},{"word":"id","structure":"Latin pronoun","meaning":"it, that","meaningCN":"它；那个"}]}},{"word":"justify","ipa_uk":"/ˈdʒʌstɪfaɪ/","ipa_us":"/ˈdʒʌstɪfaɪ/","definition_zh":"证明……正当；为……辩护；使合理化；对齐","definition_en":"to show that something is right, reasonable or deserved; to defend someone; to align text evenly on both sides","core_image":"一架天平，一侧放事实与理由，另一侧放指控，理由那一侧沉沉压下去","scene":"法庭上，律师举起一份银行记录，向陪审团说明当事人的行为有正当理由。她说：The evidence can justify my client's actions.","sceneCN":"这里 justify 是「证明……有正当理由」（第 1、3 个义项：用理由证明正当、为结论提供依据）；句意：证据可以证明我当事人的行为是正当的。图中可辨识物件：法庭、银行记录、陪审团、律师。","pos":[{"tag":"vt.","zh":"证明……正当；为……辩护；使合理化"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"（排版）使左右对齐"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"justify a decision","zh":"为决定提供正当理由"},{"phrase":"justify the cost","zh":"证明成本是值得的"},{"phrase":"justify one's actions","zh":"为自己的行为辩护"},{"phrase":"the end justifies the means","zh":"目的证明手段正当"},{"phrase":"be justified in doing","zh":"有理由做某事"},{"phrase":"justify text","zh":"使文本两端对齐"}],"forms":[{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"justifies"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"justified"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"justified"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"justifying"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"justification","pos":"n.","zh":"正当理由；辩护；辩护理由"},{"word":"justifiable","pos":"adj.","zh":"可证明为正当的；有道理的"},{"word":"justified","pos":"adj.","zh":"有正当理由的；理所当然的"},{"word":"unjustified","pos":"adj.","zh":"不正当的；无正当理由的"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Making something stand as right","titleCN":"使某事站得住：证明正当","definition":"to give reasons showing that an action, decision or belief is right or reasonable","definitionCN":"给出理由，表明某个行动、决定或信念是正确的、合理的","example":"How can you justify spending so much on one meal?","exampleCN":"你怎么能证明在一顿饭上花这么多钱是合理的？","why":"Late Latin iustificare is iustus 'just' + facere 'to make': to make something just. Justify is literally 'make right', and the reasons are what do the making.","whyCN":"晚期拉丁语 iustificare 是 iustus“正当的”加 facere“使”，即“使某物成为正当”。justify 字面就是“使正确”，而理由就是使它成立的东西。"},{"no":"02","title":"Standing up for someone","titleCN":"替人说话：为……辩护","definition":"to defend a person or their conduct against blame or accusation","definitionCN":"在指责或指控面前为某人或其行为辩护","example":"Nothing can justify what he did to those children.","exampleCN":"他所做的那些伤害孩子的事，无论怎样都无法辩护。","why":"If a person is accused, the accusation places weight on one side of the scale. To justify is to put reasons on the other side until the person can stand.","whyCN":"一个人被指控时，指控把重量压在天平的一侧。justify 就是在另一侧放上理由，直到这个人能站得住。"},{"no":"03","title":"Evidence as a reason","titleCN":"证据作为理由：为结论提供依据","definition":"of evidence or facts, to be a good reason for a belief, conclusion or claim","definitionCN":"（证据或事实）成为某个信念、结论或主张的良好理由","example":"The results justify the conclusion that the drug works.","exampleCN":"这些结果为“该药有效”这一结论提供了依据。","why":"Here the direction reverses: the evidence does the justifying. Whatever makes a claim stand upright is the justification of that claim.","whyCN":"这里方向反过来了：是证据在证明。凡是能让一个主张站直的东西，就是它的正当依据。"},{"no":"04","title":"The end and the means","titleCN":"目的与手段：目的证明手段正当","definition":"in the phrase the end justifies the means, to claim that a good result makes wrong methods acceptable","definitionCN":"在短语 the end justifies the means 中，主张好的结果可以使错误手段变得可接受","example":"He believed the end justified the means, so he lied to protect the project.","exampleCN":"他相信目的可以证明手段正当，所以为了保住项目而撒了谎。","why":"The phrase weighs one action (the means) against one outcome (the end). Saying the end justifies the means is saying the outcome is heavy enough to balance the wrong.","whyCN":"这个短语把一种行为（手段）与一个结果（目的）放在天平两端。说“目的证明手段”，就是说结果足够重，能抵消手段的错误。"},{"no":"05","title":"Even margins on both sides","titleCN":"两边留白都齐：两端对齐","definition":"in printing and typography, to adjust the spaces in a line so that both margins are straight","definitionCN":"印刷排版中调整行内空格，使左右两边都齐平","example":"The program can justify the text to fill the page width.","exampleCN":"这个程序可以把文本两端对齐以填满页面宽度。","why":"A justified line is made 'right' at both edges: the margins stand straight like the two sides of a balanced scale. The metaphor is visual rather than moral.","whyCN":"两端对齐的行在两条边上都“端正”：页边像天平两边一样笔直站立。这里的比喻是视觉的，而不是道德的。"},{"no":"06","title":"Declared righteous","titleCN":"被宣告为义：神学意义上的称义","definition":"in theology, of God, to declare a sinner righteous through faith, not through their own merit","definitionCN":"神学中，上帝因信宣告罪人为义，而不是因他们自身的功德","example":"The doctrine holds that believers are justified by faith.","exampleCN":"该教义认为信徒是因信称义。","why":"The religious sense is the most literal 'make just': a person is not merely shown to be right but is declared and treated as right. The verb's oldest English use was in this domain.","whyCN":"宗教义是最字面的“使为义”：一个人不只是被表明为正当，而是被宣告并按正当对待。这个词最早的英语用法就在这个领域。"},{"no":"07","title":"Showing lawful cause","titleCN":"表明合法理由：法律上的正当性","definition":"in law, to show that there was a lawful or sufficient reason for an act","definitionCN":"法律中，表明某项行为有合法或充分的理由","example":"The officer had to justify the search under the statute.","exampleCN":"警官必须依据法规说明这次搜查的正当理由。","why":"Law does not ask whether an act felt right; it asks whether reasons of the right kind can be produced. Justification is the legal form of 'making it stand'.","whyCN":"法律不问行为感觉是否正确，而问能否提出正确类型的理由。正当化就是“使它站得住”的法律形式。"},{"no":"08","title":"Explaining oneself","titleCN":"为自己解释：justify oneself","definition":"in the phrase justify oneself, to explain one's actions in order to avoid blame","definitionCN":"在短语 justify oneself 中，解释自己的行为以避免责备","example":"He tried to justify himself to the committee.","exampleCN":"他试图向委员会解释自己的行为。","why":"The reflexive form makes the person both the maker and the thing made just. You place your own reasons on the scale to keep yourself upright.","whyCN":"反身形式使人既是“使动者”，也是被“使正当”的对象。你把自己的理由放到天平上，以保持自己站直。"},{"no":"09","title":"The older sense: make exact","titleCN":"旧义：使精确、校验","definition":"in older technical usage, to make exact or verify, especially in typesetting and measurement","definitionCN":"较旧的技术用法中，使精确或校验，尤用于排版与测量","example":"The printer justified the type to exact width.","exampleCN":"印刷工把字行校准到精确宽度。","why":"To make a line exact is to make it conform to a standard. The 'exact' sense is a narrow technical survival of 'make right'.","whyCN":"把一行做得精确，就是使它符合标准。“精确”义是“使正确”在技术语境中的狭窄残留。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Justify comes from Old French justifier, from Late Latin iustificare 'to act justly toward; make just', from iustus 'just' + facere 'to make'. Iustus comes from ius 'law, right'. The same ius underlies judge (iudex, ius + dicere) and jury (iurare, to swear).","cn":"justify 来自古法语 justifier，再上溯到晚期拉丁语 iustificare“公正对待；使为义”，由 iustus“正当的”加 facere“使、做”构成。iustus 又来自 ius“法律、权利”。同一个 ius 也是 judge（iudex = ius + dicere）和 jury（iurare，宣誓）的词根。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN ius","en":"Ius meant 'law, right, justice'. It is the root of iustus 'just', iudex 'judge' (ius + dicere 'to say'), and iurare 'to swear', which gave jury. Law is what is 'right' in the shared sense.","cn":"ius 意为“法律、权利、正义”。它是 iustus“正当的”、iudex“法官”（ius + dicere“说”）、iurare“宣誓”（给出 jury）的词根。法律就是共同意义上的“正当”。"},{"era":"LATIN iustus","en":"Iustus meant 'upright, righteous, equitable; in accordance with law'. English just comes directly from it.","cn":"iustus 意为“正直的、公正的、符合法律的”。英语 just 直接来自它。"},{"era":"LATE LATIN iustificare","en":"Iustificare meant 'to act justly toward; to make just'. The -ficare element is from facere 'to make', so the verb literally means 'make just'.","cn":"iustificare 意为“公正对待；使为义”。其中 -ficare 来自 facere“使、做”，所以这个动词字面就是“使成为正当”。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH justifier, 12c.","en":"Old French justifier meant 'to submit to court proceedings' as well as 'to show to be right'. The legal and moral senses traveled together.","cn":"古法语 justifier 既表示“提交法庭程序”，也表示“表明为正当”。法律义与道德义一起传播。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, c.1300","en":"English first recorded justify around 1300 meaning 'to administer justice'. By the late 14th century it meant 'to show something to be just or right'.","cn":"英语最早在约 1300 年记录 justify，意为“施行正义”。到 14 世纪晚期，它表示“表明某事为正当或正确”。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, 1520s–1550s","en":"The sense 'declare innocent or blameless' is from the 1520s; the typographic sense 'make exact, align' is from the 1550s. Both are specialised applications of 'make right'.","cn":"“宣告无罪或无过”的义项来自 16 世纪 20 年代；排版义“使精确、对齐”来自 16 世纪 50 年代。两者都是“使正确”的专业化应用。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group shares the ius/iust- root; the near-meaning group contains verbs of defence and reason-giving, each with a different basis for making something stand.","cn":"形近组共享 ius/iust- 词根；近义组是辩护与给理由类动词，各自让事物“站得住”的依据不同。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"justification","ipa":"/ˌdʒʌstɪfɪˈkeɪʃn/","tag":"same verb, noun","definition":"a reason or explanation that shows something is right. It is justify + -ation, and in theology it names the act of being declared righteous.","definitionCN":"表明某事正当的理由或解释。它是 justify 加 -ation，在神学中指“称义”。"},{"word":"justifiable","ipa":"/ˈdʒʌstɪfaɪəbl/","tag":"same verb, adjective","definition":"able to be shown as right or reasonable. The -able suffix marks capacity for justification.","definitionCN":"可被证明为正当或合理的。-able 后缀标记“可被正当化”的能力。"},{"word":"justice","ipa":"/ˈdʒʌstɪs/","tag":"same root, noun","definition":"fairness in treatment and law. It comes from Latin iustitia, from iustus, and is the root idea behind justify rather than a form of the verb.","definitionCN":"待遇与法律上的公平。它来自拉丁语 iustitia，再上溯到 iustus，是 justify 背后的根观念，而不是该动词的一种形式。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"defend","ipa":"/dɪˈfend/","tag":"protect from attack","definition":"to speak or act in support of someone who is attacked. It stresses protection, while justify stresses supplying reasons.","definitionCN":"为受到攻击的人说话或行动。它强调保护，而 justify 强调提供理由。"},{"word":"excuse","ipa":"/ɪkˈskjuːz/","tag":"lessen blame","definition":"to forgive or overlook a fault, often by giving a reason. It seeks to reduce blame rather than to prove the act right.","definitionCN":"原谅或忽略过错，常通过给出理由。它寻求减轻责备，而不是证明行为正确。"},{"word":"warrant","ipa":"/ˈwɒrənt/","tag":"authorize by reason","definition":"to make an action seem necessary or proper; to justify or authorize. It is close to the 'provide grounds' sense but more formal.","definitionCN":"使某行动显得必要或恰当；证明或授权。它与“提供依据”义接近，但更正式。"},{"word":"vindicate","ipa":"/ˈvɪndɪkeɪt/","tag":"clear of blame","definition":"to prove that someone is right or free from blame after being criticized. It focuses on the person's restored reputation, not on the reasons themselves.","definitionCN":"在被批评后证明某人正确或无罪。它关注人的名誉恢复，而不是理由本身。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: Latin ius 'law/right', iustus 'just', and facere 'make', plus the ordinary family justification, justifiable, justified, unjustified.","cn":"只用真实构件：拉丁语 ius“法律/权利”、iustus“正当的”、facere“使”，以及常用词族 justification、justifiable、justified、unjustified。"},"normal":[{"en":"Iustus + facere = 'make just'. To justify is to put reasons on the scale until the thing can stand up as right.","cn":"iustus + facere = “使正当”。justify 就是把理由放到天平上，直到那件事能作为“正确”站起来。"},{"en":"Judge and jury share the same ius root: a judge says the law (ius + dicere), and a jury swears (iurare). Justice is the family's core noun.","cn":"judge 与 jury 共享同一个 ius 词根：法官说出法律（ius + dicere），陪审团宣誓（iurare）。justice 是这个词族的核心名词。"},{"en":"The direction can reverse: you justify your action with reasons, or the evidence justifies your conclusion. In both cases something is made to stand.","cn":"方向可以反转：你用理由 justify 你的行为，或者证据 justify 你的结论。两种情况下，都是某物被“使站得住”。"},{"en":"The typographic sense is visual, not moral: a justified line is straight on both margins, like a balanced scale.","cn":"排版义是视觉的，不是道德的：两端对齐的行在两条页边上都笔直，像一架平衡的天平。"},{"en":"Fixed patterns: justify a decision, justify the cost, be justified in doing, and justify text.","cn":"固定搭配：justify a decision（为决定提供理由）、justify the cost（证明成本值得）、be justified in doing（有理由做）、justify text（文本两端对齐）。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Justification never removes an act; it changes the account under which the act is held. The deed stays, the meaning moves.","cn":"正当化从不取消一个行为；它改变的是这个行为被记在哪个账目下。行为还在，意义移动了。"},{"en":"A scale can be balanced with true weights or false ones. The word describes the balancing, not the honesty of what is put on it.","cn":"天平可以用真砝码平衡，也可以用假砝码平衡。这个词描述的是“平衡”本身，而不是放上去的东西是否诚实。"},{"en":"'The end justifies the means' is a claim that consequences are heavier than principles. Whether that is true is an ethical question the word cannot settle.","cn":"“目的证明手段”是一个主张：后果比原则更重。这个主张是否成立，是这个词本身无法解决的伦理问题。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The company was asked to justify the sudden price increase.","cn":"公司被要求解释突然涨价的理由。"},{"en":"She felt fully justified in leaving early.","cn":"她觉得自己提早离开完全有理由。"},{"en":"Justify the paragraph so that both margins are even.","cn":"把这一段两端对齐，使左右页边齐平。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“扎斯提·派”——扎斯提（把）派（出的）理由摆上天平，让事情站稳 → justify 证明正当","word":"justify"},"root":"源自拉丁语 iustificare“使为义”，由 iustus“正当的”（源于 ius“法律、权利”）加 facere“使”构成，核心是“用理由把某事放到正当的位置上”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of justify, all one act: make something stand as right. Reasons, evidence, a defence, an outcome, a straight margin, a declaration of righteousness or a legal cause each supply the weight that keeps the thing upright.","cn":"justify 的九个义项都是同一个动作：使某物作为“正当”站住。理由、证据、辩护、结果、笔直的页边、称义的宣告或法律上的原因，各自提供让那件事站直的重量。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a balance scale weighted with reasons until the accused side rises level.","cn":"核心意象：一架天平被理由压到两边齐平，被指控的一侧重新抬平。"},"chain":["ACCUSATION OR DOUBT","WEIGHT ON ONE SIDE","REASONS ADDED","BALANCE RESTORED","DECLARED RIGHT","ACCEPTED AS JUST"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S8","en":"REASON-GIVING: a person supplies reasons for an action, either for someone else or for themselves.","cn":"给理由：一个人为某个行为提供理由，或替别人，或替自己。"},{"senses":"S2 · S7","en":"DEFENCE AND LAW: answering an accusation, and showing a lawful or sufficient cause in court.","cn":"辩护与法律：回应指控，以及在法庭上表明合法或充分的理由。"},{"senses":"S3 · S4","en":"GROUNDS FOR A CLAIM: evidence makes a conclusion stand, and an outcome may be claimed to outweigh a wrong means.","cn":"主张的依据：证据使结论站住；结果也可能被主张为足以抵消错误手段。"},{"senses":"S6","en":"THEOLOGICAL DECLARATION: God declares a person righteous, the most literal 'make just'.","cn":"神学宣告：上帝宣告一个人为义，这是最字面的“使为义”。"},{"senses":"S5 · S9","en":"TECHNICAL ALIGNMENT: making a line or measure exact, so that its edges stand straight.","cn":"技术性对齐：把一行或一个测量做得精确，使它的边缘站直。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Justify is a Latin-derived verb: iust- + -ify. Its family uses -ation, -able, participial -ed, and the negative prefix un-.","cn":"justify 是拉丁来源的动词：iust- + -ify。它的词族使用 -ation、-able、分词 -ed，以及否定前缀 un-。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin set is ius 'law/right', iustus 'just', iustificare 'make just', and iustificatio 'justification'. Iudex and iurare branch from the same ius.","cn":"拉丁词族是 ius“法律/权利”、iustus“正当的”、iustificare“使为义”、iustificatio“称义”。iudex 与 iurare 也从同一个 ius 分出。"},"items":[{"word":"justify","structure":"iust- (just) + -ify (to make)","meaning":"to make or show something to be right","meaningCN":"证明……正当；使合理化（-ify 表“使……”）","example":"He could not justify his absence.","exampleCN":"他无法为自己的缺席辩解。"},{"word":"justifies","structure":"justify + -es (third person singular)","meaning":"shows to be right or reasonable","meaningCN":"证明……正当（第三人称单数）","example":"The evidence justifies the search.","exampleCN":"证据使这次搜查具有正当性。"},{"word":"justified","structure":"justify + -ed (past participle/adjective)","meaning":"shown to be right; having good reason","meaningCN":"有正当理由的；理所当然的","example":"Her anger was justified.","exampleCN":"她的愤怒是有理由的。"},{"word":"justifying","structure":"justify + -ing (participle)","meaning":"giving reasons for something","meaningCN":"正在为……提供理由","example":"He kept justifying his decision.","exampleCN":"他不断为自己的决定辩解。"},{"word":"justification","structure":"justify + -ation (noun of action)","meaning":"a reason that shows something is right","meaningCN":"正当理由；辩护（-ation 构成名词）","example":"There is no justification for such violence.","exampleCN":"这种暴力没有任何正当理由。"},{"word":"justifiable","structure":"justify + -able (can be)","meaning":"able to be shown as right or reasonable","meaningCN":"可证明为正当的；有道理的（-able 表“能……”）","example":"The shooting was ruled justifiable.","exampleCN":"这次开枪被裁定为正当。"},{"word":"justifiably","structure":"justifiable + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"with good reason","meaningCN":"有理由地；正当地","example":"She was justifiably proud of her son.","exampleCN":"她有理由为儿子感到骄傲。"},{"word":"justificatory","structure":"justify + -atory (adjective)","meaning":"serving to justify, often in formal writing","meaningCN":"起辩护作用的；用于证明的（较正式）","example":"The report has a justificatory purpose.","exampleCN":"这份报告带有辩护目的。"},{"word":"unjustified","structure":"un- (not) + justified","meaning":"not shown to be right; without good reason","meaningCN":"不正当的；无正当理由的","example":"The attack was completely unjustified.","exampleCN":"这次攻击完全没有正当理由。"},{"word":"unjustifiable","structure":"un- (not) + justifiable","meaning":"impossible to show as right","meaningCN":"无法证明为正当的；不可原谅的","example":"The delay was unjustifiable.","exampleCN":"这次延误毫无正当理由。"},{"word":"justice","structure":"Latin iustitia, from iustus","meaning":"fairness; the quality of being just","meaningCN":"正义；公平（同根名词）","example":"They demanded justice for the victims.","exampleCN":"他们为受害者要求正义。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"ius","structure":"Latin noun","meaning":"law, right, justice","meaningCN":"法律；权利；正义"},{"word":"iustus","structure":"ius + -tus","meaning":"just, lawful, equitable","meaningCN":"正当的；合法的；公正的"},{"word":"iustificare","structure":"iustus + facere","meaning":"to make just, act justly toward","meaningCN":"使为义；公正对待"},{"word":"iudex","structure":"ius + dicere 'to say'","meaning":"judge, one who declares the law","meaningCN":"法官；宣示法律的人"}]}},{"word":"labor","ipa_uk":"/ˈleɪbə/","ipa_us":"/ˈleɪbər/","definition_zh":"劳动；劳工；分娩；努力；劳作","definition_en":"physical or mental work, especially hard work; workers as a class; the process of giving birth; to work hard","core_image":"一个人弯着腰在田里挥锄，汗滴落进土里","scene":"天还没亮，建筑工地上已经有人在搬砖、拌灰。工头对手下说：This job takes hard labor.","sceneCN":"这里 labor 是「体力劳动、苦工」（第 1、6 个义项：体力劳动、艰苦努力）；句意：这份工作需要艰苦的劳动。图中可辨识物件：砖块、灰桶、脚手架、工人。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"劳动；劳工；分娩；努力"},{"tag":"vi.","zh":"劳动；努力；费力地做"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"hard labor","zh":"苦工；重体力劳动"},{"phrase":"manual labor","zh":"体力劳动"},{"phrase":"labor force","zh":"劳动力"},{"phrase":"labor union","zh":"工会"},{"phrase":"go into labor","zh":"开始分娩"},{"phrase":"labor under a delusion","zh":"处于错觉之中"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（多于一个）","form":"labors"},{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"labors"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"labored"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"labored"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"laboring"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"laborer","pos":"n.","zh":"劳动者；劳工"},{"word":"laborious","pos":"adj.","zh":"费力的；艰苦的"},{"word":"laboriously","pos":"adv.","zh":"费力地；艰难地"},{"word":"laboratory","pos":"n.","zh":"实验室（同词根，原义“工作的地方”）"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Work that costs the body","titleCN":"消耗身体的活：劳动、苦工","definition":"physical work, especially when it is hard, tiring and done for others","definitionCN":"体力工作，尤指艰苦、令人疲惫并为他人而做的工作","example":"The harvest required weeks of hard labor.","exampleCN":"收割需要数周的艰苦劳动。","why":"Latin labor meant 'toil, exertion, hardship, pain'. The word never merely meant 'activity'; it carries the weight and fatigue of work that costs something.","whyCN":"拉丁语 labor 意为“辛劳、用力、艰苦、痛苦”。这个词从来不只是“活动”，它带着有代价的工作所包含的重量与疲惫。"},{"no":"02","title":"Workers as one body","titleCN":"作为整体的工人：劳工","definition":"the body of workers considered as a class, especially in contrast to employers or capital","definitionCN":"被作为一个阶级看待的工人群体，尤与雇主或资本相对","example":"The report examines the relationship between labor and capital.","exampleCN":"这份报告考察劳资关系。","why":"When many people's work is seen as one social force, the uncountable noun becomes a collective name. Labor is then the class, not one person's effort.","whyCN":"当许多人的劳动被看作一股社会力量时，这个不可数名词就变成了集合名称。此时 labor 指阶级，而不是某个人的努力。"},{"no":"03","title":"The work of giving birth","titleCN":"生育的劳作：分娩","definition":"the process of childbirth, especially the contractions and effort of giving birth","definitionCN":"分娩过程，尤指宫缩与用力的过程","example":"She went into labor shortly after midnight.","exampleCN":"午夜过后不久她开始分娩。","why":"Childbirth is work in the oldest sense: effort, pain and a hard passage. English took the phrase labour of birthe and shortened it to labor.","whyCN":"分娩是最古老意义上的工作：用力、疼痛、艰难的通过。英语把 labour of birthe 这个短语缩略为 labor。"},{"no":"04","title":"A task or project","titleCN":"一件任务：劳作、功业","definition":"a particular task or piece of work, often a long or difficult one","definitionCN":"一项特定的任务或工作，常指漫长或艰难的一项","example":"The twelve labors of Hercules are famous in myth.","exampleCN":"赫拉克勒斯的十二项功业在神话中很有名。","why":"The oldest English sense was 'a task, a project', as in the labors of Hercules. A labor is a bounded piece of toil with a beginning and an end.","whyCN":"英语最早的义项是“任务、工程”，如赫拉克勒斯的功业。一项 labor 就是一段有起点和终点的辛劳。"},{"no":"05","title":"Labor as a factor of production","titleCN":"生产要素中的劳动","definition":"in economics, the human effort used in producing goods and services, one of the factors of production","definitionCN":"经济学中，用于生产商品和服务的人力投入，是生产要素之一","example":"The cost of labor rose faster than the cost of materials.","exampleCN":"劳动力成本上涨得比材料成本更快。","why":"Economics needed a countable input alongside land and capital. It took the human exertion already named labor and treated it as a measurable factor.","whyCN":"经济学需要在土地和资本之外有一个可计量的投入。它把已经被命名为 labor 的人力付出拿来，当作一个可测量的要素。"},{"no":"06","title":"Effort of the mind","titleCN":"心智的用力：脑力劳动","definition":"mental effort, especially sustained and difficult thinking or study","definitionCN":"脑力上的付出，尤指持续而艰难的思考或学习","example":"Solving the proof took great mental labor.","exampleCN":"解出这个证明需要巨大的脑力劳动。","why":"The word began with the body, but English extended it to any effort that feels heavy. Mental labor is work that tires the mind the way digging tires the arms.","whyCN":"这个词从身体开始，但英语把它扩展到任何令人感到沉重的付出。脑力劳动使头脑疲惫，就像挖土使手臂疲惫。"},{"no":"07","title":"To work hard","titleCN":"用力去做：劳作、努力","definition":"as a verb, to work hard, especially with physical effort","definitionCN":"作动词，指努力工作，尤指付出体力","example":"They labored in the fields from dawn to dusk.","exampleCN":"他们从黎明到黄昏在田里劳作。","why":"The verb is simply the noun turned into action: to perform labor. It keeps the bodily, effortful flavour of the noun.","whyCN":"动词就是名词转成动作：进行 labor。它保留了名词那种身体性的、费力的味道。"},{"no":"08","title":"Laboring under a false belief","titleCN":"在错觉下挣扎：labor under","definition":"in the phrase labor under, to suffer from or be burdened by a mistaken belief or difficulty","definitionCN":"在短语 labor under 中，指因错误信念或困难而受苦、受拖累","example":"He labors under the delusion that everyone agrees with him.","exampleCN":"他误以为所有人都同意他。","why":"To labor under something is to carry it as a weight while trying to move. A false belief is pictured as a load on the back, not just a wrong idea.","whyCN":"labor under 某物，就是一边想前进一边把它当作重量背着。错误信念被画成背上的负担，而不只是一个错想法。"},{"no":"09","title":"Laboring the point","titleCN":"反复敲同一点：labor the point","definition":"in the phrase labor the point, to explain or repeat something more than necessary","definitionCN":"在短语 labor the point 中，指不必要地反复解释或重复某一点","example":"You don't need to labor the point; we all understood.","exampleCN":"你不必反复强调这一点，我们都明白了。","why":"If talking is work, then repeating the same point is working ground that has already been worked. The phrase images effort spent where it is no longer needed.","whyCN":"如果说话也是劳作，那么反复讲同一点，就是在已经耕过的地上再耕一遍。这个短语描绘的是把力气花在不再需要的地方。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Labor comes from Old French labor/labeur, from Latin labor 'toil, exertion; hardship, pain; a work, a product of labor'. The origin of the Latin word is uncertain. A suggested link to labare 'to totter' (tottering under a burden) is often repeated but has been judged unconvincing by some etymologists. Treat it as 'uncertain, sometimes connected with labare'.","cn":"labor 来自古法语 labor/labeur，再上溯到拉丁语 labor“辛劳、用力；艰苦、痛苦；工作、劳动产品”。这个拉丁词的来源不确定。常有人提出它与 labare“摇晃、踉跄”（在重担下摇晃）有关，但一些词源学家认为这不可信。应写作“来源不确定，有时与 labare 相联系”。"},"items":[{"era":"LATIN labor, origin uncertain","en":"Labor meant 'toil, exertion; hardship, pain, fatigue; a work, a product of labor'. It already covered both the effort and the thing produced.","cn":"labor 意为“辛劳、用力；艰苦、痛苦、疲惫；工作、劳动产品”。它已经同时覆盖付出与产物。"},{"era":"SUGGESTED LINK, not established","en":"Some sources connect labor with labare 'to totter, waver', picturing a person tottering under a load. De Vaan finds this unconvincing. No other root is securely established, so the honest label is 'uncertain'.","cn":"一些资料把 labor 与 labare“摇晃、踉跄”联系起来，想象一个人在重担下踉跄。de Vaan 认为这不可信。也没有其他词根被可靠确立，所以诚实的标注是“来源不确定”。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH labor, 12c.","en":"Old French labor (Modern French labeur) meant 'toil, work, exertion, task; tribulation, suffering'. English borrowed it after the Norman period.","cn":"古法语 labor（现代法语 labeur）意为“辛劳、工作、用力、任务；磨难、痛苦”。英语在诺曼时期之后借入。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, c.1300","en":"English first recorded labor as 'a task, a project', as in the labors of Hercules. The sense 'exertion of the body; trouble, hardship' followed in the late 14th century.","cn":"英语最早记录 labor 为“任务、工程”，如赫拉克勒斯的功业。“身体用力；麻烦、艰苦”的义项随后在 14 世纪晚期出现。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, 1590s–1839","en":"The sense 'physical exertions of childbirth' is from the 1590s, short for labour of birthe. The sense 'body of productive workers as a class' is from 1839.","cn":"“分娩的身体用力”义项来自 16 世纪 90 年代，是 labour of birthe 的缩略。“作为阶级的生产性工人群体”义项来自 1839 年。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, modern compounds","en":"Labor Day, labor union and labor force all turn the noun into a social and economic category. The spelling labour is British; labor is American.","cn":"Labor Day、labor union、labor force 都把名词变成社会与经济范畴。拼写 labour 为英式，labor 为美式。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group shares the labor root; the near-meaning group contains words for work and effort, each with a different amount of strain or dignity.","cn":"形近组共享 labor 词根；近义组是工作与努力类词，各自的辛苦程度或尊严色彩不同。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"laborer","ipa":"/ˈleɪbərə/","tag":"same root, person","definition":"a person who does hard physical work, especially outdoors or on a building site. The -er suffix marks the one who labors.","definitionCN":"从事艰苦体力劳动的人，尤指户外或建筑工地上的工人。-er 后缀标记劳动的人。"},{"word":"laborious","ipa":"/ləˈbɔːriəs/","tag":"same root, adjective","definition":"requiring a lot of time and effort. The -ious suffix turns labor into a quality of the task.","definitionCN":"需要大量时间和努力的。-ious 后缀把 labor 变成任务的性质。"},{"word":"laboratory","ipa":"/ləˈbɒrətri/","tag":"same root, place","definition":"a room or building for scientific work. It comes from Medieval Latin laboratorium 'a place for working', from laborare 'to work'.","definitionCN":"用于科学工作的房间或建筑。它来自中世纪拉丁语 laboratorium“工作的地方”，再上溯到 laborare“工作”。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"work","ipa":"/wɜːk/","tag":"general activity","definition":"activity done to achieve something, especially as a job. It is the broad native word and carries no special weight of pain.","definitionCN":"为达成某事而做的活动，尤指作为职业。它是最宽泛的本族词，不特别带有痛苦重量。"},{"word":"toil","ipa":"/tɔɪl/","tag":"long hard work","definition":"long, exhausting work. It is closer to labor than work is, and often suggests continuation without relief.","definitionCN":"漫长而疲惫的工作。它比 work 更接近 labor，常暗示没有喘息地持续。"},{"word":"effort","ipa":"/ˈefət/","tag":"attempted exertion","definition":"the physical or mental energy used to do something. It names the energy spent rather than the work as a whole.","definitionCN":"为做某事而使用的体力或脑力。它命名被消耗的能量，而不是整体工作。"},{"word":"exertion","ipa":"/ɪɡˈzɜːʃn/","tag":"strenuous use","definition":"the use of physical or mental power, especially when strenuous. It is the formal noun for the strain that labor implies.","definitionCN":"体力或脑力的使用，尤指费力的使用。它是 labor 所暗示的“用力”的正式名词。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: Latin labor 'toil', the ordinary family laborer, laborious, laboriously, laboratory, and the fixed phrases labor under and labor the point.","cn":"只用真实构件：拉丁语 labor“辛劳”，常用词族 laborer、laborious、laboriously、laboratory，以及固定短语 labor under 与 labor the point。"},"normal":[{"en":"Labor means work that costs: sweat, fatigue, pain. It is not neutral activity; it is the weight of doing something difficult.","cn":"labor 指有代价的工作：汗水、疲惫、疼痛。它不是中性的活动，而是做难事时承受的重量。"},{"en":"Laboratory is the same root: a laboratorium was 'a place for working'. Science labs are places of labor before they are places of discovery.","cn":"laboratory 是同一词根：laboratorium 就是“工作的地方”。科学实验室在成为发现之地以前，先是劳作之地。"},{"en":"The social sense came late: only in 1839 did 'labor' mean workers as a class, contrasted with capital.","cn":"社会义出现得晚：直到 1839 年，labor 才指作为阶级的工人，与资本相对。"},{"en":"Childbirth is labor in the oldest sense: effort, pain and a hard passage. English shortened labour of birthe to labor.","cn":"分娩是最古老意义上的 labor：用力、疼痛、艰难的通过。英语把 labour of birthe 缩略为 labor。"},{"en":"Two fixed phrases carry the weight metaphor: labor under a delusion (carry a false belief as a load) and labor the point (work ground already worked).","cn":"两个固定短语延续了“重量”比喻：labor under a delusion（把错误信念当负担背）与 labor the point（在已耕过的地上再耕）。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"Labor is the meeting point of body and value: the same word names the strain and the thing the strain produces.","cn":"labor 是身体与价值的交汇点：同一个词既命名辛苦，也命名辛苦所产生的东西。"},{"en":"A society's view of labor is a view of people: call it a cost, a class or a calling, and you have described who counts.","cn":"一个社会对 labor 的看法就是对人的看法：你把它叫作成本、阶级还是使命，就已经描述了谁被算作重要。"},{"en":"The word's uncertain origin is a reminder that not every deep root can be recovered; what is certain is the human experience it names.","cn":"这个词来源不确定，提醒我们并非每个深层词根都能被复原；确定的是它所命名的人类经验。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"The factory replaced manual labor with machines.","cn":"工厂用机器取代了体力劳动。"},{"en":"She was in labor for twelve hours.","cn":"她分娩了十二个小时。"},{"en":"They labored all night to finish the report.","cn":"他们整夜劳作以完成报告。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“累·伯”——累（到）伯（伯都）弯下腰去干活 → labor 劳动、苦工","word":"labor"},"root":"源自拉丁语 labor“辛劳、用力、艰苦、痛苦”，其更早来源不确定（有时被联系到 labare“摇晃”，但未获普遍认可），核心是“有代价、会让人疲惫的劳作”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of labor, all one experience: effort that costs. Fieldwork, a social class, childbirth, a mythic task, an economic input, mental strain, the act of working, carrying a false belief and repeating a point are all forms of weight-bearing work.","cn":"labor 的九个义项都是同一种经验：有代价的付出。田间劳作、社会阶级、分娩、神话任务、经济投入、脑力消耗、劳动动作、背着错误信念、反复强调一点，都是有重量的工作形式。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a worker bent over a field, sweat falling into the soil.","cn":"核心意象：一个人弯着腰在田里干活，汗落进土里。"},"chain":["BODY AT WORK","STRAIN AND FATIGUE","SOMETHING PRODUCED","WORK AS A TASK","WORKERS AS A CLASS","EFFORT AS A BURDEN"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S6 · S7","en":"EFFORT ITSELF: physical toil, mental strain and the verb of working hard.","cn":"付出本身：体力辛劳、脑力消耗，以及努力工作的动词。"},{"senses":"S2 · S5","en":"LABOR AS A SOCIAL AND ECONOMIC CATEGORY: workers as a class and human effort as a factor of production.","cn":"作为社会与经济范畴的劳动：作为阶级的工人，以及作为生产要素的人力。"},{"senses":"S3","en":"CHILDBIRTH: the oldest bodily labor, effort and pain in a hard passage.","cn":"分娩：最古老的身体劳作，在艰难通道中的用力与疼痛。"},{"senses":"S4","en":"A BOUNDED TASK: one long piece of work with a beginning and an end, as in the labors of Hercules.","cn":"有界的任务：一项有起点和终点的长期工作，如赫拉克勒斯的功业。"},{"senses":"S8 · S9","en":"LABOR AS A LOAD OR WASTED EFFORT: carrying a false belief, and working a point that is already understood.","cn":"作为负担或浪费的劳作：背着错误信念，以及在已经明白的地方反复用力。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Labor is a borrowed Latin noun that English also uses as a verb. Its family is built with -er, -ious, -iously, -atory and the place suffix -atory in laboratory.","cn":"labor 是借入的拉丁名词，英语也用作动词。它的词族用 -er、-ious、-iously、-atory，以及 laboratory 中的地点后缀 -atory 构成。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"The Latin set is labor 'toil', laborare 'to work', laboriosus 'full of toil', and laboratorium 'a place for working'. The deeper origin of labor is uncertain.","cn":"拉丁词族是 labor“辛劳”、laborare“工作”、laboriosus“充满辛劳的”、laboratorium“工作的地方”。labor 的更早来源不确定。"},"items":[{"word":"labor","structure":"Latin labor (toil), via Old French","meaning":"hard work; workers as a class; childbirth","meaningCN":"劳动；劳工；分娩","example":"The work required great labor.","exampleCN":"这项工作需要巨大的劳动。"},{"word":"labors","structure":"labor + -s (plural or third person)","meaning":"tasks, or the act of working","meaningCN":"多项劳作；劳动（第三人称单数）","example":"He labors in the field every day.","exampleCN":"他每天在田里劳作。"},{"word":"labored","structure":"labor + -ed (past participle/adjective)","meaning":"worked hard; showing effort, not natural","meaningCN":"费力的；不自然的（过去分词/形容词）","example":"His breathing was labored.","exampleCN":"他的呼吸很费力。"},{"word":"laboring","structure":"labor + -ing (participle)","meaning":"working hard; in the process of childbirth","meaningCN":"正在劳作；正在分娩","example":"The laboring workers stopped for water.","exampleCN":"干活的工人们停下来喝水。"},{"word":"laborer","structure":"labor + -er (agent)","meaning":"one who does hard physical work","meaningCN":"劳动者；劳工（-er 表施动者）","example":"The laborers built the road by hand.","exampleCN":"劳工们徒手修了这条路。"},{"word":"laborious","structure":"labor + -ious (full of)","meaning":"requiring much time and effort","meaningCN":"费力的；艰苦的（-ious 表“充满”）","example":"Copying the manuscript was laborious.","exampleCN":"抄写这份手稿非常费力。"},{"word":"laboriously","structure":"laborious + -ly (adverb)","meaning":"with great effort, slowly","meaningCN":"费力地；艰难地","example":"He climbed laboriously up the slope.","exampleCN":"他费力地爬上斜坡。"},{"word":"laboratorial","structure":"laboratory + -al (adjective)","meaning":"relating to a laboratory","meaningCN":"实验室的（较罕见）","example":"The samples were tested under laboratorial conditions.","exampleCN":"样本在实验室条件下被检测。"},{"word":"laboratory","structure":"Latin laboratorium (place for working)","meaning":"a place for scientific work","meaningCN":"实验室（字面“工作的地方”）","example":"She spent the night in the laboratory.","exampleCN":"她在实验室待了一夜。"},{"word":"labor-intensive","structure":"labor + intensive (compound adjective)","meaning":"needing a lot of workers rather than machines","meaningCN":"劳动密集型的","example":"Garment production is labor-intensive.","exampleCN":"服装生产是劳动密集型的。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"labor","structure":"Latin noun, origin uncertain","meaning":"toil, exertion; hardship, pain; a work","meaningCN":"辛劳；用力；艰苦；工作"},{"word":"laborare","structure":"verb from labor","meaning":"to work, toil, suffer","meaningCN":"工作；辛劳；受苦"},{"word":"laboriosus","structure":"labor + -iosus","meaning":"full of toil, laborious","meaningCN":"充满辛劳的；费力的"},{"word":"laboratorium","structure":"laborare + -torium (place)","meaning":"a place for working","meaningCN":"工作的地方；实验室"}]}},{"word":"label","ipa_uk":"/ˈleɪbl/","ipa_us":"/ˈleɪbəl/","definition_zh":"标签；标记；称号；唱片公司；贴标签；归类","definition_en":"a piece of paper or material attached to something to give information; a descriptive name; to attach a label or to classify","core_image":"一只箱子上挂着一块写满字的布条，在风里轻轻晃动","scene":"服装店仓库里，店员把一件外套的吊牌翻过来看成分和洗涤说明。她说：Check the label before washing.","sceneCN":"这里 label 是「缝在衣物上的标签、吊牌」（第 1 个义项：附在物品上提供信息的标签）；句意：洗之前先看标签。图中可辨识物件：外套、吊牌、成分表、货架。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"标签；标记；称号；唱片公司"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"贴标签；把……归类为"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"read the label","zh":"看标签"},{"phrase":"a warning label","zh":"警告标签"},{"phrase":"a record label","zh":"唱片公司"},{"phrase":"label somebody as","zh":"把某人归类为"},{"phrase":"designer label","zh":"设计师品牌"},{"phrase":"off-label use","zh":"药品的标签外使用"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（多于一个）","form":"labels"},{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"labels"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"labeled"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"labeled"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"labeling"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"labeled","pos":"adj.","zh":"贴有标签的；标注的"},{"word":"labeling","pos":"n.","zh":"贴标签；标注；归类"},{"word":"relabel","pos":"v.","zh":"重新贴标签；重新标注"},{"word":"mislabel","pos":"v.","zh":"贴错标签；错误标注"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"Information hanging from the thing","titleCN":"挂在物件上的信息：标签","definition":"a piece of paper, cloth or plastic attached to an object to give information about it","definitionCN":"附在物品上、提供有关信息的纸、布或塑料片","example":"The label says the shirt is 100% cotton.","exampleCN":"标签上写着这件衬衫是百分之百棉。","why":"The oldest labels were narrow strips of cloth hanging from a garment or document. The word still pictures something attached to an object and speaking for it.","whyCN":"最早的 label 是挂在衣物或文件上的窄布条。这个词至今仍描绘着附着在物品上、替物品说话的东西。"},{"no":"02","title":"The name on the outside of fashion","titleCN":"穿在外面的名字：品牌标签","definition":"the name or brand of a designer or clothing company, especially as displayed on a garment","definitionCN":"设计师或服装公司的名称或品牌，尤指标在衣物上的","example":"She refuses to pay extra just for a designer label.","exampleCN":"她拒绝仅仅为一个设计师品牌多付钱。","why":"A brand name is literally written on a label. By metonymy the label becomes the brand itself: 'a designer label' means the name and the status attached to it.","whyCN":"品牌名字面上就写在标签上。通过转喻，标签变成了品牌本身：“a designer label”指那个名字以及附着其上的身份。"},{"no":"03","title":"The company behind the record","titleCN":"唱片背后的公司：唱片公司","definition":"a record company, especially as named on the circular label at the centre of a vinyl record","definitionCN":"唱片公司，尤指在黑胶唱片中心圆形标签上所标的公司","example":"The band signed with an independent label.","exampleCN":"这支乐队与一家独立唱片公司签约。","why":"The paper circle at the centre of a record carried the company's name. Musicians began to say 'the label' for the company, and the physical tag became an industry name.","whyCN":"唱片中心的圆形纸片印着公司名称。音乐人开始用“the label”指公司，这个物理标签于是变成了行业名称。"},{"no":"04","title":"Putting something into a category","titleCN":"把某物放进一个类别：归类、贴标签","definition":"to describe or classify someone or something with a word or phrase, often too simply","definitionCN":"用一个词或短语描述或归类某人某物，常常过于简单化","example":"The media labeled him a troublemaker.","exampleCN":"媒体把他贴上“麻烦制造者”的标签。","why":"A label tells you what is inside without opening the box. To label a person is to put a short description on them and treat it as if it were the whole contents.","whyCN":"标签让你不打开盒子就知道里面是什么。给人贴标签，就是把一段简短描述放在他身上，并当作他的全部内容。"},{"no":"05","title":"A name that sticks","titleCN":"甩不掉的名号：称号、刻板印象","definition":"a word or phrase used for a person or group that sticks to them and shapes how others see them","definitionCN":"用于某人或群体、会黏在他们身上并影响他人看法的词或短语","example":"The label 'quiet' followed her through school.","exampleCN":"“安静”这个标签跟着她走过了整个学生时代。","why":"A physical label is hard to remove once attached. The social sense draws on that stickiness: a name applied from outside can become part of how a person is known.","whyCN":"物理标签一旦贴上就很难撕掉。社会义正是借用这种黏性：从外面加上的名号，可能变成一个人被认识的一部分。"},{"no":"06","title":"A sticker on a file","titleCN":"文件上的贴纸：文件夹标签","definition":"a small sticker or printed strip on a file, folder or package showing its contents or destination","definitionCN":"贴在文件、文件夹或包裹上、标明内容或目的地的小贴纸或印刷条","example":"The folder was marked with a red label saying 'Urgent'.","exampleCN":"文件夹上贴着写有“紧急”的红色标签。","why":"Paper files need a mark on the outside to be findable. The label is the visible promise that the contents have already been identified.","whyCN":"纸质文件需要在外面有一个标记才能被找到。标签就是“内容已被识别”的可视承诺。"},{"no":"07","title":"The hazardous-goods label","titleCN":"危险品标签：化学品标识","definition":"an official sign on a chemical, drug or product stating hazards, ingredients or safe use","definitionCN":"贴在化学品、药物或产品上，说明危险、成分或安全用法的正式标识","example":"The bottle carries a label warning of flammability.","exampleCN":"瓶子上有标明易燃的警告标签。","why":"When a label carries legal force, it is no longer just description: it is the object's official voice. Regulators require the label to say what the contents cannot.","whyCN":"当标签具有法律效力时，它不再只是描述：它是物品的官方声音。监管者要求标签说出内容物自己说不出口的话。"},{"no":"08","title":"A marker in an experiment","titleCN":"实验中的标记：示踪标记","definition":"in science, a marker such as a radioactive or fluorescent substance attached to a molecule so that it can be traced","definitionCN":"科学中附在分子上以便追踪的标记，如放射性或荧光物质","example":"The researchers used a fluorescent label to follow the protein.","exampleCN":"研究人员用荧光标记来追踪这种蛋白质。","why":"A label makes an invisible thing visible to an instrument. The scientific sense keeps the core function: an attached mark that identifies what it is attached to.","whyCN":"标签让看不见的东西对仪器可见。科学义保留了核心功能：一个附着的标记，用来识别它所附着的东西。"},{"no":"09","title":"Reading the label as a duty","titleCN":"读标签作为义务：标签信息与责任","definition":"the information printed on a product's label, treated as a warning or legal condition of use","definitionCN":"印在产品标签上的信息，被当作警告或使用的法律条件","example":"The instructions on the label must be followed exactly.","exampleCN":"必须严格遵照标签上的说明。","why":"Once a label is treated as the authoritative statement of the product, reading it becomes part of using the product correctly. The tag now carries responsibility.","whyCN":"一旦标签被视为产品的权威说明，读标签就成了正确使用产品的一部分。这个标签此时承载着责任。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Label comes from Old French label/lambel/labeau 'ribbon, fringe worn on clothes', probably from Frankish *labba or another Germanic source such as Old High German lappa 'flap'. It is NOT from Latin labellum 'small lip', a common but false guess. The original English sense was a narrow dangling strip of cloth.","cn":"label 来自古法语 label/lambel/labeau“缎带、衣服上的流苏”，可能来自法兰克语 *labba 或其他日耳曼语来源，如古高地德语 lappa“垂布”。它并非来自拉丁语 labellum“小唇”，这是一个常见但错误的猜测。英语最初的意思是“窄窄垂下的布条”。"},"items":[{"era":"FRANKISH / GERMANIC *lapp-","en":"The probable source is a Germanic word for a loose piece of cloth, represented by Old High German lappa 'flap' and related forms. English lap belongs to this family.","cn":"可能的来源是一个表示“松散布片”的日耳曼词，代表形式是古高地德语 lappa“垂布”，英语 lap 也属于这个词族。"},{"era":"OLD FRENCH label, 13c.","en":"Old French label, lambel, labeau meant 'ribbon, fringe worn on clothes'. Modern French lambeau 'strip, rag, shred' continues this family.","cn":"古法语 label、lambel、labeau 意为“缎带、衣服上的流苏”。现代法语 lambeau“布条、破布、碎片”延续这个词族。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, c.1300","en":"English first recorded label as a heraldic term for a narrow, dangling band or strip of cloth. The oldest use is technical, in coats of arms.","cn":"英语最早记录 label 是纹章学术语，指窄窄垂下的布条。最早的用法是纹章上的技术性用法。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, early 15c.","en":"By the early 15th century label also meant a dangling strip used as a dress ornament, and a strip attached to a document to hold a seal.","cn":"到 15 世纪初，label 也指作为服饰装饰的垂带，以及附在文件上用来固定印章的纸条。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, 1670s","en":"The general modern sense 'tag, sticker, slip of paper attached to something to show its nature or destination' is attested by the 1670s.","cn":"现代一般义“附在某物上、表明其性质或目的地的标签、贴纸、纸条”记录于 17 世纪 70 年代。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, 1853–1907","en":"The figurative sense 'categorize' is from 1853. The circular paper label at the centre of a gramophone record (1907) gave the music-industry sense 'record company' by 1947.","cn":"“归类”的比喻义来自 1853 年。留声机唱片中心的圆形纸标签（1907 年）在 1947 年前给出音乐产业义“唱片公司”。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group is the label family plus one deceptive near-spelling; the near-meaning group contains words for names and marks, each with a different function.","cn":"形近组是 label 词族外加一个易误导的近形词；近义组是名称与标记类词，功能各不相同。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"labeled","ipa":"/ˈleɪbəld/","tag":"same verb, adjective","definition":"having a label attached, or described in a particular way. The American spelling has one l; British is labelled.","definitionCN":"贴有标签的，或被描述为某种样子的。美式拼写只有一个 l；英式为 labelled。"},{"word":"labeling","ipa":"/ˈleɪbəlɪŋ/","tag":"same verb, noun","definition":"the act of attaching labels or classifying. American labeling has one l; British labelling has two.","definitionCN":"贴标签或归类的行为。美式 labeling 一个 l；英式 labelling 两个 l。"},{"word":"labial","ipa":"/ˈleɪbiəl/","tag":"look-alike, different root","definition":"relating to the lips, or a speech sound made with the lips. It comes from Latin labium 'lip', which is not the source of label.","definitionCN":"与唇有关的，或用唇发出的语音。它来自拉丁语 labium“唇”，而 label 并非来自这个词。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"tag","ipa":"/tæɡ/","tag":"small attached marker","definition":"a small piece of paper, cloth or metal attached to something to identify it. It is the closest everyday synonym for a physical label.","definitionCN":"附在物品上用于识别的小纸片、布片或金属片。它是物理标签最接近的日常同义词。"},{"word":"brand","ipa":"/brænd/","tag":"commercial identity","definition":"the name and identity of a product or company. It overlaps with 'designer label' but stresses reputation rather than the physical tag.","definitionCN":"产品或公司的名称与身份。它与“设计师标签”重叠，但强调声誉而非物理标签。"},{"word":"classify","ipa":"/ˈklæsɪfaɪ/","tag":"put into a class","definition":"to arrange things into groups according to shared features. It is the neutral, systematic version of the verb label.","definitionCN":"按共同特征把事物分组。它是动词 label 的中性、系统化版本。"},{"word":"mark","ipa":"/mɑːk/","tag":"visible sign","definition":"a visible sign made on a surface. It is broader than label: a mark can be a scratch, a symbol or a written note.","definitionCN":"留在表面上的可见记号。它比 label 更宽泛：一个记号可以是划痕、符号或笔记。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: Old French label 'ribbon, fringe', probably from Germanic *lapp- 'loose cloth', plus the ordinary family labeled, labeling, relabel, mislabel.","cn":"只用真实构件：古法语 label“缎带、流苏”，可能来自日耳曼语 *lapp-“松散布片”，以及常用词族 labeled、labeling、relabel、mislabel。"},"normal":[{"en":"The first labels were cloth strips hanging from a garment. That is why the word feels physical: something attached, dangling, and carrying a name.","cn":"最早的 label 是从衣服上垂下来的布条。所以这个词有强烈的物理感：附着的、垂着的、带着名字的东西。"},{"en":"Do not derive label from Latin labellum 'lip'. The likely source is Germanic *lapp- 'loose cloth'. Labial is the 'lip' word; label is the 'cloth strip' word.","cn":"不要把 label 追溯到拉丁语 labellum“唇”。更可能的来源是日耳曼语 *lapp-“松散布片”。labial 才是“唇”的词；label 是“布条”的词。"},{"en":"The physical tag became three institutions: the fashion brand, the record company and the hazard warning. Each is a label doing a different job.","cn":"物理标签变成了三种制度：时尚品牌、唱片公司和危险警告。每一种都是 label 在履行不同职能。"},{"en":"To label a person is to treat a short outside note as the whole contents. The metaphor is exact: you know the box by its sticker.","cn":"给一个人贴标签，就是把外面的一小段说明当作全部内容。这个比喻很精确：你靠贴纸认识盒子。"},{"en":"Fixed patterns: read the label, a warning label, a record label, and label somebody as something.","cn":"固定搭配：read the label（看标签）、a warning label（警告标签）、a record label（唱片公司）、label somebody as something（把某人归类为）。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"A label is a promise of identity made from outside. It saves the work of opening, and it risks being wrong.","cn":"标签是来自外部的身份承诺。它省去了打开查看的麻烦，也承担着出错的风险。"},{"en":"The same word serves and condemns: a label can inform a buyer or fix a child in a category for years.","cn":"同一个词既能服务也能定罪：标签可以告知买家，也可以把一个孩子多年固定在一个类别里。"},{"en":"Modern systems run on labels: brands, diagnoses, genres, warnings. What cannot be labeled struggles to be seen.","cn":"现代系统靠标签运转：品牌、诊断、流派、警告。无法被标签化的东西很难被看见。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"Always read the label before taking the medicine.","cn":"服药前一定要看标签。"},{"en":"The company was criticized for labeling the product 'natural'.","cn":"这家公司因把产品标注为“天然”而受到批评。"},{"en":"She released her first album on a small independent label.","cn":"她在一家小型独立唱片公司发行了第一张专辑。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“累·伯”——累（了就把）伯（伯的）名字写在布条上挂出去 → label 标签","word":"label"},"root":"来自古法语 label/lambel/labeau“缎带、衣服流苏”，可能源于法兰克语或日耳曼语 *lapp-“松散布片”（与古高地德语 lappa“垂布”同族），核心是“附着在物品上、垂下来的信息条”。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of label, all one object: a strip attached to something and speaking for it. A clothing tag, a brand, a record company, a category, a sticky name, a file sticker, a hazard warning, a scientific marker and an instruction all hang from that same original cloth strip.","cn":"label 的九个义项都是同一个物件：附在某物上、替它说话的条片。衣物吊牌、品牌、唱片公司、类别、黏住的名号、文件贴纸、危险警告、科学标记和使用说明，都从最初那条布条上垂下来。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: a written cloth strip hanging from an object, swinging in the wind.","cn":"核心意象：一条写满字的布条挂在物件上，在风中摆动。"},"chain":["SOMETHING ATTACHED","INFORMATION ON IT","IDENTIFIES THE THING","NAME OUTSIDE THE CONTENTS","CATEGORY ASSIGNED","IDENTITY THAT STICKS"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S6 · S9","en":"PHYSICAL INFORMATION: a tag on clothing, a sticker on a file, and printed instructions that must be followed.","cn":"物理信息：衣物上的吊牌、文件上的贴纸，以及必须遵守的印刷说明。"},{"senses":"S2 · S3","en":"INSTITUTIONAL NAMES: a designer brand, and a record company named on the centre of a record.","cn":"机构性名称：设计师品牌，以及印在唱片中心的唱片公司。"},{"senses":"S4 · S5","en":"CATEGORY AND STIGMA: a short outside description applied to a person, and the name that sticks to them afterwards.","cn":"类别与污名：加在一个人身上的简短外部描述，以及随后黏住他的名号。"},{"senses":"S7","en":"OFFICIAL WARNING: a label carrying legal force about hazards, ingredients or safe use.","cn":"官方警告：关于危险、成分或安全用法、具有法律效力的标签。"},{"senses":"S8","en":"SCIENTIFIC MARKER: an attached tracer that makes an invisible molecule findable.","cn":"科学标记：附着在分子上的示踪物，使看不见的分子可被找到。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Label is a borrowed French noun that English also uses as a verb. Its family is built with -ed, -ing, and the prefixes re- and mis-. Spelling doubles the l in British English when a suffix is added.","cn":"label 是借入的法语名词，英语也用作动词。它的词族用 -ed、-ing，以及前缀 re-、mis- 构成。英式英语加后缀时会把 l 双写。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Label has no Latin root. The common guess labellum 'small lip' is false; the probable source is Germanic *lapp- 'loose cloth'. The Latin entries below are included only to mark that false trail clearly.","cn":"label 没有拉丁词根。常见的猜测 labellum“小唇”是错误的；更可能的来源是日耳曼语 *lapp-“松散布片”。下面列出拉丁条目，只是为了明确标记这条错误的联想路径。"},"items":[{"word":"label","structure":"Old French label 'ribbon, fringe'; probably Germanic *lapp-","meaning":"an attached tag; to attach a tag or classify","meaningCN":"标签；贴标签；归类","example":"The label gives the price.","exampleCN":"标签上标着价格。"},{"word":"labels","structure":"label + -s (plural or third person)","meaning":"more than one tag, or the act of labeling","meaningCN":"多个标签；贴标签（第三人称单数）","example":"He labels every box before moving.","exampleCN":"搬家前他给每个箱子贴标签。"},{"word":"labeled","structure":"label + -ed (past participle/adjective, US)","meaning":"having a label; described in a certain way","meaningCN":"贴有标签的；被标注的（美式拼写）","example":"All samples were clearly labeled.","exampleCN":"所有样本都标注清楚。"},{"word":"labelled","structure":"label + -led (British spelling)","meaning":"the British spelling of labeled","meaningCN":"labeled 的英式拼写","example":"The jars were labelled by date.","exampleCN":"罐子按日期贴了标签。"},{"word":"labeling","structure":"label + -ing (noun/participle, US)","meaning":"the act of attaching labels or classifying","meaningCN":"贴标签；归类（美式拼写）","example":"Accurate labeling helps consumers.","exampleCN":"准确标注对消费者有帮助。"},{"word":"labelling","structure":"label + -ling (British spelling)","meaning":"the British spelling of labeling","meaningCN":"labeling 的英式拼写","example":"The labelling was found to be misleading.","exampleCN":"人们发现该标注有误导性。"},{"word":"relabel","structure":"re- (again) + label","meaning":"to label again, often with a new name","meaningCN":"重新贴标签；重新命名（re- 表再、重新）","example":"The company relabeled the product.","exampleCN":"公司给产品重新贴了标签。"},{"word":"mislabel","structure":"mis- (wrongly) + label","meaning":"to label incorrectly","meaningCN":"贴错标签；错误标注（mis- 表错误）","example":"Several packages were mislabeled.","exampleCN":"有几个包裹贴错了标签。"},{"word":"unlabeled","structure":"un- (not) + labeled","meaning":"having no label","meaningCN":"没有标签的；未标注的","example":"An unlabeled bottle stood on the shelf.","exampleCN":"架子上放着一个没有标签的瓶子。"},{"word":"off-label","structure":"off + label (compound adjective)","meaning":"of a drug, used for a purpose not listed on its official label","meaningCN":"药品的标签外使用（用于未列入官方标签的用途）","example":"Doctors sometimes prescribe drugs off-label.","exampleCN":"医生有时会标签外开药。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"labellum","structure":"Latin, diminutive of labrum","meaning":"small lip — often wrongly guessed as the source of label; it is not","meaningCN":"小唇——常被错误猜作 label 的来源；实际并非如此"},{"word":"labrum","structure":"Latin noun","meaning":"lip; edge of a vessel","meaningCN":"唇；容器边缘"},{"word":"lappa","structure":"Old High German, Germanic family","meaning":"flap, loose piece of cloth (probable source family of label)","meaningCN":"垂布、松散布片（label 的可能来源词族）"}]}},{"word":"layer","ipa_uk":"/ˈleɪə/","ipa_us":"/ˈleɪər/","definition_zh":"层；层次；地层；涂层；产蛋鸡","definition_en":"a thickness or sheet of material covering a surface; one of several levels in a system; a hen that lays eggs","core_image":"一张一张薄片叠起来，像千层饼的横截面，每一层都清晰可数","scene":"地质课上，老师用铲子切开岩壁，露出水平排列的一层层岩石。他指着说：Each layer was laid down in a different age.","sceneCN":"这里 layer 是「岩层、地层」（第 3 个义项：地质沉积层）；句意：每一层岩石都是在不同年代沉积下来的。图中可辨识物件：岩壁、铲子、水平岩层、地质锤。","pos":[{"tag":"n.","zh":"层；层次；地层；涂层"},{"tag":"vt.","zh":"把……分层叠放；分层铺设"}],"collocations":[{"phrase":"a thin layer of","zh":"薄薄的一层"},{"phrase":"the ozone layer","zh":"臭氧层"},{"phrase":"layers of meaning","zh":"层层含义"},{"phrase":"a layer of paint","zh":"一层漆"},{"phrase":"in layers","zh":"分层地；一层层地"},{"phrase":"the upper layer","zh":"上层"}],"forms":[{"label":"复数（多于一个）","form":"layers"},{"label":"三单（he/she/it）","form":"layers"},{"label":"过去式（已经发生）","form":"layered"},{"label":"过去分词（完成／被动）","form":"layered"},{"label":"现在分词（进行体）","form":"layering"}],"derivatives":[{"word":"layered","pos":"adj.","zh":"分层的；有层次的"},{"word":"layering","pos":"n.","zh":"分层；层叠；压条繁殖"},{"word":"multilayer","pos":"adj./n.","zh":"多层的；多层结构"},{"word":"interlayer","pos":"n.","zh":"夹层；中间层"}],"senses":[{"no":"01","title":"A sheet laid over a surface","titleCN":"铺在表面上的一层：涂层、薄层","definition":"a thickness or sheet of material that covers a surface","definitionCN":"覆盖在表面上的一层材料或一片物质","example":"A thin layer of dust covered the table.","exampleCN":"桌上覆盖着一层薄薄的灰。","why":"Layer is lay + -er: 'that which is laid'. A layer is material placed down on a surface, seen as one sheet rather than as a mass.","whyCN":"layer 是 lay 加 -er，即“被铺下的东西”。一层就是把材料铺在表面上，被看作一片，而不是一团。"},{"no":"02","title":"One level in a stack of levels","titleCN":"层层结构中的一级：层次","definition":"one of several levels in a system, idea or organization, each built on or above another","definitionCN":"系统、思想或组织中的若干层级之一，每一层建立在另一层之上","example":"The novel works on several layers of meaning.","exampleCN":"这部小说在好几层意义上成立。","why":"Anything that can be laid down one piece over another can be imagined as a stack. Ideas and organizations borrow the physical stack and call each level a layer.","whyCN":"任何能一层压一层铺放的东西，都可以被想象成一摞。思想与组织借用这个物理堆叠，把每一级称为一层。"},{"no":"03","title":"A stratum in the earth","titleCN":"地下的那一层：地层","definition":"in geology, a band of rock or soil of one kind, deposited at a particular period","definitionCN":"地质学中，某一时期沉积形成的同一种岩石或土壤带","example":"The fossils were found in a layer of limestone.","exampleCN":"化石是在一层石灰岩中发现的。","why":"Sediment settles in sheets, one age on top of another. Geology sees the earth's history as a stack of layers, so the word becomes a technical term for a stratum.","whyCN":"沉积物一片一片落下，一个年代压在另一个年代上。地质学把地球历史看成一摞层，于是这个词成为“地层”的术语。"},{"no":"04","title":"A band around the planet","titleCN":"包围地球的一带：大气层","definition":"in geography, a distinct band of the atmosphere or ocean at a particular height or depth","definitionCN":"地理学中，大气或海洋在特定高度或深度上的一条明显带","example":"The ozone layer protects us from harmful radiation.","exampleCN":"臭氧层保护我们免受有害辐射。","why":"The atmosphere is arranged in shells, one above another. Each shell is a layer because it can be drawn as a band laid over the one below.","whyCN":"大气按壳层排列，一层在另一层之上。每个壳层都是一层，因为它可以被画成覆盖在下面那层上的一条带。"},{"no":"05","title":"A level in software","titleCN":"软件中的一层：分层架构","definition":"in computing, one level of a system or protocol that communicates with the levels above and below it","definitionCN":"计算机中，与上下层通信的系统或协议的一级","example":"The application layer sits above the network layer.","exampleCN":"应用层位于网络层之上。","why":"Software designers picture a system as a stack of levels, each hiding the details of the one below. The physical stack of sheets becomes an architecture.","whyCN":"软件设计者把系统想象成一摞层级，每一层隐藏下面一层的细节。物理的薄片堆叠变成了架构。"},{"no":"06","title":"One coat of paint","titleCN":"刷一遍漆：涂层","definition":"one application or coat of paint, varnish or another covering material","definitionCN":"油漆、清漆或其他覆盖材料的一次涂布","example":"The wall needs two more layers of paint.","exampleCN":"这面墙还需要再刷两层漆。","why":"Painting is the most literal act of laying down a sheet of material. Each pass adds one more layer, and the old surface disappears under it.","whyCN":"刷漆是最字面的“铺下一层材料”。每刷一遍就多一层，旧表面被盖在下面。"},{"no":"07","title":"Clothing stacked for warmth","titleCN":"为保暖叠穿：一层层衣物","definition":"one garment or set of garments worn over another, especially for warmth","definitionCN":"穿在另一件外面的一件或多件衣物，尤为了保暖","example":"Wear several thin layers instead of one thick coat.","exampleCN":"穿几层薄衣服，而不是一件厚外套。","why":"Dressing in layers is stacking sheets of fabric around the body. Each garment is a layer, and warmth comes from the trapped air between them.","whyCN":"分层穿衣就是把一片片布料叠在身体周围。每件衣服是一层，温暖来自层与层之间被困住的空气。"},{"no":"08","title":"The hen that lays","titleCN":"下蛋的鸡：产蛋鸡","definition":"a hen kept for laying eggs, or a hen that lays eggs regularly","definitionCN":"为产蛋而饲养的母鸡，或定期下蛋的母鸡","example":"The farm keeps two hundred layers.","exampleCN":"这个农场养了两百只产蛋鸡。","why":"This is the agent sense of -er: a layer is 'one who lays'. It is not a sheet at all, but the same suffix that names the one performing the action.","whyCN":"这是 -er 的施动者义：layer 就是“下蛋的那一个”。它完全不是薄片，而是同一个后缀用来命名执行动作的主体。"},{"no":"09","title":"Layering a plant","titleCN":"压条繁殖：layer 的园艺动词","definition":"in gardening, to make a stem root while still attached to the parent plant, or the resulting rooted branch","definitionCN":"园艺中使枝条在仍连着母株时生根，或指这样生根的枝条","example":"They layered the rose bush to produce a new plant.","exampleCN":"他们对这株玫瑰进行压条，以培育新植株。","why":"The gardener bends a stem down and 'lays' it under soil. The new plant is produced by a laying-down, so the method and the verb share the original physical action.","whyCN":"园丁把枝条弯下并“铺”在土里。新植株由一次“铺下”产生，所以这种方法与动词共享最初的物理动作。"}],"etymology":{"intro":{"en":"Layer is an English agent noun: lay + -er, 'one who or that which lays'. Lay goes back to Old English lecgan 'to place', from the causative of the verb that became lie. The 'sheet of material' sense developed later, probably under some influence from French cookery terms.","cn":"layer 是英语的施动名词：lay 加 -er，即“放置的人或物”。lay 可追溯到古英语 lecgan“放置”，它是后来变成 lie 的动词的使役形式。“一层材料”的义项发展较晚，可能受到法语烹饪用语的一些影响。"},"items":[{"era":"PIE *legh-","en":"The root *legh- meant 'to lie down, lay'. It underlies English lie, lay and law (something 'laid down'), and German liegen and legen.","cn":"词根 *legh- 意为“躺下、放下”。它是英语 lie、lay 和 law（“被放下的东西”）以及德语 liegen、legen 的深层来源。"},{"era":"OLD ENGLISH lecgan","en":"Lecgan meant 'to place on the ground or another surface; place in order; put down'. It was the causative of licgan 'to lie': to lay is to cause to lie.","cn":"lecgan 意为“放在地上或其他表面上；按顺序摆放；放下”。它是 licgan“躺”的使役形式：lay 就是“使……躺下”。"},{"era":"ENGLISH layer, late 14c.","en":"Layer is first recorded in the late 14th century as 'one who or that lays', especially a mason who lays stones. This is the agent-noun sense of -er.","cn":"layer 最早记录于 14 世纪晚期，意为“放置的人或物”，尤指砌石的泥瓦匠。这是 -er 的施动名词义。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, 1610s","en":"The passive sense 'a thickness of material laid over a surface' is recorded by the 1610s. Because the earliest English uses were in cookery, the sense may have been influenced by French liue 'binding', a word used of a thickened sauce.","cn":"被动义“铺在表面上的一层材料”记录于 17 世纪 10 年代。由于英语最早的用法出现在烹饪中，这个义项可能受到法语 liue“黏合”的影响，后者用于浓稠酱汁。"},{"era":"ENGLISH, 1707–1875","en":"The hen sense 'a hen that lays eggs' is recorded by 1707. Layer cake is attested from 1875, naming a cake made of stacked layers.","cn":"“下蛋的母鸡”义项记录于 1707 年。layer cake（千层蛋糕）记录于 1875 年，指由叠层制成的蛋糕。"},{"era":"ENGLISH VERB, 1779–1852","en":"The verb layer is from 1779 in horticulture, as a method of plant propagation. The general sense 'form into layers' is attested by 1852.","cn":"动词 layer 来自 1779 年的园艺用法，指一种植物繁殖方法。“形成层”的一般义项记录于 1852 年。"}]},"similar":{"note":{"en":"The look-alike group is the lay/layer family; the near-meaning group contains words for sheets and levels, each from a different material or scale.","cn":"形近组是 lay/layer 词族；近义组是薄片与层级类词，各自的材料或尺度不同。"},"groups":[{"heading":"LOOK-ALIKE","entries":[{"word":"lay","ipa":"/leɪ/","tag":"base verb","definition":"to put something down on a surface; to place in order. It is the verb behind layer, and its past tense is laid, not layed.","definitionCN":"把某物放在表面上；按顺序摆放。它是 layer 背后的动词，过去式是 laid，不是 layed。"},{"word":"laying","ipa":"/ˈleɪɪŋ/","tag":"same verb, participle","definition":"the act of putting something down, or of a hen producing an egg. It is the -ing form of lay.","definitionCN":"放下某物的动作，或母鸡下蛋。它是 lay 的 -ing 形式。"},{"word":"layered","ipa":"/ˈleɪəd/","tag":"same word, adjective","definition":"arranged in layers, or having several levels. The past participle became an adjective describing a stacked structure.","definitionCN":"分层排列的，或具有多个层次的。过去分词变成形容词，描述堆叠结构。"}]},{"heading":"NEAR MEANING","entries":[{"word":"stratum","ipa":"/ˈstrɑːtəm/","tag":"geological layer","definition":"a layer of rock or soil, especially one of many deposited in sequence. It is the technical Latin word for a geological layer.","definitionCN":"岩石或土壤的一层，尤指按顺序沉积的许多层之一。它是地质层的拉丁技术词。"},{"word":"coating","ipa":"/ˈkəʊtɪŋ/","tag":"covering film","definition":"a thin layer of a substance covering a surface. It stresses the material spread over something, often for protection.","definitionCN":"覆盖在表面上的一薄层物质。它强调铺在表面的材料，常带保护目的。"},{"word":"film","ipa":"/fɪlm/","tag":"very thin sheet","definition":"a very thin layer or membrane. It is thinner than a typical layer and often continuous and transparent.","definitionCN":"极薄的一层或膜。它比一般的 layer 更薄，常是连续而透明的。"},{"word":"tier","ipa":"/tɪə/","tag":"one of ranked levels","definition":"one of several levels in a hierarchy, especially when they are ranked. It is the social or organizational counterpart of a physical layer.","definitionCN":"等级体系中的一层，尤指被排序的层级。它是物理 layer 在社会或组织中的对应词。"}]}]},"mnemonics":{"normalIntro":{"en":"Real pieces only: lay 'place down' + -er, plus the ordinary family layered, layering, multilayer, interlayer. The 'sheet' sense came later than the 'one who lays' sense.","cn":"只用真实构件：lay“放下”加 -er，以及常用词族 layered、layering、multilayer、interlayer。“薄层”义晚于“放置者”义出现。"},"normal":[{"en":"Layer = lay + -er. The first meaning was 'one who lays', like a mason laying stones; only later did it mean 'that which is laid' as a sheet.","cn":"layer = lay + -er。最早的意思是“放置者”，像砌石的泥瓦匠；后来才表示“被铺下的东西”，即一层。"},{"en":"A hen that lays eggs is also a layer, because -er can name the doer. The same suffix gives both the mason and the sheet.","cn":"下蛋的母鸡也是 layer，因为 -er 可以命名动作的执行者。同一个后缀既给出泥瓦匠，也给出薄层。"},{"en":"A geological layer is history stacked: each sheet of sediment is an older page under a newer one.","cn":"地层就是被叠起来的历史：每一片沉积物都是压在更新一页下面的旧页。"},{"en":"In computing, a layer hides the layer below it. The stack is physical in origin and architectural in use.","cn":"在计算机中，一层隐藏下面一层。这个堆叠起源于物理，却被用于架构。"},{"en":"Fixed patterns: a thin layer of, the ozone layer, layers of meaning, and in layers.","cn":"固定搭配：a thin layer of（薄薄一层）、the ozone layer（臭氧层）、layers of meaning（层层含义）、in layers（分层地）。"}],"abstract":[{"en":"A layer is both a cover and a record: it hides what is below while preserving it.","cn":"一层既是覆盖，也是记录：它遮住下面的东西，同时把它保存下来。"},{"en":"Complexity is often just depth: when a thing has too many layers, we stop seeing the surface and start seeing a system.","cn":"复杂往往只是深度：当一个东西层数太多，我们就不再看到表面，而开始看到一个系统。"},{"en":"Every layer was laid by someone or something. The word keeps the action inside the noun, which is why a stratum can be read as a date.","cn":"每一层都是由某个力量铺下的。这个词把动作保留在名词里，所以一层地层可以被读成一个年代。"}]},"examples":[{"en":"A thick layer of snow covered the car.","cn":"厚厚的一层雪盖住了汽车。"},{"en":"The problem has several layers that must be solved separately.","cn":"这个问题有几层，必须分别解决。"},{"en":"The farmer keeps a hundred layers for eggs.","cn":"农场主养了一百只产蛋鸡。"}],"dict_mnemonic":{"note":"谐音记忆 · 非词源","text":"“累·尔”——累（了就把）尔（等薄片）一层层叠起来 → layer 层","word":"layer"},"root":"由英语动词 lay“放下、铺下”加施动后缀 -er 构成；lay 源于古英语 lecgan“放置”，再上溯到原始印欧语 *legh-“躺下、放下”，核心是“被铺下去的一片”，也保留“放置者”的施动义。","sensesIntro":{"en":"Nine senses of layer, all one action: something is laid down on something else. Dust, meaning, rock, atmosphere, software, paint, clothing, a laying hen and a propagated stem each come from that same verb lay.","cn":"layer 的九个义项都是同一个动作：某物被铺在另一物上。灰尘、意义、岩石、大气、软件、油漆、衣物、下蛋的母鸡和压条的枝条，都来自同一个动词 lay。"},"semanticMap":{"core":{"en":"CORE IMAGE: thin sheets stacked one on another, each visible as a separate band.","cn":"核心意象：一张张薄片叠在一起，每一片都能被看成分明的一带。"},"chain":["LAY DOWN","ONE SHEET","COVER THE SURFACE","STACK MORE SHEETS","ONE LEVEL AMONG MANY","DEPTH AND STRUCTURE"],"branches":[{"senses":"S1 · S6 · S7","en":"MATERIAL LAID ON A SURFACE: dust, paint and clothing are added as sheets over what is already there.","cn":"铺在表面上的材料：灰尘、油漆和衣物都是一片片加在已有之物上面。"},{"senses":"S2 · S5","en":"LEVELS IN A SYSTEM: meanings and software are built as stacks, each level resting on another.","cn":"系统中的层级：意义与软件都以堆叠方式建立，每一层依托另一层。"},{"senses":"S3 · S4","en":"NATURAL BANDS: rock strata record ages, and atmospheric shells wrap the planet in bands.","cn":"自然界的层带：岩层记录年代，大气壳层以带状包裹地球。"},{"senses":"S8","en":"THE DOER: a laying hen is a layer because -er can name the one performing the action.","cn":"执行者：下蛋的母鸡是 layer，因为 -er 可以命名执行动作的主体。"},{"senses":"S9","en":"THE HORTICULTURAL ACT: a stem is laid under soil so that it roots, turning the verb back into a physical laying-down.","cn":"园艺动作：枝条被铺在土下以便生根，使动词回到物理上的“铺下”。"}]},"affixes":{"intro":{"en":"Layer is an English compound of lay + -er. Its family is built with -ed, -ing, and the prefixes multi- and inter-.","cn":"layer 是 lay + -er 的英语复合词。它的词族用 -ed、-ing，以及前缀 multi-、inter- 构成。"},"latinIntro":{"en":"Layer has no Latin root; it is native English. The Latin word for a geological layer is stratum, from sternere 'to spread out', which is a useful contrast rather than a source.","cn":"layer 没有拉丁词根，是本族英语词。地质层的拉丁词是 stratum，来自 sternere“铺开”，这是有用的对照，而不是来源。"},"items":[{"word":"layer","structure":"lay (place down) + -er (agent or thing)","meaning":"a sheet laid over a surface; one who lays","meaningCN":"层；放置者（-er 表施动者或事物）","example":"A layer of ice formed on the pond.","exampleCN":"池塘上结了一层冰。"},{"word":"layers","structure":"layer + -s (plural or third person)","meaning":"several sheets or levels; the act of layering","meaningCN":"多层；分层（复数或第三人称单数）","example":"The cake has three layers.","exampleCN":"这个蛋糕有三层。"},{"word":"layered","structure":"layer + -ed (past participle/adjective)","meaning":"arranged in layers; having depth","meaningCN":"分层的；有层次的","example":"The story has a layered structure.","exampleCN":"这个故事有多层结构。"},{"word":"layering","structure":"layer + -ing (noun/participle)","meaning":"the act of arranging in layers; plant propagation","meaningCN":"分层；层叠；压条繁殖","example":"Layering is a simple way to propagate plants.","exampleCN":"压条是一种简单的植物繁殖方法。"},{"word":"multilayer","structure":"multi- (many) + layer","meaning":"having many layers","meaningCN":"多层的（multi- 表多）","example":"The film uses multilayer packaging.","exampleCN":"这种薄膜使用多层包装。"},{"word":"interlayer","structure":"inter- (between) + layer","meaning":"a layer between two others","meaningCN":"夹层；中间层（inter- 表之间）","example":"A thin interlayer separates the two sheets.","exampleCN":"一层薄薄的夹层把两片材料隔开。"},{"word":"layer cake","structure":"layer + cake (compound noun)","meaning":"a cake made of stacked layers","meaningCN":"千层蛋糕（由叠层制成）","example":"She baked a chocolate layer cake.","exampleCN":"她烤了一个巧克力千层蛋糕。"},{"word":"ozone layer","structure":"ozone + layer (compound noun)","meaning":"the atmospheric band rich in ozone","meaningCN":"臭氧层","example":"The ozone layer absorbs ultraviolet light.","exampleCN":"臭氧层吸收紫外线。"},{"word":"lay","structure":"Old English lecgan (causative of lie)","meaning":"to place something down","meaningCN":"放置；铺下（layer 的基础动词）","example":"She laid the cloth on the table.","exampleCN":"她把布铺在桌上。"}],"latinEntries":[{"word":"stratum","structure":"Latin, from sternere 'spread out'","meaning":"a layer, bed, pavement (not the source of layer)","meaningCN":"层；地层（并非 layer 的来源，仅作对照）"},{"word":"sternere","structure":"Latin verb","meaning":"to spread out, strew","meaningCN":"铺开；撒"},{"word":"lectus","structure":"Latin, from *legh- 'lie'","meaning":"bed, couch (same PIE root as lay)","meaningCN":"床；卧榻（与 lay 同出一个原始印欧语词根）"}]}}]);
